    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL or IELTS when not exempt. TOEFL minimum 90 for tests before 21 January 2026; 4.5 on new scale thereafter. IELTS recommended overall 7. TOEFL Special Home Edition and IELTS Indicator listed as accepted. ETS code 3094; IELTS sent electronically to Brown Graduate School, not student-uploaded unofficial report. [s4] [Conflict] Completed UChicago degree qualifies under U.S./English-medium degree exemption. Mathematics additionally exempts applicants already having one or more years of study in an English-speaking country, so a current UChicago student may qualify before conferral. Central wording emphasizes earned degree; check automatic waived status 3-5 business days after submission and email admissions after submission if needed. Native-language-non-English TAs still face arrival certification; lack of certification can affect TA support beyond first year. [s1] [s4] [s3] [Standing rule] All doctoral admits covered by central support guarantee without nationality exception; inference: international Math admits included. External awards/loans may have citizenship restrictions. [s9]",
