    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Fall entry only; February 1 is the complete-file deadline for admission and financial-support consideration. Late supporting materials reduce prospects for a TA. No separate grace period or deadline time zone is published. Official transcripts are required before or during the first enrolled semester to register for the second. [s1] [s3]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] September 2026 handbook: entering stipend USD 22,510 for nine months; after Part B qualifying survey, USD 23,752. Assistant calculus/precalculus director adds USD 691 per semester. These are 2026 handbook rates, not a confirmed 2027-28 offer. Tuition benefits vary by appointment/FTE, residency and funding source. Qualifying SHIP coverage requires appointment and enrollment conditions. [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s must be completed by enrollment. Mathematics background and overall post-secondary GPA at least 3.0 are expected; a mathematics major is not mandatory. A completed UChicago mathematics bachelor’s fits the degree route; GPA and individual preparation remain to be assessed. International applications are accepted. [s1] [s3]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Create the Slate account using its temporary PIN, submit the application and fee, then complete supporting materials. The portal checklist reports missing items; email notifications report missing materials and completion. Three referee contacts must be supplied even though mathematics requires only two letters. [s1]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Published minima: TOEFL 80, IELTS 6.5, PTE 58 or Duolingo 120. Official agency reporting is required, code 4075. No conditional admission for insufficient English; the page excludes several alternate/home formats, including TOEFL Essentials/ITP/MyBest and IELTS General/Indicator. Revised 2026 TOEFL scale not stated on this page. [s1] [Standing rule] A recently earned U.S. degree qualifies for an English-test exception. The public mathematics wording does not expressly say an unfinished UChicago degree qualifies at application; confirm timing and documentation. [s1] [Standing rule] International applicants are considered for financial support through the same department application. Exact nonresident tuition coverage and fees must be checked in the offer; a general tuition benefit is not evidence that every charge is covered. [s1] [s2]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 70 for international degree-seeking applicants; USD 60 domestic. [s1] [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Both General and Mathematics Subject GRE are optional. Use institution code 4075 if reporting; processing can take 3-4 weeks. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Both General and Mathematics Subject GRE are optional. Use institution code 4075 if reporting; processing can take 3-4 weeks. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Mathematics requires TWO letters; Graduate School requires THREE referee contacts. The first two received satisfy the mathematics letter requirement. No prescribed letter format. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] SOP required. Faithful prompt paraphrase: describe academic/professional interests, prospective contributions, and how lived experiences have developed relevant skills. No published word/page cap, font or spacing; upload rather than an external-link instruction. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] The 2022 handbook’s lower stipends are superseded for this report by September 2026 rates. Central free-day materials mention a personal-history statement absent from the math checklist. Gillespie’s personal page reports tenure in 2025 while the department index still says assistant professor. [s2] [s4] [s5] [s8]",
