    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL iBT or IELTS Academic unless exempt; no DET/PTE/TOEFL Essentials. IELTS overall 7; speaking 8 meets Tier A, otherwise qualifying Tier B applicants need assessment. TOEFL before 21 January 2026: reading 20, listening 15, writing 20, speaking 22 (Tier B) or 27 (Tier A). New scale: R4/L3.5/W4/S4 for Tier B, S5.5 for Tier A. Scores valid two years at deadline; ETS code 2098. MyBest accepted centrally subject to field discretion. Home testing only when safe in-person testing unavailable. [s2] [Standing rule] U.S. bachelor’s completed by enrollment, with majority of physical attendance in the U.S., qualifies; select exemption in application, no prior email permission. UChicago degree is therefore eligible if these conditions hold. Exemption from admission testing does not remove the English Language Assessment/possible ITAP teaching requirement. Alternative exemption covers two consecutive full-time English-medium study/work years in an approved country in the last ten years with CV/transcript evidence. [s2] [Standing rule] Department states all admitted Math PhDs receive support, without a citizenship exception; inference: international admits included. Individual external fellowships may restrict citizenship. [s9]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 105 nonrefundable; credit/debit online at submission. Paying or obtaining waiver is final step and locks application. [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Not considered. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] REQUIRED; minimum 600. Applications with missing or below-600 Mathematics Subject GRE are not reviewed. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three, with extra letters allowed. Prefer current/prior academic faculty able to assess academic work; applicants away from school should ask field about professional referees. [s1] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required academic statement. Faithful prompt paraphrase: describe mathematical goals, preparation and experiences, research roles/results, relevant scholarly work, Cornell field/faculty fit and career plans. Central guidance suggests 1-2 pages in a standard font, name and program at top of each page; this is guidance, not a verified math-specific hard cap. Upload in application; exact file restrictions and permission to link papers unverified. [s1] [s7]",
