    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] December 15, 2026 for Fall 2027: all application materials must be received, including references. VTSI applicants instead need the entire PhD application, supplement and all supporting materials/letters received December 1, 2026. Exact cutoff time/timezone and any grace period are not published on the mathematics page. [s1] [s11]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Current 2026-27 contractual minimum USD 52,000 annually for a full fiscal-year appointment (12-month annual basis), with proration for shorter/partial appointments; not a confirmed Fall 2027 offer. Math guarantees full tuition and benefits with support. Owen supplement is USD 6,000/year for three years for selected exceptional applicants. Central 2026-27 cost page says resident full-time PhD health insurance is covered; tuition/insurance value is not extra cash. The agreement’s initial term ends June 30, 2027, with conditional automatic renewal, so 2027-28 rate must be rechecked. [s1] [s8] [s9] [s18]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle for direct PhD application with a UChicago bachelor’s completed before enrollment; no external terminal MA or spring admission. International applicants are accepted. The department describes preparation in calculus, linear algebra, complex analysis, real analysis, abstract algebra and point-set topology as guidance rather than rigid prerequisites. F-1 status does not itself establish academic eligibility; grades and degree completion remain to be assessed. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Prepare the KSAS online application, transcripts, current/planned courses absent from transcripts, SOP and three referees. Request the English waiver in the application, and any fee waiver before payment. Check prior undergraduate attendance against the VTSI institution list if seeking that fellowship. No pre-application adviser agreement is listed. [s3] [s4] [s11] [s12]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL or IELTS unless exempt; department minimum TOEFL 100 on the old scale or 5 on the new scale, IELTS 7. Central page retains preferred TOEFL 100/IELTS 7 and requires scores less than two years old. Codes: TOEFL 5332; IELTS 4610. Send official results directly; IELTS applicants also upload a copy, while TOEFL student copies/photocopies are not accepted in lieu of official reporting. [s1] [s4] [Standing rule] UChicago bachelor’s qualifies assuming at least two years of full-time US study; request waiver inside the application. Department explicitly includes applicants completing the bachelor’s. Central international instructions require a current US degree to be conferred within two semesters of application; confirm interpretation for UChicago quarters and your actual conferral date if outside normal spring/summer 2027 graduation. [s2] [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] Mathematics says all admitted PhD students receive support and explicitly admits international students. Contract includes international employees and immigration-related assistance. Need-based relocation maximum is USD 2,500 for international entrants versus USD 2,000 domestic; award requires admission, financial need and eventual matriculation. Funding-specific external citizenship restrictions still need checking. [s1] [s2] [s8] [s9] [s10]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 75 per KSAS application, nonrefundable; Visa, Mastercard or Discover. [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not required for Mathematics on the central exam table. Public sources do not clearly distinguish whether unsolicited General GRE scores are considered or ignored; do not label it prohibited or recommended. [s4]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional and regarded as useful by Mathematics; more weight is placed on other application elements if absent. Self-report suffices when applying, with official verification only if accepted. No published Math GRE minimum located. Central GRE validity is five years. [s1] [s2] [s4]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required. Mathematics says the online system accepts three; an additional recommender can email the department through the FAQ contact link. Standard online recommendation form must be completed. Do not assume an extra letter or a dossier-service PDF substitutes for the form. [s1] [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required uploaded SOP. Prompt paraphrase: explain academic/career aims, research interests and preparation. Personal background can be included in the same essay instead of a separate personal statement. No mathematics word/page cap, font, spacing, file-size or file-type specification was located publicly; central instructions defer length to department. Submit English text or an accompanying translation; portal limits need checking. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current department and central pages require electronic applications; FAQ retains obsolete paper-mail guidance. Department English waiver phrasing focuses on undergraduate degree, central page more broadly permits eligible post-secondary degrees; UChicago bachelor route fits both if timing/study-duration conditions met. Central admissions contact listing names Sabrina Raymond but current department names Kate Torrence; use current coordinator. JHU roster is stale for Zhuang (Stanford since 2026) and Haihan Wu (Virginia since 2026). [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s7] [s16] [f20] [f21]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Verify exact deadline time/timezone, offer commitment date, 2027-28 stipend/fee coverage, live essay/upload limits, CV/sample permission, immediate reference trigger and pre-submit timing, receipt indicators, letter replacement/reuse, fee-waiver timing and adviser capacity. Confirm UChicago conferral timing for English waiver and any prior eligible VTSI attendance before doing its supplement. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s6] [s9] [s11] [s12]",
