    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] Fall only. The live department page, updated October 28, 2026, gives February 1 for full consideration and review thereafter until positions fill. Central international deadline is also February 1. No time zone is published. A search-index version retained January 8 for international students: seek confirmation and use January 8 as a conservative planning target, not a verified current deadline. [s1] [s4]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] GTA includes a nine-month salary and fall/spring tuition waiver; amount is supplied in the individual offer and is not published on the funding page. Summer salary requires summer GTA appointment. Application instructions also describe resident fees and affordable health insurance, not a promise of all fees or full insurance payment. [s2] [s3]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A mathematics background equivalent to the K-State bachelor’s curriculum is expected. A UChicago mathematics bachelor’s is an appropriate degree route, subject to graduate committee, head and Graduate School approval; this is an eligibility inference, not an admission prediction. International applicants are explicitly eligible. [s1] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Create the graduate application; upload transcripts, résumé and academic-objectives statement; enter three referees and request a TA if desired. Financial support documentation is for immigration processing after admission, not an academic selection criterion. [s2] [s4]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Admission accepts TOEFL, IELTS or PTE; not Duolingo or TOEFL ITP. Published minima are TOEFL 79 (4.5 on the revised scale), IELTS 6.5 or PTE 58. Teaching has a separate speaking requirement: SPEAK 50, TOEFL speaking 22/revised 4.5, or IELTS speaking 7. [s2] [Standing rule] A received U.S. degree exempts the admission English test. The page does not expressly extend this to an unfinished UChicago degree. The separate TA speaking requirement applies to nonnative English speakers regardless of citizenship; do not assume the admission waiver satisfies teaching certification. [s2] [Standing rule] International students may hold GTAs; teaching speaking certification is separate. GTAs teach recitations and grade examinations. The offer controls exact financial terms; continuation duration is not established here. [s2] [s3]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] International degree application: USD 75; domestic fee USD 65. Pay on submission. [s2] [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] GRE scores are optional; the current instructions do not differentiate General and Mathematics Subject tests. Copies may be used in review; official reporting institution code 6334, mathematics 0703. [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] GRE scores are optional; the current instructions do not differentiate General and Mathematics Subject tests. Copies may be used in review; official reporting institution code 6334, mathematics 0703. [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three letters; enter names and email addresses. Department says no separate letter form. [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Academic-objectives statement required, maximum two pages. Prompt paraphrase: explain enthusiasm for mathematics, research interests and academic goals, relevant teaching or research experience, and optionally faculty fit. Upload in application; font, spacing and file type not specified publicly. [s2]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Search-index international deadline January 8 differs from the live February 1 rule. Central funding-affidavit timing is after admission, while departmental instructions discuss it within application preparation. [s1] [s2] [s4]",
