    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s degree with GPA normally at least 3.0; preparation should include abstract algebra, linear algebra, real analysis and complex variables. A UChicago math bachelor’s student can apply for direct doctoral study; degree completion and individual preparation must be verified. [s1] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Prepare two referees, CV, personal statement and transcripts; use the CAS online application. Send referee requests early. Check the linked 2027 CAS language policy and claim the US-study exemption with supporting records. No extra application is required for departmental funding. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "international": "[Unresolved] English proficiency is required unless exempt. Tests must remain valid through I-20 processing; submit an unofficial score report or test documentation, not merely typed scores, with official results after admission. PTE is accepted beginning 2027. CAS links a 2027 PDF for exact minimums; its content did not render publicly in this review, so thresholds remain unresolved. [s3] [s4] [s15] [Standing rule] The university exemption covers a degree earned by enrollment at a US institution with at least two consecutive years of in-person study; a separate route covers two consecutive years of English-country study/work in the preceding five years. Your UChicago degree therefore appears eligible if those duration/mode conditions hold, including pending conferral before enrollment. This is an inference from the published conditions, subject to CAS review. [s4] [Unresolved] A funded mathematics offer’s international eligibility and renewal-year guarantee are not explicit in the checked public FAQ; confirm the actual assistantship contract, summer support and spoken-English teaching obligations. [s1] [s2]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] US $50 nonrefundable application fee. [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Optional for 2027 and 2028 CAS applicants except History. Mathematics FAQ recommends General GRE, so optional does not mean irrelevant. [s1] [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Mathematics FAQ says a subject score can help, but is less important than General GRE; it is not required. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Two recommendations required. [s1] [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required personal statement (also described as essay/statement of purpose in CAS FAQ). The public mathematics/CAS checklist does not give a precise prompt, length, font/spacing or file-type limit; inspect the current application before drafting. A separate second statement is not established. [s2] [s3]",
    "warnings": "[Standing rule] No substantive GRE conflict: optional at CAS and recommended by mathematics can both hold. General CAS June 30 deadline and usual late-material accommodation do not override the mathematics January 1 rule. [s1] [s3] [s5]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm January 1 year/time zone and actual late-reference allowance; read current portal statement prompt; obtain CAS 2027 English minimums/exemption approval; verify annual stipend, funding duration, international TA language rules, commitment date and letter receipt/reuse. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5] [s15]",
