    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing relational rule: January 20 of the entry year, i.e. January 20, 2027 for Fall 2027 if unchanged. No clock time/timezone stated. Fall only; confirm the live term in Slate. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Fall 2027 ordinary Math stipend not established. Old department page quotes USD21,990 first year including conditional summer teaching, and later summer about9000; these are stale, not a 2027 offer. University 2026-27 minimum half-time TA level1 is1162 biweekly; research/teaching-excluded level1 is1028, so classification matters. Current 2027-28 UDF: approximately 32500 yearly GA base plus10000 annual fellowship; later department base must match. Ordinary offer needs separate confirmation. [s3] [s4] [s10] [s12]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor's entry is compatible with the department's PhD route; complete the UChicago degree before enrollment. University normally expects at least 3.0 in junior/senior undergraduate work. Math admits internationally and only for fall; the ordinary Math/Applied Math MS is not a separate entry route. F-1 status is not academic disqualification; new immigration documentation follows admission. [s1] [s2] [s7] [s8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Contact grad@math.msu.edu about current requirements/fee support; select Mathematics PhD in Slate, supply junior/senior/graduate mathematics and statistics courses including planned courses, register three referees, upload the required documents and pay or arrange departmental payment. No prior supervisor agreement is published. Check the English waiver before omitting a test. [s1] [s5] [s13]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] If not waived, TOEFL taken after January 21, 2026: total4.5, reading/speaking≥4, listening/writing≥4.5; older TOEFL80 with R/L/S≥19,W≥22. IELTS6.5 with every band≥6. Central PTE53(R/L/S≥51,W≥59) and DET110 also appear, but Math explicitly names TOEFL/IELTS, so confirm alternatives. Reports valid two years before entry; do not infer Math accepts provisional English admission. [s1] [s6] [s7] [Standing rule] A completed regular US four-year bachelor's with most credits earned in the US qualifies for automatic admissions waiver (not an online/experiential/overseas-branch degree). UChicago meets the institutional setting; confirm handling while the BA is still in progress. A nonautomatic waiver is submitted by the department. Admission waiver does NOT waive spoken-English TA certification: TOEFL speaking27/5.5, IELTS speaking8, MSU Speaking Test50, or specified language-course plus oral-test route. [s6] [s9] [Conflict] Department support applies to admitted international students; old college and departmental recruitment awards explicitly include all applicants. Old UDF/UEF page limits eligibility to citizens/permanent residents, whereas the updated 2027 central UDF criteria publish no citizenship condition. International UDF eligibility therefore needs explicit clarification before counting the award. [s2] [s4] [s12]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD75 shown in central international Slate payment instructions; nonrefundable status not established in the checked page. Confirm displayed amount for the 2027 application before payment. [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] REQUIRED by both current department admissions page and FAQ; unofficial report initially, official if admitted; five-year validity. No published Fall 2027 exception found. [s1] [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Strongly recommended, not formally required. FAQ warns admission without it is very rare and asks for other strong mathematical evidence, such as advanced courses or research examples. Do not mistake optional for indifferent. Five-year validity. [s1] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three recommendations, submitted electronically by the writers. Math does not publicly specify a different mandatory academic/professional mix or maximum. [s1] [s2]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] Required Academic Statement. Public Math checklist supplies the label but no exact prompt, length cap or formatting rule. Obtain the live Math supplement wording before drafting; generic screenshots for Accounting or Chemistry prompts are not Math requirements. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Official-versus-unofficial initial transcript wording differs between Math checklist and FAQ; use electronic unofficial review copies and arrange official verification when required. Old department funding/UDF model is superseded in part by the 2027 central award; ordinary stipend and citizenship restrictions unresolved. Trailing-slash UDF URL yields stale 2026 content whereas canonical no-slash URL gives 2027. Do not copy historical dates or Chemistry/Accounting essay prompts. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s12]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm Fall 2027 ordinary stipend and full fee/summer coverage; current UDF international eligibility; exact Academic/Personal Statement prompts and upload limits; pending-BA English waiver; separate letter/score deadlines; reference replacement/reuse; acceptance date. Ask Kulkarni/Magyar for recent research and each faculty member about 2027 supervision if shortlisted. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5] [s12]",
