    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] Unresolved conflict: Courant lists January 4 without year; NYU Shanghai’s same GSAS Mathematics PhD process expressly lists January 6, 2027 for Fall 2027. Do not silently transfer Shanghai’s date to New York. Treat January 4 as the conservative planning date, with year/timezone unconfirmed; request written New York confirmation. [s1] [s6]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] 2026-27 GSAS doctoral base stipend USD 37,132 for the academic year (USD 18,566/semester), not a verified 2027-28 Courant offer. MacCracken covers nine months plus tuition, registration fees and individual comprehensive health insurance. February 2026 math guidebook says no general departmental/GSAS summer allocation; summer grant, teaching or internship support must be separately arranged. [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s degree completed by enrollment permits direct PhD application; full-time study only. Minimum background: three calculus semesters including advanced calculus or linear algebra; actual preparation is normally greater. UChicago bachelor’s and international status are compatible with application; GSAS explicitly considers applicants irrespective of citizenship. [s1] [s7]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select Mathematics PhD in GSAS (not Tandon); only one GSAS application per term. Gather transcripts, three references and subject GRE or short impossibility explanation. Resolve conflicting January dates with admissions@math.nyu.edu before submission. [s1] [s2] [s6]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Department names TOEFL or IELTS for applicants without native English or an English-medium bachelor’s/master’s. GSAS guidance reproduced by another department recommends TOEFL 100 (old scale) or IELTS 7; current GSAS English page was inaccessible, so new test-scale thresholds and acceptance of DET require verification. [s1] [s10] [Standing rule] Completed UChicago English-medium bachelor’s fits departmental degree exemption. Whether an in-progress degree qualifies at submission and whether evidence/waiver form is required could not be verified centrally; confirm if not yet conferred. F-1 status alone is not the exemption. [s1] [s8] [Standing rule] International applicants use same deadline and are not excluded by merit-based MacCracken description. Exact offer and any outside award citizenship condition control; federal need-based aid should not be assumed available to F-1 students. [s1] [s3] [s7]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 110 listed in official NYU Journalism instructions for the same GSAS application; current mathematics portal amount not independently accessible, so verify before payment. [s10]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Admissions policy: neither required nor accepted. Funding page incorrectly/olderly says general and subject optional; follow specific admissions policy pending confirmation. [s1] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[Conflict] Admissions policy expects Math Subject GRE; if impractical, attach short explanatory statement. Funding page says optional for all PhD applications; conflicting official pages. ETS institution 2596, GRE department 0703. [s1] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three electronic letters; strongly recommended that at least two be mathematics/science course instructors. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] Exact current Mathematics required/optional status, prompt, length/format and upload-versus-link rule were not established: public math checklist is incomplete and GSAS statements/resource-center pages returned access errors. Retrieve current application instructions before drafting; do not import another NYU school’s requirements. [s1] [s8] [s9]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Main admissions page expects subject GRE and rejects General; funding page says both optional. Main New York January 4 annual deadline differs from Shanghai explicit January 6, 2027. Central help could not settle these. [s1] [s3] [s6]",
