    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Fall 2027 priority December 15, 2026; final funded-PhD deadline March 1, 2027. Central rule: application and supporting documents due by midnight Eastern Standard Time on the applicable deadline. John is international even while studying in Chicago; do not use domestic June dates. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] July 2026 Math guide: USD22,125 per academic year for standard50%TA(20h/week), not an explicit Fall 2027 amount. PhD offers include stipend, tuition and student health insurance; student fees remain payable. SummerTA may exist but is not guaranteed. RA pay generally≥TA. Generic fellowship range22000-34000 yearly is not an individual offer. [s1] [s11] [s12]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago mathematics bachelor's meets the degree/field route, subject to completion and academic review. University normally requires GPA3.0; Math publishes no additional GPA cutoff. Expected preparation: proof-based linear algebra, modern algebra and two semesters of analysis; missing second analysis must be made up. International/F-1 applicants eligible for on-campus PhD. [s1] [s6] [s8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD; prepare unofficial transcripts, ≤2-page personal/academic goals statement, CV and three referees. Email graduate_applications@ncsu.edu for UChicago-study English waiver review. No supervisor consent/interview required publicly. After academic acceptance, complete Visa Clearance Form and Certificate of Financial Responsibility; VCF becomes accessible only then. Admission acceptance precedes I-20 creation. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s8]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Without waiver: newTOEFL total4 and every section≥4; speaking≥5 forTA. LegacyTOEFL total80,each≥18; speaking23 for interactiveTA or26 for lecturing/labTA. IELTS Academic6.5 every band, speaking7 forTA; DET110 with listed literacy/comprehension/conversation/production≥110, conversation/production125 forTA. Scores valid24months before entry. [s8] [s40] [Standing rule] At least one completed year full-time in a degree program at a regionally accredited four-year US institution, cumulativeGPA≥3.0, permits admission waiver. Thus a completed UChicago BA normally qualifies if GPA condition met; graduation is not necessary to meet the one-year rule. Email graduate_applications@ncsu.edu for transcript evaluation. Confirm whether any separate TA oral assessment is required; admissions waiver is not explicitly a blanket exemption fromTA standards. [s7] [s8] [s40] [Standing rule] International PhD applicants eligible for departmentalTA/RA and university fellowships generally. F-1 students ineligible for state residency retain total tuition coverage while GSSP-eligible; do not apply US/PR second-year residency rules to John. Named external awards can impose citizenship limits. [s1] [s8] [s11] [s14]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD95 for international/nonresident-alien applicants, nonrefundable. USD85 domestic/USPR does not apply merely because John attends UChicago. [s2] [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional/accepted for PhD and MS; no longer required. The GRE requirements stated for certificate students do not govern PhD applicants. [s1] [s6]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional/accepted. Catalog explicitly says a good Math Subject score may help admission; not a test-blind policy. [s1] [s6]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three online recommendations from people who know academic record and graduate potential; mathematics/related professors who taught or supervised research are preferred. [s1] [s4] [s5]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Math calls the main essay Personal Statement. Faithful paraphrase of full public prompt: explain academic aims, career plans and particular mathematical interests. Maximum two pages; upload electronically. No font, spacing, file-size or margin specification published. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Final-transcript timing differs: application handbook permits pending-degree completion by end of first semester whereas required-document schedule says before first semester. Department English table omits newTOEFL scale, supplied by central current handbook/help. July 2026 guide says most students funded while current admissions page promises fundedPhD offers; verify individual offer. OldServiceNow versions may contradict current November 3 revision rules. [s1] [s5] [s8] [s9] [s11] [s17]",
