    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] December 31 for full consideration, in the department’s September 2027 admissions context (therefore December 31, 2026 by contextual inference). The date line itself omits year and time zone; obtain portal confirmation. Applications opened September 15, 2026 centrally. [math] [dates]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Published university-wide 2026-27 minimum: USD 47,748 per year, four quarters/year (12 months), before tax; not a confirmed 2027-28 Mathematics offer. Funding covers tuition, health-services fees and annual health-insurance premium; activity and other uncovered fees remain student expenses. Individual mathematics amount and 2027-28 increase require offer confirmation. [fund] [fundfaq] [fundmodel]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle with the UChicago bachelor’s completed before enrollment; no prior master’s required. Mathematics offers a PhD, not a terminal master’s. International students may apply. TGS currently restricts applications from persons located in or ordinarily resident in specified comprehensively sanctioned regions; citizenship alone is not the published test. F-1 status alone does not settle that question. [requirements] [intl] [math]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Use the TGS New Student application; only one TGS program per year. Prepare two essays, academic records and the detailed mathematics-course list. Ask professors before entering requests. If seeking the limited international fee waiver, upload both essays and transcript FIRST, then email math-gradadm@northwestern.edu; the recommended October 31 contact date has passed. Request English waiver through Mathematics after submission. [requirements] [math] [letters] [intl]",
    "international": "[Conflict] If no waiver: Math publishes TOEFL iBT 95, IELTS 6.5, MET 64. TGS publishes PhD TOEFL 90, IELTS 7, MET 61, so IELTS is an explicit discrepancy; ask for the governing minimum and revised TOEFL-scale handling. Scores must be within two years before intended entry. DET and TOEFL Essentials are not accepted. Separate spoken-English qualification applies to TA/GA funding, including entrants with an admission waiver. [math] [intl] [taenglish] [Standing rule] A completed UChicago English-medium degree qualifies in principle. Mathematics explicitly includes degrees that WILL be completed; central FAQ permits an in-progress English degree waiver provided the degree is earned before enrollment. Approval is processed only after application submission and supporting documentation. Do not mistake this admission waiver for TA-language clearance; Math requires spoken-English qualification by the start of year two. [math] [intl] [faq] [taenglish] [Standing rule] TGS explicitly says international students generally receive the same funding as domestic students. TA funding requires separate spoken-English qualification; degree-based admission waiver does not remove it. Federal/external awards have award-specific citizenship rules. [fundfaq] [taenglish]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 95, nonrefundable. Portal accepts Visa, Mastercard, Discover and American Express; debit card must carry a supported card logo. [fee]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Not considered for September 2027 applications. This is stronger than optional; there is no admissions benefit to sending a score. [math]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Not considered for September 2027 applications. This is stronger than optional; there is no admissions benefit to sending a score. [math]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Minimum three, maximum four; professors familiar with advanced mathematical work, preferably experienced in PhD advising. Strong advice: no more than one REU letter. This supersedes the TGS general minimum of two. [math] [letters]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required Academic Statement upload, 500-1,000 words (maximum 1,000). Prompt paraphrase: academic interests and reasons for this program; preparation through education, work, research or training; Northwestern fit with intellectual/professional aims; questions to investigate and relevant faculty. Math additionally asks specificity about qualifications and research fit. Font, spacing and file-type limits beyond portal upload are not public. [essays] [math]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Math IELTS minimum 6.5 conflicts with TGS 7; Math TOEFL/MET higher than TGS floors is ordinary program tightening. TGS two-letter baseline is superseded by Math 3-4. General TGS GRE examples refer to older years but Math explicitly excludes both tests for September 2027. ESAM CV/writing-sample rules must not be transferred to pure Mathematics. [math] [intl] [letters] [faq]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm portal’s exact deadline/time zone and CV/sample permissions; request English waiver after submission; check remaining international fee-waiver allocation immediately after uploading required preliminary documents. Confirm 2027-28 stipend, letter reuse/Interfolio, commitment date and advising capacity, especially Antieau’s leave. Tamarkin’s recent research-paper metadata could not be verified despite official-page and targeted searches. [math] [intl] [fund] [faq] [decision] [roster]",
