    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] December 15 for fall full consideration, on the standing page linked to the 2027 portal; no explicit year/time or separate letter grace period given. Submit complete materials by then. Later materials are not guaranteed review; contact math-gstudies@tamu.edu before a late application. The applicant-selected referee due date is a reminder, not an extension. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] Department advertises $2,350/month; support page specifies nine paid fall/spring months, yielding $21,150 academic-year stipend (calculated). First summer support is guaranteed, but amount not specified; subsequent summers depend on standing and funds. Tuition/required fees covered for eligible PhD GAs. New university floor effective October 1 2026 is $2,000/month at 50%FTE, below the advertised departmental rate; neither is a confirmed Fall 2027 offer. [s6] [s7] [s8] [qrt1]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor's preparation suffices; most applicants hold mathematics degrees, but other backgrounds are considered. Minimum preparation advanced calculus, linear algebra and differential equations; typical admitted preparation includes two semesters each of real analysis and senior algebra plus another advanced course. International F1 applicants are eligible. [s2] [s3]",
