    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s degree and generally 3.0 GPA. Pure track preparation: multivariable calculus, introductory differential equations, linear algebra, and at least three advanced mathematics courses including abstract algebra and real analysis in one and several variables, with 3.0 average. Mathematics major is not obligatory. A UChicago mathematics degree is an eligible route subject to these details. [s1] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Prepare unofficial transcripts, personal statement, three referees, passport and current visa copies; financial documentation is also listed for international applicants. Submit the application early enough to trigger referee invitations before the all-materials deadline, then pay through Nelnet. [s1] [s3]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Central minima include TOEFL 79/revised 4, IELTS 6.5, PTE 55, Cambridge 185 and Duolingo 120. Official agency reports must be within two years when International Admissions reviews the application. Departments may assess English readiness beyond an exemption. [s2] [Standing rule] Automatic exemption for international students transferring from a U.S. college who completed or WILL COMPLETE a degree, or attended at least two years, with GPA at least 2.0 and no more than a three-year break. UChicago attendance fits if these conditions hold. Nonstandard exceptions require a departmental petition, not a student petition. [s2] [Standing rule] International students are explicitly eligible for Presidential Fellowships if qualified. Department supports graduate TAs; individual assistantship immigration and language conditions still need confirmation. Schomburg Fellowship requires U.S. citizenship or permanent residence, so an F-1-only applicant is ineligible. [s4]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 75 nonrefundable. After submitting, pay online by credit card or ACH through Nelnet. [s1]",
