    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three letters, normally professors or employers. No prescribed format; referees should use their institution’s letterhead. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] One required personal statement. Prompt paraphrase: describe preparation (academic and relevant work/life experiences), motivation, proposed mathematical and interdisciplinary interests, career aims and useful additional context. No public word/page cap or formatting requirement; submit in application, external linking not specified. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Presidential GPA eligibility is unequivocal on central fellowship page but CAS offers an unclear alternative GRE criterion. Use GPA 3.40 as the verified rule and ask department about exceptions. [s5] [s6]",
