    "funding": "[Conflict] University-wide AY 2026-27 minimum for a 0.50-FTE graduate assistant is USD 25,654 for nine months; fiscal-year minimum USD 33,350 is a distinct appointment basis. Neither is a published Fall 2027 Math offer. Handbook's February 2026 table starts at USD 23,000 and is superseded by the later higher floor. At 0.50 FTE, base tuition and individual student health premium are covered; mandatory/program/course fees are not generally covered. University Fellows first year: USD 37,000 (15,000 fall + 15,000 spring + 7,000 summer), base fall/spring tuition and health; year-two professional-development USD 500. [s5] [s6] [s7] [s9]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago bachelor's is a qualifying degree route, provided it is completed before enrollment and the mathematical preparation requirement is met: advanced analysis, abstract algebra and linear algebra; fuller algebra/analysis sequences and topology preferred, complex variables expected for PhD. Research is not a prerequisite. F-1 status does not itself establish academic eligibility. [s1] [s2]",
