    "international": "[Conflict] Central doctoral admission: TOEFL iBT 4.0 on the new scale (old scale 79), IELTS 7.0 with each component 6.0, or listed alternatives including PTE 60. TOEFL Essentials is not a doctoral admission option. Scores must be within two years of enrollment. Math's older TOEFL 79 wording predates the new scale. TA qualification is separate: new TOEFL speaking 5.0/old 24, IELTS speaking 7.5, or another approved teaching-language route; a US degree does not automatically waive it. [s1] [s2] [Standing rule] A completed US bachelor's qualifies for the admission English exemption. If applying before degree completion, the central rule requires two years full-time study and 48 graded upper-division semester units within the specified two-year window; have Arizona verify how UChicago quarter units and upper-division coursework satisfy this. Admission waiver does not waive TA speaking qualification. [s2] [Standing rule] International students may pursue departmental assistantships subject to teaching-English and appointment rules. University Fellows eligibility says any newly admitted qualifying doctoral student, without a citizenship restriction. Graduate Access Fellowship explicitly targets domestic students and is not an F-1 funding route. [s1] [s8] [s9]",
