    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] December 1 annual complete-file deadline, including supporting documents. No explicit December 2026 year or cutoff/time zone was verified. Do not treat the page's December 2027 GRE-waiver note as the application deadline. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[Unresolved] Exact annual Math stipend for Fall 2027 not publicly established. Department lists TA/GSR/fellowships and fee/health remissions; its undated residual fee figures (USD 256.50/quarter, 769.50/year) appear old and should not be treated as 2027 costs. Additional current evidence: the UC contract fixes Group 1 quarter-campus entry TA pay at USD 4,278 per month for a 50% appointment effective October 1, 2027. Nine paid months would be USD 38,502 gross by arithmetic; this is a salary scale, not a guaranteed department offer, appointment length, September payment, or summer award. Higher steps depend on qualifying experience. [s8] [s27]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago bachelor's satisfies the recognized-degree route; final award required before enrollment, with minimum cumulative undergraduate GPA 3.0 unless an exception is approved. International applicants may apply; select PhD rather than simultaneous MS/PhD applications in the same program. [s3] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[2027 confirmed] Fall 2027 portal opened October 1, 2026. Choose Physical Sciences / Mathematics / PhD and state research area; arrange official Math GRE or obtain clarification on the exceptional waiver; confirm pending-degree English exemption with mathgrad@uci.edu. [s1] [s10]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Unless exempt, official TOEFL minimum 80 before January 21, 2026 or 4 afterward; IELTS overall 7 with each module at least 6. Two-year validity; no MyBest, Essentials or ITP Plus. TA requirements differ: speaking TOEFL 26 old/5 new, IELTS 8, or campus-approved assessment if no exemption. [s3] [s4] [s26] [Conflict] Central admission exemption covers an earned undergraduate/master's degree whose sole instructional language is English in WHED; completed UChicago degree should fit, subject to record verification. Treatment of an in-progress degree is not explicit. Math page instead says US post-baccalaureate degree, conflicting with central policy. TA exemption separately covers sole-English undergraduate degrees earned within five years before UCI admission. [s1] [s3] [s7] [Standing rule] Nonresident tuition fellowships and TA support are available; exact nonresident tuition coverage depends on award. Public page mentions three-year post-candidacy nonresident tuition reduction; verify current offer terms. [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 155 international; USD 135 US citizen/permanent resident; credit card only, nonrefundable. [s1] [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional to submit; no minimum; official ETS scores code 4859, five-year validity. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Conflict] Required standing rule, official scores within five years. Exceptional inability-to-test waiver has conflicting dates: indexed main page says December 2025 applications, live mirror says December 2027. It asks a paragraph at end of Personal Statement plus future test date to permit submission. Ask whether exception applies to this December 2026 application before relying on it. [s1] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three electronic letters required. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required. Paraphrased Math prompt: career/research goals, why UCI Math and its faculty fit, and preparation to become a strong researcher. Exact Math length/format not published on the checked page; the 1,200-word limits on other UCI departments should be confirmed in the Math portal rather than assumed. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] GRE exception says December 2025 vs December 2027 across official versions; English degree waiver post-baccalaureate vs central undergraduate/master's; TA mandatory speaking wording vs central degree exemption; final transcripts degree institutions vs all institutions; fee waiver financial need vs current domestic prep/veteran-only policy. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s5] [s6] [s7]",
