    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] 13 December 2026. Time and time zone not established on math listing or department page; verify portal cutoff. [s1]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No exact annual mathematics stipend published on reviewed admissions, financial-support or handbook pages; amounts vary annually. Guarantee normally includes living income, full registration fees, health insurance and nonresident tuition. Obtain 2027-28 gross cash, appointment months and summer amount from offer. Cost-of-attendance or maximum-support limits are not stipend offers. Published UC contract Table B.1 provides UCLA Group 2, salary point 1, 50% TA appointment USD 4,323/month effective October 1, 2026 and USD 4,432/month effective October 1, 2027. These are contractual monthly appointment rates, not a promised 12-month Mathematics package; multiply only by actual paid months in the offer. [s2] [s3] [s10] [ucwages27]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago bachelor’s completed by matriculation is eligible in degree type; academic eligibility additionally requires 3.0 in junior/senior and post-baccalaureate work, 3.5 upper-division math GPA, and at least 12 quarter/8 semester substantial upper-division math courses. Exceptions only for demonstrated exceptional quantitative ability. International applicants need comparable record. PhD admission only; MA/MAT suspended. [s1] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select pure or applied area and field in application; choose only one UCLA major. Prepare transcripts, required math-course list, SOP, personal statement, three letters, Math GRE and fee/waiver evidence. Check whether department still wants original transcripts at application. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL 87 before 21 January 2026 or 4.5 on/after that date; IELTS Academic 7.0. No TOEFL MyBest. Scores valid two years at application; latest test only. Admission proficiency, academic writing placement and TA oral proficiency are distinct requirements. [s6] [Conflict] Completed or forthcoming accredited US bachelor’s degree qualifies for admission-test exemption. UChicago undergraduate degree also meets central prior-education route for TA oral-proficiency eligibility. Department blanket TOP requirement for non-native speakers conflicts with this newer central exemption: verify application to math funding. [s6] [s2] [Standing rule] International students eligible for departmental fellowships/TA/RA and nonresident tuition support. US federal/need-based loans and work-study generally unavailable. Some extramural/RTG awards have separate citizenship restrictions. [s2] [s3] [s9]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] US $155 for international applicants, nonrefundable, credit/debit card. [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not listed among required tests; current math program specifies only Subject Mathematics. Public source does not establish whether unsolicited General GRE is considered or ignored; not required should not be read as forbidden. [s1] [s2]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Required in current 2027-28 program listing and department checklist. No public 2027 exception identified. [s1] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three, preferably all and at least two from mathematicians familiar with recent work; additional letters not considered helpful by departmental FAQ. [s1] [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required upload. Central prompt paraphrase: purpose/subfields, preparation and research outcomes, other relevant experience, UCLA fit/potential mentors, career plans. Central page says programs choose 500/1,000/1,500-word caps; math cap and typography not publicly established. Verify before drafting to length. [s2] [s5]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Four versus five years guaranteed; blanket TOP testing versus US-degree exemption; first versus second January week score grace; original-transcript requirement needs confirmation; current personal statement appears centrally but not department checklist. [s2] [s3] [s5] [s6] [s7]",
