    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Priority December 14, 2026; final January 5, 2027 for Fall 2027 PhD admission. Time of day/timezone not published on the checked department page. [s1]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] Most mathematics PhD admits receive stipend/salary plus tuition, fees, and health coverage, but no exact annual 2027-28 stipend was established. Distinguish the actual offer from general support descriptions. UC Article 35, Table B.1, sets the Group 1 quarter-system 50% TA salary at USD 4,278/month at point 1 from October 1, 2027 (points 2/3: 4,449/4,582). UCSC and UCR fall in Group 1. Nine paid months at point 1 would total USD 38,502 by arithmetic; this is a negotiated wage scale, not a verified mathematics annual package, funded-month promise, net stipend or summer guarantee. Confirm appointment fraction, starting point, dates and supplements in the offer. [s3] [s10] [ucwages2027]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Accredited bachelor’s degree and GPA 3.0. Mathematics requires six quarter courses or four semester courses of upper-division proof-based mathematics, covering suitable algebra, analysis, topology, differential equations, numerical analysis, or probability. Planned/in-progress courses completed before graduation can count. International UChicago applicants can apply. [s2] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Apply to Mathematics PhD for fall; prepare a mathematics course list with descriptions and textbooks and arrange three referees, including at least two mathematics faculty. Current requirements should be used instead of the old /grads/apply/ pages. [s1] [s2]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Central minimum old TOEFL 80/new 4.0 or IELTS 7 with each section 6. Tests must remain valid within two years at enrollment. TOEFL MyBest and IELTS One Skill Retake are not accepted; TOEFL Home and IELTS Online are accepted. TA English eligibility is a separate employment requirement. [s4] [Standing rule] An applicant who has earned OR WILL EARN a bachelor’s or higher degree from a US institution where instruction is solely in English meets the degree exemption. This explicitly covers an expected UChicago degree, subject to completion. TA employment language rules remain separate. [s4] [Unresolved] Department support is offered to international PhD students through the same multiyear framework; confirm all nonresident tuition and TA language provisions in the individual offer. Citizenship eligibility for particular supplemental fellowships is unverified. [s3] [s10]",
    "costs": "[Prior cycle] Central page lists USD 155 international/USD 135 domestic, but explicitly labels that rate Summer 2024 through Spring 2027. The Fall 2027 rate is therefore not confirmed by this statement. [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Neither required nor considered; the department says submitted GRE scores are not viewable in its application review. Older pages claiming a required general GRE are superseded. [s2] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Neither required nor considered; the department says submitted GRE scores are not viewable in its application review. Older pages claiming a required general GRE are superseded. [s2] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required; at least two must be mathematics faculty under the department’s rule. All letters must be in English. Extra letters are discouraged centrally. [s2] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required single Graduate Statement of Purpose, maximum 2,000 words. Faithful paraphrase of six areas: academic/professional preparation; research/professional interests; fit with UCR faculty/resources; motivation now and long-term aims; intended scholarly or public contribution; and leadership, collaboration, mentoring, or outreach. Upload to the application. Font, margins, and file-size rules were not publicly established. [s4]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Old pages claim GPA 3.20, required general GRE, two essays, and reference invitations only after paid submission. Current pages state GPA 3.0, no GRE consideration, one combined SOP, and immediate referee invitations on saving. Old international May 1 deadlines must not replace the current January 5 final PhD deadline. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s8] [s9]",
