    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Fall 2027 Mathematics PhD: opens September 2, 2026; closes December 2, 2026. The same deadline applies to the listed mathematics PhD variants including CSME/statistics; separate mathematics master's programs close February 3, 2027. The checked mathematics page does not state a closing clock/time zone. Late applications are not accepted. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] The department does not publish an exact guaranteed 2027 annual package. For a UCSD Group-1 quarter-system TA at 50% FTE, the signed UC wage table explicitly sets October 1, 2027 monthly salary points at $4,278, $4,449 and $4,582. A nine-month point-1 appointment would total $38,502 gross (9 × $4,278; calculation, not an offer). October 2026 point 1 is $4,100. Tuition/fee remission and qualifying health-premium coverage are additional benefits governed by appointment and contract; summer pay is separate. [s19] [s3] [s20] [s21]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle for the Mathematics PhD with a UChicago mathematics bachelor's completed before enrollment. A mathematics degree is recommended, or comparably strong preparation; normally GPA 3.0 or better. A year each of upper-division algebra and real analysis is encouraged. Admission is departmental, with no published requirement to secure an adviser first. International F1 applicants are accepted. [s1] [s8] [s7]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD in the online application; UCSD permits only one application to a program within a department, so do not also submit the mathematics MA/MS application. Prepare unofficial records, SOP, a list of mathematics courses already taken and projected with textbooks, and at least three referees. Arrange official test delivery if submitting scores. No interview or advance faculty commitment is required by the public mathematics process. [s1] [s10] [s2]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Current central minimums if not exempt: TOEFL 4.5 on the revised scale or 85 on the previous scale, IELTS 7, PTE Academic 65, or DET 120; scores normally valid two years. DET is accepted from the fall-2026 cycle. Mathematics also recommends strong speaking performance. The mathematics FAQ retains an older one-year-study exemption formulation and older TOEFL scale; the current central degree-and-GPA rule should be checked when recording an exemption. [s4] [s2] [Standing rule] The current central policy exempts an applicant who has earned or will earn a bachelor's, master's or doctorate with at least B/3.0 grades from a regionally accredited US institution where English is the sole instructional language. A UChicago bachelor's therefore qualifies conditionally on those academic facts. The current TA policy explicitly accepts this qualifying prior-degree admission exemption for teaching certification as well; ensure the completed degree and exemption are recorded before the first TA appointment. [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] International PhD students can receive department TA/GSR/fellowship support. Record the admission-English exemption and satisfy TA certification before teaching. Verify nonresident supplemental tuition coverage explicitly: the UC agreement's automatic postcandidacy NRST reduction/remission has a limited three-year period and is not a substitute for an offer's precandidacy funding commitment. [s3] [s5] [s20]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] International application fee $155; US citizens/permanent residents $135. John's F1 status places him in the international fee category. [s1] [s12]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not required. Public mathematics wording permits optional submission; it does not say scores are forbidden or ignored. [s1] [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Not required, but highly recommended. No departmental minimum score is published, and the overall application is reviewed holistically. [s1] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] At least three recommendations. Central admissions permits more in principle but advises checking with the department before exceeding the requested number. [s1] [s6]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] SOP is required. The central prompt asks, in paraphrase, how your interests developed; preparation through research, study/work/service and lessons learned; degree/subfield and career goals; one or two possible research directions; and fit with UCSD faculty. It also invites relevant qualities, initiative, independence and educational barriers. No public mathematics-specific word/page, font or margin limit was found. Upload through the application; the linked source preserves the full wording. [s1] [s11]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current central English policy uses a completed/forthcoming degree and GPA threshold, while the mathematics FAQ retains an older one-year-study formulation; John's expected US degree can meet the current rule. Use current TA degree-exemption guidance rather than the linked 2017 policy PDF. Current catalog/history identifies Wenzl and Rabin as emeriti despite older research-group placements, and records DeVleming's arrival from UMass and Zhang's arrival from Wisconsin. Do not infer active recruitment from old group pages. [s4] [s2] [s5] [s28] [s29]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Confirm the December 2 closing clock/time zone, live SOP/CV/optional-upload limits and exact initial-reference send trigger. Ask referees to aim for December 2 despite later rolling review. Verify the UChicago 3.0-degree exemption is recorded for admission and TA eligibility. Obtain written stipend months, salary point/FTE, summer pay, all tuition/NRST/fees/health terms, official-record due date and offer reply deadline. Ask potential advisers about 2027 availability, especially emeriti and visitors. [s1] [s6] [s5] [s3] [s8]",
