    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] Fall 2027 live directory: Wednesday, December 16, 2026. The department instead publishes December 15, 2026 while incorrectly calling the coming quarter Fall 2026. The new university standardized schedule supports December 16, but the discrepancy requires confirmation. Math-specific hour/timezone not published in checked sources. Practical safeguard: complete everything by December 15. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s40]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] No fixed Mathematics offer amount is published. Binding UC scale effective October 1, 2027: Group 1 TA at 50% appointment, entry salary point, USD 4,278/month; nine paid months would equal USD 38,502 gross by arithmetic, not a guaranteed year-round offer. Current October 2026 rate is USD 4,100/month (USD 36,900 for nine months). Summer, appointment percentage and first September timing require the individual offer. Qualifying appointments remit tuition, specified fees and health premiums. [s8] [s17] [s18] [s19] [s41]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle with a mathematics/related bachelor's completed before enrollment and undergraduate GPA at least 3.0. International status is allowed. For applicants without a master's, central instructions recommend selecting the combined PhD/MA where available; this differs from the UCSB-undergraduate-only five-year combined program. [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD/MA or confirm the appropriate objective with math-gradinfo@math.ucsb.edu. Prepare the required Math GRE, three referees, two statements, CV and course descriptions/textbooks. Only one UCSB application per year is allowed. No prior supervisor agreement is listed. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL iBT: 4.0 for tests on/after January 21, 2026, or 80 on the older scale; IELTS 7; Duolingo 120. Home Edition/approved academic online formats accepted; TOEFL Essentials/ITP Plus and IELTS One Skill Retake are not. Teaching certification is separate. [s1] [s5] [Standing rule] A completed UChicago bachelor's qualifies under the accredited US English-only degree route. Public wording says completed: if the degree remains in progress at application, ask whether an anticipatory exemption is available. Completing the entire undergraduate degree in English also exempts Grad ELPE placement, after verification. Non-native-English prospective TAs still require the TA language evaluation. [s4] [s12] [Standing rule] International doctoral students are eligible for assistantships and automatic IDRF. IDRF covers nonresident supplemental tuition from the fourth quarter until candidacy, conditional on timely progress/good standing; it does not cover year one. After candidacy, nonresident tuition is waived for up to nine registered quarters. Verify year-one NRST funding in the offer. Federal need-based loans/work-study listed by Math are restricted to US citizens/permanent residents. [s8] [s9] [s10]",
    "costs": "[Conflict] USD 155 for an F-1 international applicant; USD 135 applies only to US citizens/permanent residents. Nonrefundable; payment must be received by the deadline. The guide permits credit-card payment through the portal after submission, whereas FAQ wording says at submission; plan to pay promptly within the deadline. [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not accepted: the department explicitly instructs applicants not to submit General GRE scores. [s3]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Required for Fall 2027. Official ETS reporting is necessary; no minimum score published. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required; academic references preferred. Portal accepts up to four electronic letters. [s1] [s5]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required narrative upload. Prompt paraphrase: graduate-study motivation, intended specialization, previous academic preparation and career plans, plus evidence of aptitude for UCSB. Avoid repeating the Personal History Statement. No hard public maximum; FAQ suggests approximately two pages or more. Font/spacing limits not established. [s1] [s5]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] December 16, 2026 in current directory versus December 15 on Math pages; department's Fall 2026 label conflicts with that date. Final official records: September 1 on admitted-international page versus first instruction day in general guide. Department warning about later NRST omits central IDRF coverage. Current roster marks Goodearl, Huisgen-Zimmermann, Stopple and Yitang Zhang emeriti despite research-group listings. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s8] [s10] [s12] [s20] [s21] [s22]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm December 15/16 and cutoff timezone for every item/funding; anticipatory English exemption if UChicago degree unfinished; current course-list upload slot; SOP/CV formatting; submitted-letter replacement; 2027 Math monthly schedule, summer and year-one NRST coverage; fellowship nomination extras; and adviser availability. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s8] [s16]",
