    "deadlineDetails": "[Unresolved] Fall 2027 graduate applications are explicitly open on the public application portal, but the exact Mathematics PhD closing date and time remain unverified. The current department page gives only an October-to-end-of-January application window; the current catalog says the deadline is usually in the first half of January. Neither supplies an exact Fall 2027 deadline. The former January 2, 2025 at 8:59 p.m. Pacific deadline belongs to the 2025-26 application cycle and must not be shifted to January 2, 2027. [s1] [s9] [s10] [s11] [qbd1_d1] [qbd1_d2] [qbd1_d3] [qbd1_d4] [qbd1_d5]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] No exact annual mathematics stipend was established. A 50% TA appointment is 220 hours per quarter, approximately 20 hours/week. Central guidance warns ordinary TA tuition remission excludes nonresident supplemental tuition unless another award covers it; obtain explicit NRST coverage in the offer. UC Article 35, Table B.1, sets the Group 1 quarter-system 50% TA salary at USD 4,278/month at point 1 from October 1, 2027 (points 2/3: 4,449/4,582). UCSC and UCR fall in Group 1. Nine paid months at point 1 would total USD 38,502 by arithmetic; this is a negotiated wage scale, not a verified mathematics annual package, funded-month promise, net stipend or summer guarantee. Confirm appointment fraction, starting point, dates and supplements in the offer. [s1] [s7] [ucwages2027]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A bachelor’s degree must be completed before enrollment; a mathematics degree is recommended, with advanced coursework/research/teaching helpful. Central guidance requires at least a B average in the last two undergraduate years. International applicants are eligible. [s1] [s4] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select the doctoral route and submit only ONE application in the admission cycle; simultaneous applications to multiple UCSC departments are not accepted. Register referees at least two weeks before the deadline. If requesting a mathematics fee waiver, prepare and upload the separate financial-need statement. [s1] [s3] [s8]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Mathematics admission minimums fall under the general category: old TOEFL 83/new 4.0, or IELTS 7. TA eligibility separately requires TOEFL speaking 26/new 5.0 or IELTS speaking 8. Scores expire after two years and must be electronic. DET and Versant are not accepted. IELTS One Skill Retake language still contains a stale 2024 postponement, so current acceptance needs confirmation. [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] Applicants who have completed a four-year English-medium bachelor’s may request an admission waiver in the English Proficiency section, specifying a backup test method/date. Waivers are decided only when admission is recommended, not beforehand; in-progress UChicago degree treatment is not explicit. The separate TA waiver ordinarily requires a US master’s plus TA experience, final transcript, and supervisor verification. A UChicago bachelor’s alone does not meet that published TA waiver route. [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] International PhD students can receive support, but TA oral-English eligibility and nonresident supplemental tuition coverage must be checked separately. F-1 applicants should not assume federal FAFSA aid eligibility. [s1] [s5] [s7]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 155 international; USD 135 domestic. Nonrefundable and not deferrable. [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Unresolved for Fall 2027. The old 2025-26 department page says GRE scores are not required; the current catalog still lists GRE, particularly the subject test, among admission factors. The current central program-by-program test table was not retrievable. Obtain current written confirmation rather than treating either old statement as controlling. [s5] [s9] [s10]",
    "greMath": "[Conflict] Unresolved for Fall 2027. The old 2025-26 department page says GRE scores are not required; the current catalog still lists GRE, particularly the subject test, among admission factors. The current central program-by-program test table was not retrievable. Obtain current written confirmation rather than treating either old statement as controlling. [s5] [s9] [s10]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required; up to five allowed. Electronic PDF upload or typed/pasted text; qualitative assessment rankings are optional for the writer. No emailed or faxed letters. [s3] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required; recommended length 2-4 concise pages. Faithful paraphrase: describe graduate study/research and career plans, plus preparation and qualifications. Upload in the application; no public font/margin rules found. [s2]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current department versus catalog descriptions of deadline timing differ; old department says GRE not required while catalog includes it as a factor. Central no-post-submission-edit instructions are stricter than the department’s no-post-close-change wording. FERPA correction instructions differ. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s9] [s10]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Read the Mathematics row in the central graduate deadline Google Sheet or its linked accessible PDF, confirm its cycle and time zone, and obtain clarification from mathgradadvising@ucsc.edu or gradadm@ucsc.edu if the row remains unavailable. The central page returned HTTP502 in this audit; indexed text confirms public Sheet/PDF alternatives but did not expose their target URLs. No login, account creation or challenge bypass was attempted. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s11] [qbd1_d1] [qbd1_d4] Evidence history and corrections (earlier statements may be superseded) Entry 1 Field deadline_application Earlier Text Exact Fall 2027 mathematics date could not be established: the current department says the cycle ends in January and delegates precise dates to a central embedded table that could not be retrieved. An older page gives January 2, 2025 at 8:59 p.m. Pacific for the 2025-26 cycle; this is NOT a 2027 deadline. The catalog’s first-half-of-January description also differs from the current department’s end-of-January wording. Confirm directly. Status U Supporting sources: [s1] [s9] [s10] [s11] Reason Superseded by final targeted deadline audit. Entry 2 Field unresolved_actions Earlier Text Urgently confirm Fall 2027 date/timezone, both GRE policies, English waiver before degree conferral, TA certification, exact annual funding and NRST/summer coverage, and offer response deadline. Clarify amendment and FERPA processes before submitting. Status U Supporting sources: [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s11] Reason Superseded by final targeted deadline audit.",
