    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing deadline: December 1 for international applicants (December 15 domestic), 10 p.m. Mountain Standard Time under the university FAQ. Department and central directory agree. No explicit Fall 2027 year appears on the inspected mathematics page; verify the portal's dated deadline. John should plan around December 1, not December 15. [s2] [s3] [s10]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Department publishes only the older AY 2024-25 TA stipend of US$27,369 for a 50% appointment; this is not a 2027 offer. Central AY 2026-27 page prints '$14.001 per semester', an apparent punctuation error that must be confirmed, so no corrected annual total is asserted. Current ≥20% appointments cover mandatory fees, approximately 90% of student health premiums and dental insurance; vision costs extra. Department's older fee-exclusion statement conflicts. Tuition remission applies, with approval needed above 15 credits. [s1] [s7] [s9]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago bachelor's satisfies the accredited US degree route if completed by entry; university minimum undergraduate GPA 2.75. Mathematics expects substantial proof-based algebra and analysis. International applicants are eligible; current F-1 does not turn this into a domestic application. [s1] [s5]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select Mathematics PhD, rather than the separate Applied Mathematics program. Assemble transcripts, CV, personal statement and referees; request the study-based English exemption with official records. No prior faculty agreement is published as a prerequisite. Funding/visa evidence is requested after admission. [s1] [s4] [s5]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Current central mathematics table: TOEFL iBT26 5.0, earlier iBT 100, IELTS 7.5, Duolingo 135, Pearson 75 or Cambridge 190. Scores must remain within two years of admission. Department's older page gives IELTS 7.0, so follow the higher current table pending written confirmation. Verifiable reports can be uploaded/emailed; agency reports may be required if unverifiable. [s1] [s6] [Standing rule] Study exemption requires at least one completed full-time academic year at a US/qualifying-country university, studies ending within two years before intended entry, and official transcript proof. Thus recent UChicago study should qualify if these conditions hold; it is not citizenship-based. Medium-of-instruction letters alone are not accepted. No separate mathematics TA oral-testing exemption verified. [s6] [Standing rule] International students can receive departmental assistantships and nominated fellowships. Department states their tuition waiver can continue without the Colorado-residency requirement imposed on domestic students. Confirm every fellowship's citizenship restrictions individually. [s7] [s27]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] US$80 international application fee (US$60 domestic); F-1 UChicago attendance does not establish the domestic category. Pay before the application deadline. [s5] [s26]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not accepted by Mathematics. [s2]",
