    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] December 1 preceding fall entry is the standing mathematics deadline, hence December 1, 2026 for fall 2027 by interpretation of the recurring rule; the checked page does not explicitly label the 2027 cycle or state a clock/time zone. Fall admission only. Late files may be considered if time and places permit, not a guaranteed extension. [s1]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] A guaranteed mathematics fall-2027 annual stipend was not published. UF HR's October 1, 2024 minimum schedule lists $20,600 for a 9-month 0.50-FTE appointment and $27,467 for a 12-month 0.50-FTE appointment; these are institutional minimums for those appointment terms, not a 2027 mathematics offer. Mathematics describes tuition waiver and assistantship support, but students retain some fees; its approximate $680 per 9-credit semester fee estimate is undated and must be refreshed. GatorGradCare provides qualifying graduate-employee health coverage; exact 2027 deductions and dependent costs require the offer/benefit schedule. [s5] [s6] [s7] [s29]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle after a mathematics bachelor's or equivalent preparation; the catalog ordinarily requires a 3.0 undergraduate GPA for work beyond the first 60 semester/90 quarter credits. Proof-based algebra and analysis preparation is important. International applicants can enter the PhD and receive assistantships. F1 status is not permanent residence; an old departmental instruction asking every noncitizen for a resident-alien number does not fit an F1 applicant, so use the current portal's actual immigration category and ask admissions if that legacy field appears. [s1] [s3] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Prepare the UF/ApplyWeb application, transcripts, required CV and mathematics statement; request all three references before final submission, because UF says references cannot be added or deleted after submission. Send any required official English scores early. Apply for Mathematics PhD and indicate funding interest. Do not enter a resident-alien number if you do not have one. No advance supervisor agreement is published. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "international": "[Conflict] For spring 2027 onward, central international admissions lists TOEFL 4.5 overall with at least 4 in each section on the revised scale; IELTS Academic 6.5 or completion of the UF English Language Institute is also accepted. The graduate catalog still presents the older TOEFL 80 minimum. Do not combine multiple tests using MyBest. Admission exemption and teaching certification are separate. [s3] [s4] [s8] [Standing rule] A completed US degree, or at least one academic year in a US degree program, can meet the published admissions English exemption, subject to departmental discretion; John's UChicago attendance should qualify if documented. A US bachelor's does not by itself waive UF's separate oral-English requirement for a nonexempt international TA. Current TA minimums include TOEFL speaking 4.5, IELTS speaking 7 or SPEAK 45; middle scores require EAP 5836 during the first teaching semester. Summer teaching requires the higher direct-clearance threshold because EAP is unavailable then: TOEFL speaking 6 plus listening 4.5, IELTS speaking 8.5 or SPEAK 55. UF's country exemptions must be checked against actual nationality, which is unspecified here. [s1] [s3] [s8] [Standing rule] International PhD students are eligible for departmental assistantships, subject to employment eligibility and oral-English certification for teaching. The admission English waiver does not settle TA eligibility. Exact nonresident-tuition coverage and any remaining fees should be stated in the offer; do not equate tuition remission with all charges being paid. [s1] [s5] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] $30 nonrefundable application fee. [s1] [s2]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Recommended but optional in the mathematics application; not a published mandatory requirement. Confirm the 2027 portal has not changed the standing policy. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Mathematics Subject GRE is recommended but optional. No published mandatory minimum was found. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three recommendations are required. The department wants at least two from instructors familiar with the applicant's performance in proof-based mathematics courses. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required mathematics statement: describe your mathematical background and possible areas of interest (faithful paraphrase; use the linked page and live prompt for the exact wording). No public mathematics word/page limit, formatting rule or separate 2027 prompt was established. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Resolve three material differences: (1) current central TOEFL 4.5 scale versus catalog's older 80-point minimum; (2) half-time assistantship language versus one-third-time mathematics funding-guide language; (3) legacy blanket resident-alien-number instruction versus an F1 applicant's actual status. Admission English exemption must not be confused with separate international-TA certification. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s8]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Before paying: verify the 2027 deadline clock, live statement/CV limits and conditional fields; send all three requests before final submission; confirm the UChicago admission-English exemption and a separate TA oral-English plan; obtain written stipend, months, appointment fraction, summer/tuition/fees/insurance terms and offer reply date. SPEAK is a possible postarrival route, costs $100 in the checked schedule, and registration closes at least a week beforehand or when full. Recheck all current charges and dates. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s7] [s8]",
