    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] December 15, annual standing deadline for fall PhD entry; the department does not attach an explicit 2027 year, submission hour or timezone. Fall 2027 applications are available centrally. Confirm December 15, 2026 and the portal cutoff rather than treating that inferred date as a published cycle-specific deadline. [s1] [s3] [s47]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] The published August 2026-May 2027 minimum for a 50% nine-month appointment is USD 25,652, with full tuition and partial fee waivers; this is a university floor/current appointment basis, not a confirmed Fall 2027 math offer or 12-month stipend. Summer support and exact health-insurance residual cost are unverified. University Fellowship currently pays USD 33,000 over 12 months (USD 2,750/month), with tuition and specified partial fee/health support. [s13] [s14] [s46]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle for direct bachelor's-to-PhD admission once the UChicago bachelor's is completed before enrollment; F-1 applicants apply as international. MSCS expects a related undergraduate degree, GPA at least 3.0 in the final 60 semester/90 quarter hours and in mathematics beyond calculus. Pure mathematics preparation includes linear algebra, abstract algebra and a year of analysis. These are minimum qualifications, not an admission prediction. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6] [s8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose the Mathematics PhD, arrange three academic referees, upload records and the personal statement, and pay or obtain an authorized fee waiver. International applicants must have all supporting items received by the program deadline. Supervisor consent is not listed as an admission prerequisite. Visa/financial certification is an after-admission step. Ask the department early about University Fellowship nomination and its internal deadline. [s2] [s6] [s7] [s14]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Math PhD catalog: TOEFL new scale overall 5, Reading 4, Listening 4, Speaking 5, Writing 4.5; old scale overall 100, R19/L17/S23/W21. IELTS overall 7 and each component 7; PTE overall 68, R66/L66/S68/W66. MSCS's general page instead gives lower speaking thresholds (TOEFL 4.5 or old 20; PTE 66), creating a conflict: use the PhD-specific threshold pending clarification. Central Duolingo acceptance begins Fall 2027 (130, each 125), but MSCS acceptance is not established. International TAs have additional assessment/orientation. [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6] [Standing rule] A UChicago student with two years of full-time academic study in the United States within the preceding five years can satisfy UIC's admission-test exemption once transcripts are evaluated; degree completion is not stated as necessary for this route. English-medium instruction alone elsewhere is insufficient. This admission exemption does not remove the international-TA spoken-English assessment/orientation. Request confirmation if the portal still lists a test. [s5] [s6] [Standing rule] Department assistantships are open to eligible international students subject to lawful employment and TA language clearance. University Fellowship explicitly has no citizenship restriction. Access Fellowship requires US citizenship/permanent residency or qualifying Illinois RISE eligibility and therefore is not an ordinary F-1 option. PIF may be accessed through University Fellowship nomination; confirm its individual eligibility. [s13] [s14] [s15] [s16] [s46]",
    "costs": "[Conflict] USD 80 application fee, effective Fall 2026. A further USD 100 credential-evaluation fee applies to applicants with postsecondary coursework outside the United States, not simply to all foreign citizens. A UChicago-only academic history should avoid that extra fee; confirm any overseas study/transfer record. The MSCS FAQ's USD 70 fee is outdated. [s5] [s6]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional; MSCS says applicants are not penalized for omitting the GRE. No numerical minimum published. [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional; the same no-penalty policy covers the Mathematics Subject GRE. No score cutoff published. [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three academic letters are required for the Mathematics PhD. The general graduate-school minimum does not reduce the department's requirement. [s2] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] The department requires a document labeled Personal Statement rather than separately listing an SOP. No exact departmental prompt, word/page limit or typography was found on the public instructions. Upload through the application; do not invent a separate SOP requirement. Verify the live program question. [s2] [s4]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Major discrepancies: MSCS FAQ USD 70 versus central USD 80; its implied USD 100 international fee versus actual overseas-coursework criterion; MSCS general English minima versus stricter PhD-catalog speaking thresholds; old versus new TOEFL scales and newly accepted central Duolingo not confirmed by Math. UIC's April 15 page includes older release language. Current UChicago faculty Benjamin Bakker must not be counted as a UIC adviser despite older UIC CVs/pages. [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s17] [s18]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm the Fall 2027 cutoff/timezone and all-letter receipt deadline; exact personal-statement prompt/limit and optional CV/course uploads; reference Save/Send trigger and replacement policy; PhD English threshold/TA clearance and Duolingo acceptance if relevant; actual 2027 stipend, summer/health benefits and guarantee; 2027 fellowship internal deadline; eligibility for an MSCS-paid fee; and each prospective adviser's capacity. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6] [s9] [s13] [s14]",
