    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] December 1, 2026 for Fall 2027: application and all supporting materials, including letters. No public time/time zone or separate grace period verified. Late or incomplete files generally will not be reviewed. No Spring 2027 entry. Ordinary support consideration accompanies the PhD application. [u1]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Math publishes a 2025-26 TA stipend of $24,620 for fall/spring, not a Fall 2027 promise. Central 2026-27 minimum at 50% is $24,200 for nine months ($2,688.89 monthly), or $32,266.68 over twelve months; appointment duration matters. These carry forward rates effective August 16, 2025 while successor contract negotiations continue. Illinois Distinguished Fellowship is indexed at $75,000 total; other official departments describe $25,000 annually for three years, a standing cross-program description rather than a verified 2027 Math award. Tuition waiver is separate; ordinary summer income is not guaranteed. [u6] [u9] [u10] [u14] [u25] [u26]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago bachelor's completed before enrollment is an eligible direct PhD route; F1 status does not exclude admission. Final-year applicants may be conditionally admitted. Central GPA minimum is 3.0/4.0 over the last two undergraduate years; Mathematics typically does not admit below 3.25. Actual record and preparation remain to be assessed. A master's is not required; an MS may be earned en route. [u1] [u7] [u8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select Mathematics PhD and Fall 2027. Prepare transcripts, three mathematics referees, academic statement and central personal short answers; check whether the portal asks for a CV. No advance supervisor sponsorship or research proposal is listed. Start references early; do not wait for letters to submit. Pay the fee before the deadline unless an approved exemption applies. Resolve separate TA speaking certification even if exempt from admission English testing. [u1] [u2] [u3] [u4]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Central admission table: new TOEFL 4 limited / 5 full status; old TOEFL 79 / 103; IELTS 6.5 / 7.5; DET 115 / 135. Math additionally lists old TOEFL 95 total and 22 speaking, or IELTS 6.5 speaking, without a new-scale conversion. Math encourages scores even from exempt applicants. TA certification is separate: new TOEFL speaking 5, old 24, or IELTS speaking 8; institutional oral assessment is an alternative. DET does not establish TA qualification. Math permits temporary nonclassroom TA duties for old speaking 22-23, with full teaching qualification within two years; new-scale equivalent unverified. TOEFL Home Edition/IELTS Online accepted centrally; Essentials, MyBest and IELTS One Skill Retake are not. [u1] [u3] [u8] [u15] [Standing rule] Admission exemption likely applies through at least two years of postsecondary US study within five years of entry, or a US degree received within five years. Thus an on-campus UChicago undergraduate normally qualifies; confirm actual dates and study location. This inference is not individual approval. The exemption does not waive the independent TA speaking requirement. Math's encouragement to submit scores remains despite central exemption. [u1] [u3] [u8] [Standing rule] Ordinary assistantships and associated tuition waivers are available to international students, subject to work authorization and TA English qualification. GAANN opportunities advertised for US applicants do not establish F1 eligibility. Dean's Doctoral Fellowship eligibility was not fully accessible; do not assume F1 eligibility. Financial certification for immigration follows an accepted offer, not the academic application. [u1] [u3] [u6] [u13] [u17]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] $90 nonrefundable application fee, paid electronically before the application is processed/submitted. Budget the current central fee and confirm portal amount. [u2]",
