    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] December 10, 2026, 11:59 p.m. Eastern Standard Time for Fall 2027 MATH and required materials including letters. No separately verified late-letter/document grace. Do not use STAT's different deadline. [s1] [s3]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] MATH FAQ historical 2024 base: $28,311 plus a usual $5,000 in each of the first two years = $33,311, NOT a 2027 amount. FY27 central full doctoral precandidacy minimum: $29,023 over 9.5 months or $36,660 over 12 months (2026-27), not a Fall 2027 departmental guarantee. Do not add the historical supplement to the newer minimum or assume summer coverage. [s2] [s11]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible degree route: UChicago bachelor's before enrollment; F1 does not exclude international admission. MATH expects real analysis, theoretical linear algebra and abstract algebra. FAQ says GPA should exceed 3.0; actual GPA/preparation are unknown, so individual eligibility remains conditional. [s1] [s2] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select MATH, not STAT/AMSC; choose one or two research areas rather than 'undecided' (not binding). Prepare course supplement, transcripts, CV, statements and three referees. Resolve conflicting English-waiver instructions before relying on UChicago. Start a fee-waiver request before paying/submitting. No advance supervisor consent stated. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s9] [s17]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Admission and TA certification differ. New TOEFL speaking 5 / IELTS speaking 7.5 avoids the TA English class; 4.5 / 7 requires class. Writing 5 / IELTS 7 avoids the writing course; reading/listening 5 / IELTS 7 are relevant minima. Central overall TOEFL 5 / IELTS 7. Legacy MATH PTE speaking 76 and central PTE overall 68 measure different things. Confirm the test/date-specific table and department waiver; admission exemption alone does not establish TA eligibility. [s1] [s2] [s9] [Conflict] CONFLICT: the central qualifying-US-degree exemption permits a degree completed or expected by enrollment, with in-country study; online/branch study is excluded and transfer/dual routes need at least two years in an eligible country. A full on-campus UChicago bachelor's appears centrally eligible (inference). The MATH catalog nevertheless requires TOEFL/IELTS even for otherwise exempt applicants; the main page uses no-exceptions language. FAQ describes a US master's waiver but does not resolve bachelor's eligibility. Obtain a written MATH ruling. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s9] [Standing rule] Ordinary TA funding is available to international PhD students; the department supports accepted students except some employer-funded cases. Federal citizenship-restricted awards are separate. A 9.5-month salary and 12-month visa financial requirement may differ; assistantships are not ordinarily performed abroad. [s2] [s11] [s14] [s15]",
    "costs": "[Conflict] Current central fee: $90 per program, online before processing, nonrefundable. MATH's $75 is older/conflicting. Budget $90 and verify the portal. [s1] [s6] [s17]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Current admissions: optional. FAQ strongly encourages scores after the pandemic policy. A legacy educational-policy page still says required; the current optional admissions rule takes precedence, with the conflict preserved. [s1] [s2] [s16]",
    "greMath": "[Conflict] Optional, strongly recommended; FAQ advises submitting scores above 700 and prioritizing Math Subject if taking one. Legacy 'required' wording is stale. This is not a 'not considered' policy. [s1] [s2] [s16]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three; mathematically informed faculty preferred. Ask before assuming extra letters beyond three will be considered. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required. MATH gives no hard limit; a few sentences to a few pages can be suitable. Prompt paraphrase: mathematical preparation, motivation, projects, interests, UMD/faculty fit, goals and optional record anomalies. Central guidance also mentions community contributions. Exact wording linked; no font/spacing rule verified. [s2] [s3] [s4]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Central US-degree English waiver versus MATH test requirement; current $90 versus departmental $75 fee; optional GRE versus legacy required wording; varying Personal Experience required status; changed English-course coverage and course numbers. Seek written rulings where unresolved. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s9] [s13] [s16] [s17] [s22]",
