    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible degree route: accredited US bachelor's completed before entry; university GPA guideline 2.75. Department expects advanced calculus and linear algebra, recommends real analysis, differential equations and abstract algebra. International students are explicitly welcome; no master's prerequisite. [s1] [s3] [s33]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Apply in Slate to Mathematics (Ph.D.); optionally specify mathematical subfields. Arrange required Math GRE, records and referees; assemble the main essay, resume, community essay and suggested course supplement. No prior supervisor agreement is listed. [s1] [s3]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] If not exempt: TOEFL new scale 4/old80, IELTS Academic6.5, DET115 or PTE53; two-year validity through entry. Official agency transmission required. No superscoring/MyBest/IELTS One Skill Retake; no TOEFL Essentials/ITP Plus or IELTS Indicator. Department expects strong spoken English and may require ITA screening for teaching. [s2] [s4] [Standing rule] Published exemption routes include an earned US bachelor's/master's, or current full-time US enrollment with two academic years completed before expected entry. John should qualify through recent UChicago study if these facts hold; confirm waiver processing in Slate. Admission exemption does not establish exemption from teaching screening. [s2] [s4] [Standing rule] International applicants may receive university funding and departmental TA support; no citizenship exclusion appears for ordinary admission funding. TA language screening and appointment eligibility still apply. [s2] [s4] [s6]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] US$90 nonrefundable, paid online when submitting. [s3]",
