    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed · checked 2026-11-09] PhD: December 15, 2026. Master’s: February 1, 2027. The PhD snapshot date must not be used for the master’s route.",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] October 2026 HR update: 50% GSA appointment pays USD 29,192 over two four-month semesters (USD 3,649/month by division). Math summer policy pays prevailing 50% GSI rate; applying unchanged rate for 12 months gives USD 43,788, a DERIVED planning benchmark, not published 2027-28 offer. Negotiations ongoing; salary last rose September 2025. Tuition, GradCare and basic dental covered; exact mandatory-fee coverage must be checked. [s7] [s8] [s9]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s from accredited university before entry; UChicago math degree compatible. Expected preparation roughly U-M math major: calculus, differential equations, algebra/linear algebra, geometry/topology, advanced calculus, three further math courses and two related-field courses. Historical successful GPA around 3.3 is descriptive, not a formal cutoff. [s1]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD (distinct AIM program), collect institutional transcripts and English-medium evidence, CV and two statements; register referees before final submission. Optional Math GRE must be merged as PDF with transcript or personal statement. [s1] [s4] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Math directs nonnative speakers to TOEFL/IELTS and Rackham minima/exemptions. Department still mentions IELTS Indicator; current acceptance should be checked against central testing page before booking. Scores official and no older than two years by deadline. [s1] [s5] [Standing rule] Exempt if ALL undergraduate education was at an English-only institution and degree completed before U-M classes. UChicago fits if no non-English transfer education. Self-assess in application; upload transcript front/back and registrar English-medium letter if language not recorded. Admission review verifies exemption. [s5] [Standing rule] PhD support applies to admitted international students; handbook provides international hiring/I-9 procedures. MLB funded master’s bridge restricted to US citizens/permanent residents, so not this F-1 applicant’s fallback. External citizenship rules require separate review. [s7] [s1]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD90 non-US citizen; nonrefundable, due upon submission. UChicago student does not receive current-Rackham USD10 rate. [s6]",
