    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Department requires a completed fall application by February 15; no year/time zone specified. Amigo scholarship best consideration also requires all materials by February 15. No separate reference grace period is published. [s1] [s2] [s9]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Department stipend page is explicitly 2014-15 (USD 8,646/semester, 12 tuition credits and insurance), so it is obsolete. Central 2026-27 minimum for 50% pre-master’s TA is USD 9,953.18 per 18-week term; two terms total USD 19,906.36 by arithmetic. Post-master’s minimum is USD 10,949.27/term. These are university minimums, not a confirmed math offer or 2027-28 rate. [s7] [s8]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] International applicants, including noncitizens already on a U.S. visa, apply through Global Education Office plus departmental review. The department describes a bachelor’s-to-PhD route, so a completed UChicago mathematics bachelor’s is appropriate in principle; exact individual GPA/preparation approval remains unverified. [s2] [s18]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select Arts & Sciences > Mathematics & Statistics > Mathematics, prepare letter of intent and three referees, and indicate assistantship interest in the letter. International review must be completed before departmental selection. After admission, accept and provide financial/official academic records for immigration documentation. [s1] [s2] [s4]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Graduate minima: TOEFL 79/revised 4.5, IELTS 6.5, Duolingo 105, PTE 53, TOEFL Essentials C1, Cambridge C2 or PTE Express 85. TOEFL code 4845. Medium-of-instruction certificates are expressly not accepted as a test substitute. TA applicants may face additional departmental requirements. [s3] [s10] [Standing rule] A bachelor’s from a regionally accredited U.S. institution exempts the test, so a completed UChicago degree qualifies. In-progress degree timing is not explicit. Another exception is two qualifying U.S. freshman-composition semesters with C or higher, graded A-F; UChicago humanities equivalence is not established. [s3] [Standing rule] International students may receive assistantships. Central rules: appointments lasting over half a semester provide health insurance; at least 10 hours/week over half a semester qualifies for resident tuition. Some appointments additionally cover tuition/fees; exact benefits are offer-dependent. [s9]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] International graduate application USD 70; domestic USD 60. [s5]",
