    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] January 7, published annual fall-entry deadline; the public page does not explicitly identify January 2027 or a time zone. Submit a complete file by this date; no separate reference or funding grace period was verified. [s2] [s4]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] University science doctoral standard for 2026-27: USD 40,590 for twelve months; select fellows up to USD 50,000. This is a current university benchmark, not a confirmed Fall 2027 Math award. Math admits receive living support and tuition. Tuition scholarships cover fees except a small activity fee; eligible fully funded students' standard 2026-27 health premium subsidy covers the premium. [s1] [s8]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible to apply while completing a mathematics bachelor's or equivalent; central minimum GPA 3.0. Successful preparation usually includes two semesters of abstract algebra (or one plus applied algebra), proof-based analysis including complex analysis, and several further proof courses. Fall PhD admission only; no standalone master's. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Prepare online application, transcripts, CV, statement and three referees. Upload proof of at least two academic years of English-medium study and email gradapp@nd.edu to confirm the language exemption. Request a fee waiver with evidence if needed before paying. [s2] [s3] [s7]",
    "international": "[Conflict] If not exempt: TOEFL 80 with speaking 23 on the old scale; current FAQ gives 4.5 overall and 4.0 each section on the new scale; IELTS 7.0 or Duolingo 120. Scores valid two years. Math can review lower speaking scores using additional evidence/interview. Current Math/FAQ accept Duolingo although an older requirements page omits it. [s2] [s3] [s5] [Standing rule] At least two academic years of study at an English-medium institution qualifies; a completed or expected UChicago undergraduate education should meet the Math rule. Upload transcript or medium-of-instruction certification in Test Scores instead of scores, then email gradapp@nd.edu for confirmation. [s2] [s3] [Standing rule] Math support is offered to admitted students, including international applicants; select fellowships state all admitted full-time students are considered, while individual award eligibility differs. [s1] [s9]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 75 per application, preferably credit card; check payable to University of Notre Dame can be sent to Graduate Recruitment and Admissions, 115 Main Building, Notre Dame IN 46556. [s7]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional; unofficial results can be reviewed, valid five years. No minimum. Optional is not a promise that submitted scores are ignored. [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional; strong scores may help, especially when the committee knows less about the applicant's undergraduate institution. No minimum. Math reports limited weight historically. [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required; central system permits up to five. [s2] [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required statement of intent. General guidance: 1-3 double-spaced pages; name and prospective program on every page. Paraphrased prompt: explain intellectual development, research interests, reasons for the degree and program/faculty fit, future plans, strengths, and unusual circumstances without excuses. Upload through application. [s2] [s6]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] FAQ allows postsubmission amendments but general application page says submitted materials cannot be changed; use graduate admissions for replacements. Current Math/FAQ include Duolingo and newer TOEFL scale; older general page has stale English-test information. [s2] [s3] [s5]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm January 2027 date/time, actual referee cutoff, offer response deadline, new funding amount and detailed fellowship follow-up. Inspect portal for any additional personal/research/writing/publication fields, whose absence on public pages does not prove prohibition. Ask Dyer for current publications if pursuing that fit. [s2] [s3] [s4]",
