    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] January 15, 2027 for full Fall 2027 consideration; later applications may be considered through April or until places fill. A timely MathJobs fee-waiver application counts as meeting this deadline, followed by a department-assigned official application window. The normal portal timezone is not published. [s1] [s3]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] Entering base stipend is advertised as USD 23,000, with full tuition and medical insurance; student fees remain the student’s responsibility. The public page does not clearly identify the stipend’s month basis. Summer opportunities are separately described as USD 3,500-4,500 and are not guaranteed. [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A bachelor’s degree must be completed before enrollment; applicants may apply with up to three semesters remaining. Mathematics usually expects GPA 3.0 but states no hard departmental minimum. Bachelor’s applicants with doctoral intent should choose the MA route; PhD entry is for applicants already holding a mathematics master’s. The terminal MS is a separate route. [s1] [s5]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select MA if entering from UChicago with doctoral intent. No advance adviser agreement is required. Applicants seeking a fee waiver first submit a separate MathJobs mini-application and wait for the department’s decision before completing the official graduate application within the subsequently assigned window. [s1] [s3]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Current central minimums: old TOEFL 79 with each section 20, new TOEFL 4.5 with each section 4; IELTS 6.5 with each section 6; PTE 60 with each section 55; DET 130 with each section 115 under its pilot. Scores must be under two years old at enrollment. No MyBest or IELTS One Skill Retake. Departmental older IELTS 6 language should not override the newer central 6.5 rule. [s1] [s6] [Standing rule] Completion of 24 credit hours at an accredited US institution, or an earned US bachelor’s degree, can establish admission English proficiency. UChicago coursework therefore provides an apparent route before graduation; confirm how quarter credits are evaluated. Teaching certification is separate: a US bachelor’s alone does not meet the listed bachelor’s-plus-master’s exemption pathway. [s6] [s7] [Standing rule] Successful MA/PhD-track applicants are offered teaching support; international terminal-MS students are not offered departmental assistantships. Admission-level English proficiency does not substitute for teaching certification. [s1] [s6]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 100 for international applicants; USD 50 for US citizens/permanent residents. [s5] [s6]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Not required for the current application; the department encourages available GRE evidence and the MathJobs waiver permits optional scores. No mandatory score threshold is established. [s1] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Not required for the current application; the department encourages available GRE evidence and the MathJobs waiver permits optional scores. No mandatory score threshold is established. [s1] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three letters from people familiar with mathematical work. The department’s advice asks writers to assess preparation, research potential, motivation, comparative strength, maturity, and teaching-related experience. [s3] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required statement of interest. A brief section explaining COVID-related academic effects is optional. No public word/page limit or detailed current prompt was found. Upload to the relevant application. [s1] [s3]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Stale reference advice says January 12 versus current January 15. Departmental older IELTS 6 conflicts with central 6.5. Central no-waiver language has a specific mathematics MathJobs exception. Funding headings do not transparently reconcile all possible supplements. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Retrieve the fee-waiver cover sheet and exact statement prompt; confirm quarter-credit English exemption and TA certification; reference invitation/receipt/reuse in both portals; stipend month basis, 2027-28 rate, and exact offer response deadline. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s6] [s7]",
