    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] Authoritative explicit Fall 2027 deadline: 8 December 2026, 11:59 p.m. Eastern/EST, agreed by central SAS calendar and math FAQ. However, How to Apply retains a parenthetical saying submit by December 7, and program description retains December 15 in an older paragraph. Clarify with graduate@math.upenn.edu; prudent planning target is December 7, not a newly asserted official deadline. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Math explicitly lists USD 49,000 for a 12-month 2026-27 fellowship plus tuition, fees and health insurance. Older FAQ’s USD 43,050 is labeled 2025-26. Ratified CBA Article 5 raises the covered-worker annual minimum by 3% on 1 July 2027: calculated USD 50,470 (also stated in union summary). However, educational fellows without teaching/research services are excluded from the bargaining unit; therefore USD 50,470 is a covered-worker minimum, not yet a verified first-year math fellowship offer for 2027-28. [s3] [s2] [s8] [s9]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Bachelor’s degree by enrollment, no master’s required; strong proof-based advanced calculus, abstract/linear algebra and advanced electives expected. Department says mathematics grades should mostly be A/A−. UChicago math bachelor meets degree-route eligibility if completed before entry; F-1 does not itself disqualify. This is not an admissions-likelihood assessment. [s2] [s3]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Apply through SAS Slate to Mathematics PhD (AMCS is separate). Gather CV, academic/personal statement, unofficial transcripts and 3-5 referees; investigate English waiver and fee waiver early. Only one program application within the same Penn school is allowed. No prearranged supervisor required. [s1] [s4]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL or IELTS unless exempt. Department looks for TOEFL total at least 100 and speaking at least 20 on the older scale; IELTS minimum 7. Current public page does not translate these numbers to the 2026 TOEFL scale. English scores valid two years. Non-native PhDs must establish spoken-English teaching proficiency before second year; department mentions TOEFL speaking 27 or its internal test. [s2] [s5] [Standing rule] Entire four-year undergraduate study in the US qualifies under the math rule; confirm if transfer/study history differs. Central SAS asks applicants to contact their program about waiver activation, generally after uploading unofficial transcript. Admission exemption does not automatically waive later teaching-language certification; summer International TA preparation may require early arrival and carries additional stipend. [s3] [s4] [s2] [Standing rule] Department’s PhD support promise is not citizenship-limited: inference that admitted F-1 students qualify. CBA also expressly provides international-worker protections/funding. Specific outside awards or Bridge fellowship may have separate nationality restrictions, presently unverified. [s3] [s9] [s10]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 90; credit/debit card at submission, international instructions specify major credit card. Central FAQ also mentions a nonrefundable enrollment fee after accepting, but does not establish a Mathematics amount or whether exempted for funded PhDs. [s2] [s4] [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not required; How to Apply broadly welcomes GRE scores if available. No explicit not-considered prohibition. Confirm current portal if submitting General GRE, because FAQ specifically discusses Mathematics only. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional, accepted and used as an information point in review. Earlier-year valid scores permitted; GRE validity five years. ETS institution 2926, mathematics department 0703. [s2] [s5]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] At least three, at most five. Prefer mathematics professors who can assess proof-based coursework, projects, research ability and mathematical engagement. Names of at least three must be entered before submission. [s1] [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required statement, called Personal Statement in math instructions and Statement of Purpose centrally. Prompt paraphrase: explain how background and academic experience led to graduate study and Penn; research interests, intellectual goals, educational trajectory, curiosity and ambitions. Math additionally recommends concrete mathematical problems/theories, how interest developed, new work/results and future vision, and Penn faculty of interest. Length, spacing, font, file type and upload/link specification beyond an application statement are not publicly fixed; do not copy another department’s two-page rule. [s1] [s4]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Use central/FAQ December 8, 2026 23:59 EST, while flagging older December 7 parenthetical and December 15 program text. Reference grace cutoff remains unclear. GRE broad optional wording and Math-specific optional FAQ agree. 2026-27 math funding supersedes older 2025-26 amount; CBA 2027 worker minimum does not automatically cover teaching-free first-year fellows. Bridge master’s is closed despite old application instructions remaining online. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s9] [s10]",
