    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Department states December 15, a hard deadline for all application materials, with no materials accepted afterward. Public departmental page does not label Fall 2027. Liaison submission/payment cutoff is 11:59 p.m. Pacific. No separate Math funding or referee grace deadline established; complete by the department deadline. [s1] [s7]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] The university's AY 2026-27 minimum total doctoral stipend is $42,436, plus tuition remission and specified health support. This is a prior-year university floor, not a published Fall 2027 Math offer; the memo does not justify converting it into a particular monthly or summer schedule. Math promises tuition, health and dental benefits with its package. [s8] [s1]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Direct PhD admission with a bachelor's is permitted; about two-thirds of admits have bachelor's degrees. GPA below 3.0 is not considered (page also says above 3.0). Require two terms each of advanced analysis and advanced algebra; for quarter institutions three terms are encouraged. Courses may be in progress. International applicants are eligible. [s1]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD in USC's Liaison application. Mathematics and Applied Mathematics are reviewed together; applying to both has no advantage. Arrange official-issued transcripts and three academic referees early. Request any fee waiver before submission. Establish English exemption or submit official scores. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Math lists TOEFL 100, IELTS 7 or PTE 68. Central policy for Spring 2027 onward accepts TOEFL, IELTS, PTE and Cambridge C1 Advanced; scores valid two years at submission. Its PhD ISE-exemption thresholds are old TOEFL 100/20 each, new TOEFL 5/4 each, IELTS 7/6 each, PTE 68/53 each, Cambridge 185/169 each; distinguish placement thresholds from departmental admission rules. Official scores required; ETS 4852. Confirm the Math policy for the new TOEFL scale/Cambridge. [s1] [s3] [Standing rule] Central graduate policy exempts a holder of a US bachelor's degree, including permitted transferred credits. Completed UChicago degree fits. A still-pending bachelor's is not explicitly covered by 'hold': obtain confirmation. A bachelor's exemption does not itself exempt the separate ITA interview. ITA test may be waived for TOEFL speaking/listening 6/5.5 (old 29/25) or IELTS 8.5/7, but the department may still require it. [s3] [s10] [Standing rule] The departmental package applies to admitted students regardless of nationality. International teaching assignments require separate English clearance. [s1] [s10]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] $120 for most graduate programs in the Fall 2027 application guide; the older Fall 2026 fee was $105. Pay electronically using accepted cards. [s2]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not considered. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional and considered; especially encouraged for applicants from less familiar institutions or nontraditional preparation. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three required. Ideally all are higher-education mathematics faculty who taught the applicant for at least a semester within the last three years; at least one should have supervised mathematical research. The page excludes unsuitable sources such as high-school teachers, TAs, coaches and coworkers; nontraditional paths should meet the spirit of these criteria. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Statement of purpose required. Exact Math PhD prompt, length and formatting are not published on the accessible departmental page; inspect Program Materials. Do not import the 750-word Mathematical Finance master's requirement. [s1] [s6]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Departmental English page retains old TOEFL scale and omits Cambridge; central policy is newer. Central general PhD priority dates are not substituted for Math's December 15 hard cutoff. Transcript pages emphasize different upload/direct-delivery steps. Department geometry roster does not prominently flag Siegel's leave; personal page does. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s21]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm expected-degree English exemption, updated Math TOEFL threshold, precise 2027 deadline and time, exact SOP/CV portal limits, all optional upload slots, final annual stipend/summer coverage, commitment date, and completed-letter reuse. Request adviser availability, especially Siegel. [s1] [s3] [s6]",
