    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Central doctoral fall priority is February 1, but the mathematics funding priority is January 1 and should govern a funded application. Central catalog guidance prefers international credentials 120 days before enrollment; it is not a substitute for the earlier mathematics priority. A final Fall 2027 mathematics closing date was not established. [s1] [s3] [s4]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] The live mathematics GTA page advertises $25,666.56 over twelve months ($2,138.88 monthly), 100% tuition benefit and year-round student health coverage. A student opting out of summer work keeps health coverage but receives no summer stipend. The page is undated and is not a guaranteed Fall 2027 offer. [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] The General Mathematics BS-entry PhD explicitly accepts a mathematics or closely related bachelor’s degree. The catalog lists a 3.0 undergraduate GPA and permits holistic exceptions to GPA/test thresholds. An international UChicago mathematics graduate is academically eligible to apply, subject to those standards. [s1] [s3] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select the BS-entry General Mathematics PhD in ApplyUTA, arrange three letters, prepare all college records and any requested academic/research statement, and resolve tests or waivers. Ask the department for any fee-waiver code before submission. F-1 transfer eligibility and financial certification are needed for the later I-20 process. [s1] [s4] [s5] [s9]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Without an exemption: TOEFL new-scale overall 4, with published section targets writing 4.5 and speaking/reading/listening 4; former TOEFL overall 79 with writing 22, speaking 21, reading 20 and listening 16; IELTS 6.5 or Duolingo 100. Send official scores to ETS code 6013 where applicable. [s4] [Standing rule] Holding a bachelor’s or master’s from an accredited US institution exempts admission English testing. The catalog also exempts a US bachelor’s degree from the separate international teaching-assistant English demonstration requirement. Whether the admission waiver can be processed while the UChicago degree is still pending is not established. Otherwise GTA certification can require speaking assessment/training; Duolingo admission acceptance does not itself establish GTA certification. [s3] [s4] [Standing rule] International students can receive the same graduate tuition benefit as eligible domestic appointees. The international-services fee is not covered. The department gives funding preference to unconditionally admitted PhD-bound students; not every eligible admitted student is funded. [s1] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] The international graduate application fee is $90 and nonrefundable. Non-US transcript review, if applicable, carries an additional $90 FCSA fee. [s3] [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] The current 2026-27 BS-entry catalog lists General GRE thresholds of verbal 143 and quantitative 155 for unconditional admission, while allowing a holistic exception when GPA and/or GRE criteria are unmet. No blanket mathematics GRE waiver was found; treat it as required unless the department approves otherwise. [s6]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No Mathematics Subject GRE requirement or preference was established. The catalog’s numerical GRE thresholds concern the General test and must not be misread as a subject-test requirement. [s6]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] At least three letters from people familiar with academic and/or professional work. Enter referee contact details in the application; letters are submitted through an emailed link. [s1] [s6]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] The BS-entry catalog identifies a statement of professional or research interests as evidence in holistic review, especially when GPA/GRE criteria are not met. The public checklist does not establish a mandatory exact prompt, word/page limit or format for every applicant. Confirm the current portal’s statement field before drafting. [s1] [s6]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] The live department gives January 1 funding priority, earlier than central February 1. Current central admissions allows unofficial review transcripts while catalog wording requests official records. The current departmental fee-waiver-code route differs from the undergraduate form’s exclusion of graduate applicants. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s9]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm Fall 2027 GRE waiver availability, exact statement/CV requirements, referee invitation and replacement mechanics, current GTA package/renewal, final application and acceptance dates, and the pending-US-degree English waiver. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s6]",
