    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] December 15 for Fall 2027 on the current math admissions page (i.e., 15 December 2026 by cycle context); exact cutoff time/time zone not published in reviewed math instructions. Catalog says posted deadline is receipt deadline for all documents and scores. Late materials are not guaranteed full consideration; no separate guaranteed referee/score grace date. [s1] [s7]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] 2027-28 math offer amount not verified. 2026-27 CNS TierIII (all CNS PhDs) TA scale: USD3,059.50/month, USD13,767.75 per long semester; two semesters total USD27,535.50 (calculated9months). Listed three-month summer rate USD9,178.50 applies when appointed, not a universal summer guarantee. First-year summer fellowship usually offered; amount not stated. Twenty-hour TA tuition benefit covers9resident credits/long semester; resident-rate entitlement requires qualifying appointment. Eligible AcademicBlue employees receive100% own premium support (dependent50%); verify fees and first-year fellowship insurance separately. [s6] [s10] [s11] [s13]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Accredited US bachelor’s degree or equivalent, adequate mathematical preparation and normally GPA at least 3.0 in upper-division and any graduate work. Below-minimum applicants may apply with an explanatory letter. UChicago math bachelor is an eligible degree route if completed in time; GPA/history remain unverified. Only fall PhD admission; mathematics master’s is actuarial only. [s4] [s1]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Apply early enough for multi-step processing: initial form takes 2-3 business days to load; then pay fee and complete MyStatus documents. Transcript verification takes another 2-3 business days. Use assigned UT EID, never create a duplicate. Choose primary interest ANG for algebra/number theory/geometry, optional secondary and up to three specific areas; choices guide reviewers but do not bind your eventual specialty. [s2] [s1]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Central accepts TOEFL, IELTS Academic or DET; minimum TOEFL79/120 or4/6, IELTS6.5, DET115. Math gives stronger guidance: IELTS7.5 or DET135 (145 preferred). Its TOEFL numbers 21.5 and23 are not clearly identified by scale and are inconsistent with ordinary total-score presentation; clarify rather than treating these as usable thresholds. Official scores required before an offer; ITP and IELTS General Training not accepted. [s1] [s3] [Standing rule] Central rule exempts applicants possessing a bachelor’s degree from a US institution. A completed UChicago degree qualifies. Wording does not expressly resolve an expected degree still in progress at application time; ask giatest@austin.utexas.edu if not yet conferred. A US master’s alone is insufficient. Teaching assistant English certification is separate. [s3] [s6] [s15] [Standing rule] International students explicitly eligible for individual-faculty NSF grant GRA support and ordinary admitted-student support. NSF RTG support and NSF GRFP are citizenship/permanent-residence limited; do not equate these with ordinary GRA eligibility. [s5]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] International graduate application USD90 nonrefundable; domestic USD65 does not apply solely because studying at UChicago. Pay via MyStatus after initial application processing, credit card/electronic check. [s2]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Requirement waived effective Fall 2027 by August 2026 update. No explicit not-considered rule found; optional acceptance of General scores should be checked in portal. Older prose comparing General and Math weights is not a current requirement. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Optional but highly recommended; no score cutoff, used as one holistic information point rather than a research measure. ETS code6882; valid five years. [s1] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three, through UT’s online recommendation system. Public Mathematics page does not establish a higher maximum or exact referee-question text. [s1]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required narrative, typically2-3pages (guidance, not stated hard maximum), uploaded through MyStatus. Prompt paraphrase: mathematical/research experience, interests and UT faculty fit, leadership/teaching/community impact, career aims, personality/life experience and special circumstances. No spacing/font/margin/file-format rule established publicly. [s1]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Math TOEFL21.5/23 wording conflicts with standard scales and central79/120 or4/6; seek clarification if testing required. Central US-bachelor waiver says possesses a degree, leaving expected-degree timing unclear. Current General GRE waiver supersedes older comparative-GRE prose. Central2-3business-day setup may exceed math24-48hours. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm expected-UChicago-degree English waiver timing, TOEFL scale if needed, deadline time zone, 2027-28 stipend/fee coverage and summer guarantee, response deadline, referee exact trigger/update/reuse, portal file limits and any course supplement. Confirm Damiolini leave/return and Allcock emeritus supervision. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s5]",
