    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] January 1 annually for full consideration; 2027 year and time zone not explicitly stated. Late applications: FAQ says March 15, program page April 1, only if places remain. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] All admitted PhD applicants are offered a TA: approximately USD 27,000 per academic year plus tuition waiver and health insurance, according to the undated FAQ. Summer support is decided annually and is not guaranteed. Fall 2027 amount and residual fees require the offer. [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A bachelor's degree must appear on the transcript before graduate study begins; a master's is unnecessary. UChicago bachelor's route is eligible in principle; admission depends on preparation and central academic requirements. F-1 status is not a departmental exclusion. [s2] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics PhD and fall term; identify pure/applied preference, up to three areas, and possible supervisors. Those choices are nonbinding. Arrange three academic referees and verify any English exemption before paying the application fee. [s3]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Central tests: TOEFL iBT 80 on the old scale or 4.5 on the new scale, IELTS 6.5, or DET 110; scores generally within two years of application-fee payment. Teaching English assessment is separate; departmental materials discuss stronger spoken/listening performance. [s5] [s1] [Unresolved] Central exemption covers a completed US bachelor's or higher degree within two years of paying the application fee. Whether an unfinished UChicago degree qualifies at application is not established; obtain confirmation before relying on exemption. Mathematics cannot independently waive the central rule. [s5] [s2] [Standing rule] Ordinary PhD TA support is available within the all-admitted-students policy; NSF RTG funding expressly excludes F-1-only applicants because it requires US citizenship/permanent residence. [s2] [s3]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 65 international graduate application fee; USD 55 domestic. Central rules apply. [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional and considered if submitted; omission does not hurt. Unofficial scores accepted in application. [s2] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Optional and considered, especially relevant to pure mathematics; omission does not hurt. Unofficial scores accepted; ETS institution 4853. [s2] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three letters; strongest sources are advanced mathematics instructors and research mentors. Referees may explain unusual circumstances. [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required upload. Faithful paraphrase: current mathematical interests, preparation/research, educational and career aims, and why Utah fits; potential group/faculty, teaching, relevant difficulties and student activities may help. No explicit word/page limit or typography rule. [s3] [s2]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Late deadline differs (March 15 FAQ versus April 1 program page). F-1/J-1 waiver exception conflicts with blanket international exclusion in the same text. Older research listings can be stale: Harold Blum is now Georgia Tech; Yuan-Pin Lee's current university appointment is adjunct. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s8] [s15]",
