    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] 1 January 2027 for application, letters, official test scores and supporting materials; timezone/cutoff time not published. Main page explicitly labels Fall 2027 changes and defines January 1 as entry year. Older FAQ Dec 15 application wording is superseded; do not assume additional grace after January 1. [s1] [s2] [s6]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] Official FY 2026-27 Math rate sheet, 50% appointment: TA academic-year gross USD 30,614; PA/RA academic-year 31,306; PA/RA annual 37,417. University forecast explicitly sets 2027-28 annualized 50% minimum 39,288, not a math 12-month offer. Its A-to-C conversion is 9/11; arithmetic academic minimum≈32,144.73, pending official 2027 rate confirmation. Summer cash guarantee not established. Tuition remission excludes segregated fees, international student fee, and one-time official document fee (current 130). Health coverage available with employee premiums; not full premium-free guarantee. [s10] [s11] [s9] [s1] [s15]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle after completing a UChicago bachelor’s before entry; central GPA minimum 3.00 over last 60 semester hours (about 2 years), with program consideration below minimum possible. Math preparation normally analysis I/II, algebra I/II, linear algebra and 4 advanced electives; graduate exposure common, not an absolute requirement. No master’s needed. Actual GPA/course equivalence must be checked. International/F-1 applicants are eligible. [s5] [s6] [s2] [s4] [s12]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select Mathematics PhD/Fall 2027; arrange required Math GRE and official reporting; assemble transcripts, 20-course dossier, CV, two-page SOP and roughly 200-word background answer; request ≥3 faculty letters early with Send to Recommender. For department fee grant, complete but do not submit application, stop at Funding and Program Participation, email grad_program@math.wisc.edu by standing Dec 1 deadline. No supervisor agreement required. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] If not exempt: official TOEFL≥92 before 21 January 2026 or≥5.0 thereafter; IELTS/Indicator≥7; DET≥125; scores under 2 years at enrollment. No combined/MyBest or IELTS One Skill Retake; TOEFL Home accepted. Program-approved lower ranges TOEFL 80-91/4.5, IELTS 6.5, DET 115-124 require arrival ESLAT and assigned ESL courses. TA spoken-English qualification is separate. [s5] [s4] [s16] [Conflict] Completed accredited US bachelor’s satisfies admission English requirement; alternatively≥2 full-time semesters of graded exclusively English coursework within 5 years qualifies while degree is in progress (verify quarter equivalence). No extra waiver essay published. TA policy exempts US bachelor’s recipients, but departments may test those attending degree institution less than 4 full years. Math main page broadly says non-native incoming students take SPEAK; request written confirmation of UChicago exception. [s5] [s17] [s16] [s1] [Standing rule] International students eligible for assistantships, University Fellowships and some departmental fellowships. All-admit math support statement has no nationality exclusion. F-1 work authorization/SEVIS transfer is separate and should be handled with ISS after admission. [s12] [s1]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 75 nonrefundable application fee plus USD 6 international processing=USD 81. One fee covers up to 3 programs in same entry term; separate applications and new referee uploads needed. MasterCard/Visa/debit accepted. [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Optional according to mathematics checklist; not required in Graduate Guide. This is distinct from mandatory mathematics subject exam. [s1] [s6]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] REQUIRED for Fall 2027, official ETS report code 1846 by 1 January 2027. FAQ says GRE must be within 5 years of matriculation in August. Department warns delivery may take 4 weeks; central matching takes 2-3 weeks after submission, so arrange earlier than deadline. No published minimum score. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] At least 3 letters addressing mathematical promise, from mathematics faculty or other faculty able to judge readiness for graduate mathematics. FAQ allows more than 3. Referees upload PDF directly through secure system; Interfolio/file services not accepted. [s1] [s2] [s6] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required PDF, maximum 2 pages. Faithful prompt paraphrase: why study mathematics at UW; research interests, career goals, and preparation, including coursework, work, research, publications, presentations, awards, honors. No font/margin/spacing rule published. Central guidance encourages specific program/faculty fit and brief explanation of anomalies. [s6] [s1] [s8]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Main Fall 2027 notice/Graduate Guide January 1 supersede older FAQ Dec 15 application wording. Math blanket SPEAK language must be reconciled with L&S US bachelor exemption (especially 4-year attendance). Math fee grant procedure remains posted while new program grant purchases suspended centrally. Old personal faculty ranks/lists can lag current roster; Marshall/Erman/Shankar moved. [s1] [s2] [s6] [s7] [s16] [s17] [f0] [fm1] [fm2] [fm3]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm January 1 cutoff timezone; fee grant code availability and USD 6 coverage; TA UChicago degree exemption and required arrival training; 2027 salary, summer months, fees and health premiums; submitted letter replacement/reuse rules; optional paper links/upload permission; faculty capacity. Verify degree conferral/GPA/course equivalence. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s7] [s9] [s11] [s17]",
