    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] January 1 for full fall admission and GTA/GRA consideration; standing rule with no year or time zone. Later applications are accepted with no funding guarantee. Central international outer application date is April 1 and acceptance must occur by May 15, but these do not replace January 1. [s1] [s23]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Mathematics pays a nine-month GTA stipend plus tuition waiver but does not publish its exact step. University 2026-27 ordinary full-time Step 1 minimum is $2,909/month, $26,181 for nine months; this is a floor, not a math offer. Rates include a $665 monthly academic-year supplement intended to offset comprehensive fees. Step 0 requires supplemental fellowship bringing total above Step 1. Fall 2027 amount remains unverified. [s2] [s9]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Graduate admission normally requires GPA 3.0, with holistic exceptions. UChicago bachelor’s preparation is eligible for graduate study, and F-1 applicants can enroll at Blacksburg. Mathematics describes an MS-to-PhD progression; ask whether your bachelor’s applicant should select PhD or MS en route, because initial degree-selection instructions were not explicit. [s2] [s3] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] The department strongly encourages identifying and contacting potential research advisers before applying and naming interests/faculty in the personal statement. It describes beginning an adviser relationship as important for competitiveness, but does not publish a signed supervisor-approval prerequisite. Prepare three letters, transcript uploads and any English waiver documentation; request fee waiver before submitting. [s1] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Current testing page: TOEFL new scale 4.5 overall and each subsection 4.5; earlier iBT 90 overall, each 20; IELTS 6.5. GTA speaking expectation is new TOEFL 5; 4.5 requires unit justification and below 4.5 Graduate School justification. Teaching requirements are separate from admission. [s4] [Standing rule] An awarded degree from an accredited institution with English instruction may waive admission testing after transcript/degree-conferral and language review. UChicago should meet the institution/language condition, but the public rule specifies an awarded degree; waiver while your degree is pending is not established. Confirm separately whether teaching-language assessment remains. [s4] [Standing rule] The program welcomes international students and describes funding for all admitted graduate students; assistantship employment eligibility and English teaching assessment apply. This supports international assistantship consideration, not eligibility for every named fellowship. [s2] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] US $75 nonrefundable. [s3] [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Neither General nor Mathematics GRE is required. Department explicitly promises equal consideration to applications without scores; it does not say scores are forbidden. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Neither General nor Mathematics GRE is required. Department explicitly promises equal consideration to applications without scores; it does not say scores are forbidden. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three letters, preferably upper-level mathematics instructors or research mentors; writers should address mathematical synthesis and graduate research potential. Electronic email contacts or paper letters directly to the department are supported. [s1] [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Personal statement is expected. Faithful paraphrase of mathematics supplement: discuss research areas you might explore and faculty who could mentor you, if identified. No separate research statement is established. Public mathematics instructions do not give exact full portal prompt, page/word limit, formatting or upload/link specification. [s1]",
