    "international": "[Standing rule] TOEFL iBT or IELTS Academic unless exempt; no GSAS admission minimum. Teaching/summer-English threshold: TOEFL speaking 26 old scale or 5.5 for tests from January 21, 2026; IELTS speaking 8.0. IELTS Online/One Skill Retake, TOEFL Essentials and MyBest are not accepted. [s7] [s8] [Standing rule] Completed or forthcoming UChicago English-medium undergraduate degree qualifies provided at least THREE years in residence. Answer language/institution questions in application; no separate documentation. Transfer/shortened-residency history therefore matters. Voluntarily reporting English scores makes official verification mandatory and low speaking scores can trigger summer English even if otherwise exempt. [s3] [s8] [Standing rule] University funding statement applies to all PhD students, with no citizenship exclusion; international students are eligible for departmental support. External citizenship-restricted awards and loans must be checked independently. [s10] [s7]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] USD 105 nonrefundable, due upon submission unless waiver granted. Visa/Mastercard/Discover/AmEx accepted; debit cards, debit authorizations and wire transfers not accepted. [s9]",
