    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Fall 2027: opens October 15, 2026; closes January 11, 2027. All materials must be complete then; no late applications. No closing hour/time zone is stated. Central mathematics FAQ confirms Fall 2027, correcting the department page’s inconsistent Fall 2026 label. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] Standing math guarantee: CAD 25,000/year MSc; CAD 30,000/year PhD, gross across fall-summer, plus a first-term SGES of CAD 2,500-10,000. Individual offer specifies composition. Tuition is not waived: central 2026-27 full-time rate CAD 2,192.57/term (three-term arithmetic CAD 6,577.71/year) plus other fees; this is not 2027-28 pricing. International and domestic math students pay the same tuition. [s1] [s5] [s6] [s7]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Conflict] A completed UChicago bachelor’s permits MSc consideration, subject to minimum CGPA 3.0 or equivalent. Mathematics specifies a completed master’s and CGPA 3.5 for PhD; exceptional transfer from an SFU MSc is possible. Central regulations allow some bachelor’s-to-PhD admission at higher GPAs, but math’s narrower rule controls unless the department confirms an exception. International applicants are eligible; F-1 is not Canadian study authorization. [s1] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Use goGRAD; prepare CV, a 1-2-page research statement, all postsecondary records and three referees. Supervisor contact is optional. Submit the form and pay 5-7 days before the final deadline so the checklist and reference invitations can be completed in time. No pre-application supervisor promise guarantees admission. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Central minimum: TOEFL from January 21, 2026 onward overall 4.5 and each section 4.0; older test 90/each 20; IELTS Academic 6.5/each 6; CAEL 70/each 60; PTE 65/each 60; Cambridge C 1/C 2 180; DET 125/each 105. Scores valid two years at submission, achieved in one sitting; TOEFL MyBest/Essentials not accepted, iBT Home accepted. Official verification follows self-reporting. [s4] [Standing rule] No English test is required for an international applicant who completed a bachelor’s or higher taught and examined in English in a country where English is primary. A completed UChicago degree meets this criterion (inference from the US degree context). If still in progress, confirm when the completion-based exemption can be recorded. [s4] [Conflict] Regular mathematics guarantees and SGES include international students. Citizenship-specific awards are separate. Provost International Fellowship requires a qualifying major home-country/equivalent scholarship; central terms say CAD 1,500/term up to 2 years MSc/4 years PhD, conflicting with the math page’s CAD 5,000/year. Confirm the current PIF offer rather than adding either amount automatically. [s1] [s5] [s9]",
    "costs": "[Conflict] Budget CAD 160 for UChicago/foreign transcripts under central goGRAD instructions; Canadian-transcript rateCAD 112. The math page still quotesCAD 150/110, an official conflict. Visa/Mastercard credit cards, including prepaid/gift credit cards, accepted; debit not accepted. Fee is nonrefundable. [s1] [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Recommended, optional, and considered useful by mathematics; not mandatory. The department explicitly invites optional General and Mathematics Subject GRE results. [s1]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Recommended, optional, and considered useful by mathematics; not mandatory. The department explicitly invites optional General and Mathematics Subject GRE results. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three, at least two from evaluators familiar with academic achievement. MSc references should assess readiness for advanced study; PhD references original-research ability. Professional/institutional email, signed institutional letterhead, and direct referee submission are required centrally; friends, relatives and romantic partners are excluded. [s1] [s3]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No separately named SOP appears on the math checklist; the required research statement serves the research-fit purpose. Additional SOP prompt or separate upload is not established. [s1]",
