    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing annual calendar: opens November 1; complete application January 15 for fall entry, no extension. These official math pages do not label this as January 15, 2027, so the 2027 date and closing time/time zone require confirmation. No winter/spring admission competition is advertised. [s1] [s3] [s4]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Actual 2026-27 mathematics base: CAD 34,000 per year for international thesis MSc/PhD students (CAD 33,000 domestic), gross and including teaching/research components across the year; tuition and fees are paid from it. The March 2026 Science policy explicitly PROJECTS a 2027-28 international base of CAD 35,700 (domestic CAD 33,600); this is a forecast, not a fixed 2027 offer. Final annual minima use actual tuition/fees and are announced at least two months before the funding year. Course-based MSc is unfunded. [s9] [s10] [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible in principle for the thesis MSc after a four-year UChicago mathematics bachelor’s, subject to a 3.0/4.0 GPA over the final two years and academic fit. The published PhD requirement is a relevant master’s; a bachelor’s-only direct-PhD route was not established. International applicants are accepted. F-1 status is not Canadian study authorization. A supervisor is needed by commencement, not necessarily before applying. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose the funded thesis MSc rather than the unfunded course MSc. Contact possible supervisors with CV and transcript; list names on the application. Obtain three referees’ consent, create an eID, complete/pay the application, then use Student Centre for documents. Request an English exemption decision if relying on UChicago. Apply separately for GAC once an applicant UCID is available. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s8] [s11]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Science’s higher threshold applies: TOEFL taken before January 21, 2026: 97 with every section 23; tests on/after that date: overall 5.0 and every section 5.0. Alternatives: IELTS 7.0 with each 6.5; CAEL 70/each 60; PTE 76/each 70; Duolingo 135/each 125; Cambridge 180/each 175; Calgary ACC A− in each course. Official results must come from the testing agency. [s7] [s8] [Standing rule] A graduate program director may exempt a completed bachelor’s of at least three years or graduate degree taught AND examined in English at a WHED-listed English-language institution. A completed UChicago bachelor’s appears to meet the substantive criterion (inference), but exemption remains discretionary; obtain confirmation, especially if the degree is still in progress at application. F-1 status itself gives no exemption. [s8] [Standing rule] International full-time thesis students are included; the published base is higher to account for tuition. Fully externally sponsored students are an exception. GAC has no overall citizenship restriction, but each award has its own eligibility. University doctoral recruitment awards highlighted on the recruitment page are domestic and should not be assumed available based on US F-1 status. [s1] [s9] [s11] [s16]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] CAD 145 international application fee; CAD 125 Canadian citizens/permanent residents. Pay through the online application; fee is separate from subsequent tuition. [s5] [s6]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not required: both central program profiles list no admission test scores. The public sources do not establish whether unsolicited GRE results are accepted or considered. English testing is a separate requirement. [s3] [s4]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Not required: both central program profiles list no admission test scores. The public sources do not establish whether unsolicited GRE results are accepted or considered. English testing is a separate requirement. [s3] [s4]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Three admission referees, with reference forms and letters on institutional letterhead. Central rules require recommendations specific to the program and prohibit friends, relatives, colleagues or current graduate students as referees; academic evaluators are preferred for recent graduates. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s6]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No statement of purpose is listed on the public admission checklist; central profiles list no special documents. A portal-only statement prompt/length cannot be ruled out without the current form. [s1] [s3] [s4]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Use Science’s higher English test minimum over the generic graduate-school minimum. Central admissions is more explicit than the math FAQ about invitation timing. Funding projections must not be substituted for fixed offers. Research-area pages still place Matthew Greenberg in number theory, but his current supervisor page lists statistics/data science/machine learning and his personal page says he has left number theory. Nguyen’s dated personal page reports promotion to professor in July 2025 although a directory still says associate. [s1] [s5] [s7] [s8] [s9] [s10] [s17] [s21] [s22] [s29] [s30]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm January 15, 2027 and its time zone; mathematics GAC internal deadline and current essay limits; discretionary English waiver for UChicago if not yet graduated; current admission-letter replacement/reuse rules; fee-waiver availability; final 2027-28 funding amount and tuition/fees; acceptance deadline; any portal-only writing tasks. Ask Mark Bauer for recent research and verify supervisory eligibility for teaching-track faculty before outreach. [s1] [s5] [s8] [s9] [s11] [s12] [s27] [s28]",
