    "rankNote": "QS Mathematics 2026 world rank 301-350. Additional research-fit program; outside Canada top ten including ties. Official QS public table verified 5 November 2026; rank bands have no internal ordering.",
    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing public selector: February 1 for fall and summer; September 1 for winter, for both international and Canadian applicants and both MSc and PhD. It publishes no year or timezone, so February 1, 2027 is NOT yet a verified cycle-specific deadline. All required materials must arrive by that deadline; later consideration is capacity-dependent, not a guaranteed extension. [s5]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No universal mathematics MSc annual guarantee was found. Special Merit awards are considered automatically, but faculty sets amount/duration. Central PhD admission scholarship may provide at least CAD 72,000 across four years (CAD 18,000/year): CAD 9,000/year scholarship plus at least CAD 9,000/year academic-unit assistantships/internal awards. This is an award with eligibility/offer conditions, not an unconditional stipend for every admit; tuition/fees are not explicitly waived. OGS is CAD 5,000/term, up to CAD 15,000 for one year. [s8] [s9] [s11]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago mathematics bachelor’s can qualify for the MSc with a related four-year honours-equivalent degree and B+/75% equivalent, subject to research preparation and supervisor acceptance. The normal PhD requires a relevant master’s at B+/75%; bachelor’s-only direct PhD was not established. Ottawa MSc students can seek PhD transfer within 16 months after two graduate courses each A−, a basic comprehensive examination, research progress, supervisor/advisory recommendations and committee approval. International applicants must demonstrate financial support. F-1 status is not a Canadian study permit. [s3] [s4] [s5] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select the MSc thesis/project/course route; for research, contact supervisors early. Catalogue requires a supervisor name when applying, and acceptance by registration. Arrange two academic referees. Submit and pay through OUAC; uoZone credentials normally follow within one week (follow up after two). Upload required documents and add referees there. OGS can precede the admission application; external candidates request a scholarship-portal account through the published awards-office route. [s3] [s5] [s2] [s11]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Conflicting TOEFL conversion: mathematics selector lists old-scale 84 overall, writing 24, other sections 20, and “New TOEFL 4”; current central page gives post-January 21, 2026 overall 4.5, writing/reading/listening 4.5 and speaking 4 (old-scale equivalents 86/21/22/20/20). Both give IELTS 6.5 overall/writing, other bands 6. Central alternatives: Cambridge 170/160, PTE 60/59, CAEL 70/60. MyBest is accepted centrally. Mathematics requires good English writing even if French proficient. Confirm the applicable conversion if a test is needed. [s2] [s5] [Standing rule] Likely eligible by inference after completing at least two full-time years at UChicago where English is the sole instructional language: United States is on Ottawa’s exemption list. The university reserves discretion to request testing. Obtain explicit exemption confirmation; F-1 status itself provides none. [s2] [2027 confirmed] International applicants can receive doctoral admission scholarships and Special Merit awards. OGS international competition allows candidates without a Canadian visa/permit at application, provided valid proof is supplied before award activation; this differs from some Ontario universities. QEII-GSST excludes international students. Do not infer Canadian citizenship/residency from UChicago attendance. [s9] [s8] [s11] [s12]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] CAD 125, nonrefundable, paid through OUAC. The mathematics selector and university fee schedule effective September 1, 2026 agree. [s5] [s10]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not listed as required or recommended in either mathematics program’s complete public checklist. Whether the portal accepts unsolicited GRE results is unverified; central instructions say extra documents are deleted, so do not assume optional submission is allowed. [s5] [s2]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Not listed as required or recommended in either mathematics program’s complete public checklist. Whether the portal accepts unsolicited GRE results is unverified; central instructions say extra documents are deleted, so do not assume optional submission is allowed. [s5] [s2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Two admission recommendations for either degree, academic referees preferred. They should be able to assess research ability; English or French letters are permitted. [s5] [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required letter of intent. Exact public prompt: “A letter of intent outlining your career goals and proposed research area.” No word/page/font limit published. Upload as a requested uoDoc document; no link-only alternative is stated. [s5] [s2]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] (1) Mathematics selector’s new TOEFL 4 differs from central 4.5 and has legacy component formatting. (2) Live OGS English/French deadlines agree November 19 candidate/November 25 reference, but guidelines call November 25 the applicant deadline and say both reports must arrive before submission. Ask the awards office how to finalize November 19 when reports remain pending; use the dedicated candidate deadline. (3) Old indexed OGS dates November 12/18 are stale. (4) OGS assessment PDF header says 2027-28 while footer/metadata still say 2026-27; its explicit November 25, 2026 date matches current pages. [s2] [s5] [s11] [s12] [s13] [s14]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm fall 2027 admissions year/timezone, supervisor acceptance and funding proof; obtain UChicago English exemption; obtain résumé/intent-letter length rules and exact letter receipt/update/reuse policy. Resolve OGS submission workflow urgently before November 19, 2026; candidate and referee deadlines differ. Obtain an individualized MSc/PhD funding breakdown including tuition, fees, summer and TA duties, and ask about fee assistance before paying. [s2] [s3] [s5] [s8] [s9] [s11] [s14]",
