    "international": "[Standing rule] If not exempt: program page lists TOEFL 4.5 overall with writing/speaking 5, or IELTS Academic 7.0 with writing/speaking 6.5. Scores valid two years; TOEFL MyBest and IELTS One Skill Retake not accepted. Central guidance also accepts specified Cambridge, CAEL, PTE and EFAS routes; consult applicable current score table. [s2] [s7] [Standing rule] Expected exemption: at least three years of postsecondary education in the United States completed by Waterloo program start qualifies regardless of F-1 status. This is an inference applying the explicit country/length rule to UChicago; confirm three years of qualifying study. A generic English-medium letter alone does not establish exemption. [s7] [Standing rule] International admitted research students receive support and additional tuition-offset support. OGS international competition excludes prospective applicants; the department’s general scholarship examples must not override that current restriction. [s8] [s11]",
