    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Contact relevant faculty and discuss research/funding. Complete university application and separate departmental research-experience form; collect official-record scans, CV and two references. Direct PhD adds department approval, supervisor support and project. [b] [e] [f]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] No TOEFL/IELTS requirement or threshold appears in mathematics admissions materials. PhD regulations explicitly require sufficient French and describe English knowledge as desirable; teaching is French. Graduate French proof can be required case-by-case. [c] [d] [g] [Unresolved] No English-test waiver needed on the published math checklist because no English test is specified. UChicago English-medium study does not establish a French exemption: obtain graduate-committee authorization if needed. MSc language arrangements and any French test should be confirmed. [c] [d] [g] [p] [Standing rule] International students included subject to funding-policy eligibility. Tuition exemption renewed for admissions throughWinter 2028; excludes French/Francophone-Belgian candidates covered by other arrangements and applicants with another exemption or external sponsor. Valid CAQ/studypermit, continuous full-time registration required. [n] [o]",
    "costs": "[Prior cycle] Latest displayed schedule is Winter 2027: CAD 83.40 base per term plus 23.35 per regular program =106.75 for one math application. Fall 2027 amount not independently confirmed. Pay on submission; accepted Visa/VisaDebit/Mastercard/ApplePay/GooglePay; noAmEx. Same account/session avoids repeated base fee. [j]",
