    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Fall 2027: January 15, 2027 for all applicants and degree routes; application period September 30, 2026-January 15, 2027. Time of day/timezone not published. FAQ late-October opening is older conflicting guidance. [program] [apply] [faq]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] No verified 2027 offer amount. Official 2025 brochure search extracts report yearly packages: MA CAD 24,547 domestic / 37,596 international; PhD CAD 31,199 / 46,730; Applied MSc CAD 26,670 / 37,596. Direct MA/PhD PDFs now returned 404, so figures are retained as historical indexed evidence only. Undated department FAQ instead gives master’s roughly CAD 14-17k and PhD 27k; basis/year differs or is stale. These are total packages, not verified net living stipends or separate tuition waivers; individual terms, tax, summer and tuition deductions require the offer. [moneyma] [moneyphd] [moneymsc] [faq] [account]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Conflict] UChicago four-year mathematics bachelor’s can satisfy the MA degree-level route, subject to York equivalency and B standing in the final two full-time-equivalent years. The pure-mathematics master’s is the one-year MA; MSc is Applied & Industrial Mathematics. PhD normally needs an acceptable master’s and B+; the required supplementary form explicitly requires a master’s by admission, while the 2025-26 calendar permits one year of comparable work. No direct-from-bachelor PhD exception verified. Older calendar MA B− conflicts with current B. F-1 does not establish Canadian immigration permission; this dossier assesses academic eligibility. [reg] [program] [form1] [calendar]",
    "admissions": "[2027 confirmed] Choose MA/pure mathematics for the bachelor’s route; identify research fit. Submit the initial application and payment early enough for MyFile access (central estimate 3-5 business days); supporting files and referee information follow there. Both downloadable mathematics forms are mandatory; a missing Degree and Program Form prevents consideration. The PhD/MSc form requires two prospective supervisors and their areas. For thesis MSc/PhD, the committee must find a supervisor before admission; prior contact is advised, not documented as a universal pre-submission agreement requirement. OGS has an earlier separate deadline. [apply] [central] [form2] [faq]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Current program lists IELTS Academic 6.5, DET 120, PTE 60, CAEL 60 overall and each component, TOEFL old scale 88 / new scale 4.5, YUELI Level 6 pass or GSPP pass. Central science regulations instead list old TOEFL 79-80 (valid through December 2027) / new 5-6 and GSPP distinction; Cambridge CPE/CAE entries also differ (program C1/C versus central C/C1). Obtain written clarification if a test is required. Agency delivery required; applicant score upload is not accepted. [program] [reg] [central] [Standing rule] Standing exemption: at least one completed full-time year at an accredited university in an English-instruction country or institution. UChicago study should satisfy this by inference, even before degree conferral, provided the year is completed. Department FAQ corroborates possible exemption. York reserves discretion to require testing; confirm waiver in MyFile and supply evidence if requested. Waiver-specific form/deadline and separate TA assessment were not verified. [reg] [faq] [Standing rule] Central funding table explicitly marks MA/MSc and PhD funding available to international students. Department warns funded international places have been few and competitive; eligibility is not a guarantee. Full-time York employees cannot hold graduate packages. OGS admits international applicants, subject to full-time enrollment and academic eligibility; specific quota/study-permit timing should be checked. [fund] [faq] [ogs]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] CAD 140 nonrefundable at initial application, payable by Visa, Visa Debit or Mastercard. Separate applications/payment for multiple programs. [central]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Prior cycle] 2023-24 department calendar explicitly says GRE examinations are not required, without separating general and subject tests. Current 2027 checklist and two forms do not list GRE, but a current explicit accept/consider/recommend/prohibit policy was not found. Treat non-requirement as prior-cycle evidence and confirm optional-score treatment with the program. [oldgre] [program] [form1] [form2]",
    "greMath": "[Prior cycle] 2023-24 department calendar explicitly says GRE examinations are not required, without separating general and subject tests. Current 2027 checklist and two forms do not list GRE, but a current explicit accept/consider/recommend/prohibit policy was not found. Treat non-requirement as prior-cycle evidence and confirm optional-score treatment with the program. [oldgre] [program] [form1] [form2]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] MA: two; PhD: three. The 2025 MSc brochure also lists two. York normally uses its own emailed standardized assessment, and the central application page says prewritten recommendation letters are not accepted. Mathematics-specific professional-versus-academic restrictions were not verified; select academic mathematicians as practical advice, not a quoted rule. [program] [moneymsc] [central]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required Statement of Interest. Central guide suggests 500-1,000 words, not a verified mathematics hard cap. Faithful paraphrase of its questions: intended study; reasons for field and York choice; relevant preparation and experiences; goals after the degree; distinguishing strengths. Upload PDF through MyFile (generic 2.5 MB); font, spacing and mathematics-specific additional prompts unverified. [program] [guide] [help]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current MA B versus 2025-26 calendar B−; current forms require master’s for PhD versus calendar comparable-work alternative. English: program TOEFL 88/4.5 versus central 79-80/5-6, plus GSPP and Cambridge mismatches. FAQ October opening conflicts with explicit September 30, 2026. Undated low funding estimates conflict with 2025 brochures. Generic two-week document advice varies between after application and after deadline; no guaranteed mathematics grace inferred. Normal online reference rule versus approved physical/reuse exceptions must be resolved case by case. [program] [calendar] [reg] [form1] [faq] [moneyma] [moneyphd] [help] [central]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Ask gradmath@yorku.ca: binding support/referee/test cutoff; English waiver recording and any TA oral assessment; current GRE consideration; full MA funding breakdown/terms/tuition/UHIP/TA hours; fee sponsorship; 2027 supervisor availability. Ask FGS awards staff before December 1: OGS-only form access, master’s proposal limits, referee receipt/update rules, visa eligibility timing and handling Fall 2026 grades not yet released. Check MyFile for additional prompts after initial application. [program] [gradfaq] [ogs] [ogsguide]",
