    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] MSc summer 2027 non-EU: January 15, 2027, midnightCET under the current timeline; submit before 23:59 to avoid boundary ambiguity. Portal opening was postponed from November 1 to November 5, 2026. PhD recurring rounds: February 1, May 1, August 1 and November 1, 23:59 localCET/CEST, opening two months before. International candidates wanting August-October start must apply by May 1 at latest (four-month lead time), or an earlier round. Specific 2027 project availability is not yet guaranteed. [s2] [s3] [s12]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] MSc: no living stipend guaranteed. Natural Sciences scholarships are100% tuition waivers only; typically one or two awards/programme, competitive. Mathematics tuition 2026-27 is EUR17300/year;2027-28 not published. PhD4+4 PartA: DKK14852/month before tax at 2026 level, arithmetic DKK178224/year, plus optional paid student-teaching work. Salaried phase sources conflict: approximately DKK30000/month in one paragraph versus28000 elsewhere (annual arithmetic360000 or336000 gross, excluding pension/holiday). Neither is a verified 2027 contract rate. [s10] [s11] [s13] [s14]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: UChicago bachelor may qualify if equivalent to a Danish180-ECTS degree and containing60 ECTS broad mathematics plus10 ECTS programming. Programming is a genuine separate prerequisite; do not assume the math major alone satisfies it. PhD: current flexible4+4 route requires bachelor plus at least60 ECTS additional master-level study; a four-year US bachelor is not automatically declared equivalent. Seek assessment of graduate courses beyond bachelor requirements. Ordinary5+3 PhD requires master-level qualification. [s1] [s13] [s14]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc: check programming and mathematical prerequisites; gather official syllabi, records, English proof and fee receipt; rank up to three programmes. PhD: discuss project and funding with a prospective adviser, prepare every attachment before opening the form - the PhD form cannot be saved partially for later. Separate general-project and advertised-project applications have distinct research-description content. [s1] [s5] [s6] [s12] [s16]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc EnglishB: IELTS6.5 overall/6 each; legacy TOEFL83/20 each; new-scale TOEFL4.5 overall/4 each; Cambridge qualifying certificates. TOEFL/IELTS must be no more than two years old when the application portal opens. No Duolingo/PTE, TOEFLMyBest/Essentials/ITP or IELTSOneSkillRetake. PhD expects fluent academic English comparable to TOEFL83/IELTS6.5 and may request proof during recruitment. [s4] [s12] [Unresolved] A completed English-taught bachelor/master from the USA qualifies for MSc educational exemption, with medium-of-instruction evidence. Because the page says completed and the timeline says English qualifications must be passed by January 15, the pending UChicago degree is NOT a confirmed waiver route for a senior-year application. Ask admissions before relying on it, or obtain a valid test by the deadline. PhD does not state an automatic UChicago exemption from any requested evidence. [s3] [s4] [s12] [Standing rule] Tuition-liable non-EU applicants can receive MSc state waivers. International applicants can compete for PhD positions, subject to qualification and funded plan. Separate ordinary Danish SU entitlement is not implied by PhD-SU scholarship eligibility or US F-1 status. [s11] [s12] [s13]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] MSc EUR150/DKK1125 application fee, covers up to three AU programmes; pay through webshop by deadline and attach receipt to each. Refunded if offer accepted and still enrolled October 1 (summer) or March 1 (winter); not refunded on rejection. PhD GSNS application explicitly free. [s9] [s12]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No GRE General requirement or recommendation in the mathematics MSc requirements or GSNS PhD guide. No public permission/weight for unsolicited scores was established. [s1] [s5] [s12]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No GRE Mathematics requirement or recommendation in the mathematics MSc requirements or GSNS PhD guide. [s1] [s5] [s12]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PhD minimum one reference; additional relevant references permitted. MSc ordinary mathematics checklist lists none. [s5] [s12]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] PhD exact short prompt: “Explain your reasons for applying.” Maximum one page. No specified font/spacing. This motivation is distinct from the project description. No MSc mathematics SOP listed. [s1] [s5] [s12]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] PhD income page contains conflicting28000/30000 monthly salary examples; retain both pending current contract. Older pages imply self-financed students, while application guide now excludes personal/private means and separately permits vetted external scholarships. MSc FAQ says earlyMarch decisions but updated timeline says lateMarch; use timeline/offer. Older openingNovember1 is superseded by November 5, 2026 notice. [s2] [s3] [s8] [s12] [s13] [s14]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Obtain explicit ruling on whether your four-year bachelor plus graduate coursework satisfies flexible doctoral entry; verify10ECTS programming for MSc. Confirm whether a not-yet-completed UChicago degree can meet January 15 English qualification deadline. Check 2027 tuition, exact salaried PhD amount, actual funded projects, reference confidentiality/update process and scholarship response deadline.",
