    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Mathematics bachelor or equivalent of at least three years, with strong algebra/geometry/number-theory preparation. UChicago BA is potentially eligible; selection is academic. Final-year students may apply conditionally, finishing before the next academic year. Already having a master’s is not disqualifying. [apply] [faq]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Apply through apply.algant.eu; choose a preferred two-country mobility pathway and indicate flexibility. The consortium has Bordeaux, Concordia, Duisburg-Essen, Leiden, Milano, Padova, Paris-Saclay and Regensburg. Admission later requires visas, permits and insurance. [home] [apply]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Strong written/spoken English; consortium accepts recognised test evidence or proof of English-taught bachelor, subject to its decision. Host-specific rules still apply. FAQ sends Leiden applicants to current university rules; Padova specifies B2. Concordia has separate official minimums which should be checked directly for the chosen pathway. [apply] [faq] [Standing rule] A UChicago English-taught BA is relevant evidence, but the consortium FAQ expressly makes exemptions discretionary. Obtain consortium and both hosts’ acceptance; do not treat the Leiden US-degree exemption as automatically binding every partner. [faq] [Standing rule] FAQ makes mathematics bachelor/equivalent applicants eligible for merit scholarship consideration without a stated nationality restriction. Visa and host admission requirements still apply. [faq] [apply]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] Nominal programme tuition €4,000/year; merit fee waivers available. A separate consortium application fee is not published, so do not equate absence of a listed fee with a confirmed €0 charge. [faq]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
