    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] International bachelor’s applicants must apply 1-30 November 2026; final deadline 30 November 2026, 11:59 AM CET, for autumn 2027. The official page explicitly says AM. April 2027 is restricted to Swiss bachelor’s applicants and is not a fallback for UChicago graduates. Semester starts 20 September 2027; no spring MSc entry. [a]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] ESOP explicitly increases from autumn 2027 to CHF13,500 per semester plus a tuition-fee waiver. Two semesters equal CHF27,000 by arithmetic; the award is denominated per semester, not a salary. Regular MSc admission has no automatic stipend. Direct Doctorate requires professor-funded MSc scholarship and later salary; a 2027 mathematics salary amount was not established. [b] [h]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A UChicago mathematics bachelor’s can qualify for MSc consideration if its preparation matches ETH’s subject profile and grades are excellent; the degree must be completed by the start of lectures. The 90-ECTS MSc normally takes three semesters. Exceptional bachelor graduates can apply to the integrated Direct Doctorate only after securing a supervisor and funding commitment; ordinary doctoral entry normally follows a master’s. Do not infer eligibility or Swiss immigration rights from US F-1 status. [b] [c] [e]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Review ETH mathematics subject prerequisites, assemble official records from all institutions and the detailed course-content form, select MSc/ESOP/Direct Doctorate in eApply, and obtain two referees’ consent and institutional emails. For Direct Doctorate, find an ETH professor and obtain a written commitment to fund MSc scholarship plus doctoral salary before submitting. For ESOP, prepare the independent thesis preproposal. [b] [c] [e] [g] [h]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] The mathematics MSc is English-taught and requires C1 English unless exempt. Recognized certificate validity is generally two years for TOEFL/IELTS/C1 Advanced, five for C2 Proficiency or C1 Advanced Grade A. The exact score table was not exposed by the public page extraction; use the live recognized-certificates list if the exemption does not apply. [b] [d] [Standing rule] A bachelor’s programme taught entirely in English qualifies for exemption; no separate language-of-instruction confirmation is required for bachelor’s degrees from the United States. Thus a completed English-taught UChicago BA meets the published exemption basis. Applicants still finishing the degree should ensure their eApply evidence establishes that basis rather than assume a later test can cure a missing exemption. [d] [Standing rule] The November ESOP route expressly includes international bachelor’s applicants and does not list a citizenship restriction. International students can apply to Direct Doctorate subject to admission, supervisor funding and Swiss immigration requirements. No assumption about nationality follows from F-1. [a] [b] [h]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] CHF150 per programme for an international bachelor’s application, non-refundable, payable at submission by Visa/Mastercard or PostFinance card. At most two different degree programmes per semester. [e]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not listed in the mathematics-specific application checklist. ETH’s general GRE page applies only where the particular programme stipulates it; do not import the GRE requirement of ETH computer science or other programmes into mathematics. Whether optional scores can be entered for mathematics was not established. [b] [n]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No Mathematics Subject GRE requirement is listed. ETH’s general guidance says a Subject Test cannot replace a required General Test elsewhere; that does not create a mathematics MSc test requirement. Optional-score acceptance was not established. [b] [n]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Two recommendation letters; academic referees or academically trained referees preferred for MSc. Use valid official institutional emails; private addresses such as Gmail are not accepted. [b] [g]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required motivation letter, approximately one A4 page in English. Faithful paraphrase: explain why this ETH mathematics programme, your preparation and intentions, and proposed courses, specializations and project supervisors. Direct Doctorate applicants also explain their suitability for the planned research. Upload; font/margin rules not published. [b] [f]",
    "warnings": "[Standing rule] The headline complete-application deadline has an explicit exception for referee uploads two weeks later. General GRE text must be read subject to programme-specific requirements. Some public dynamic sections omit country labels and English score tables in extraction; no numeric US GPA minimum or alternative test score was guessed. [a] [b] [d] [f] [n] [s]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Confirm any direct-doctorate supervisor immediately given the November cutoff. Verify exact referee grace-period time in the invitation and acceptance deadline in the offer. Inspect live English table only if the US-degree exemption fails. Confirm mathematics Direct Doctorate scholarship/salary and contract duration in writing. Research fit below prioritizes enumerative/arithmetic geometry and number theory; prospective 2027 capacity is unconfirmed. [b] [c] [d] [f] [h] [m]",
