    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] MSc with a foreign degree: May 1-June 15 for winter; October 1-November 15 for summer, standing annual schedule,2027 clock unconfirmed. The later September 30/March 31 domestic dates are not the relevant route for a UChicago degree. Faculty doctoral acceptance has no annual deadline; decisions typically take1 week-2 months, longer outside term. GAUS open call is rolling. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s7]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No guaranteed MSc stipend. Deutschlandstipendium: EUR300/month, EUR3600/year. GAUS salary uses TV-L E13, but workload percentage/step and annual amount are not specified in the open call. LGF standing amount EUR1650/month including EUR100 materials/travel, EUR19,800/12months by arithmetic; it is not an available 2027 award yet. [s7] [s10] [s11]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Conflict] MSc accepts a recognized three-year-or-longer mathematics/equivalent bachelor with above-average performance. The binding regulations allow subject-grade assessment as well as a German2.7 threshold; the summary instead says better than2.7. A degree with at least50% mathematics needs a mathematics thesis,90 relevant ECTS and16 advanced ECTS in each of two areas; limited conditional admission can remedy up to16 ECTS. UChicago equivalence is individually assessed. Doctorate normally requires master/equivalent; §4(5)-(6) permits exceptional bachelor graduates to enter a preparatory qualification route or directs them to the MSc. GAUS jobs require MSc/equivalent. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s6] [s7]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc: assess German readiness and degree/credit equivalence, create heiCO account, prepare academic records and motivation/CV material. For PhD, obtain supervisor agreement, register in heiDOCS and separately seek faculty acceptance and funding. A supervisor’s willingness or a graduate-school offer does not itself establish academic eligibility. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] The pure Mathematics MSc is German, with some English; it requires German proficiency, generally DSH-2 or accepted equivalent by enrollment. Do not import English-only rules from Scientific Computing or South Asian Studies. No universal English examination requirement is stated for the individual mathematics doctorate; clarify with supervisor and doctoral office. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] UChicago’s English-medium degree does not waive the German requirement for the Mathematics MSc. No mathematics-specific automatic doctoral English waiver policy was found; demonstrate language readiness to the supervisor/office if requested. [s3] [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] Deutschlandstipendium accepts all nationalities and incoming MSc students, conditional on enrollment; doctoral students are excluded. GAUS supports international applicants. LGF permits foreign qualifying degrees, but faculty doctoral acceptance must be established before applying; a supervisor letter alone is insufficient. [s7] [s8] [s9] [s13]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] University states there is no application fee. Current non-EU MSc tuition EUR1500/semester plus EUR189.80 semester contribution (winter 2026-27); older faculty estimates nearEUR170 are stale. These are enrollment/study costs, not application fees.2027 rates need reconfirmation. [s3] [s15] [s16]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No requirement in the current MSc regulations, faculty doctoral checklist or GAUS call. Unsolicited score consideration is not specified. [s2] [s5] [s7]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No requirement in the current MSc regulations, faculty doctoral checklist or GAUS call. Unsolicited score consideration is not specified. [s2] [s5] [s7]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] MSc: no mandatory count; supporting recommendations are optional under the regulations. Faculty PhD acceptance: signed supervisor agreement, not a fixed external-letter count. GAUS: two referee names, zero initial letters. LGF: exactly two professor reports for a new application. Deutschlandstipendium: optional scheme-specific letters, no required count. [s2] [s5] [s7] [s9] [s12]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] MSc requires a motivation letter with a tabular chronology of education/employment relevant to the programme, optionally supported by evidence such as recommendations (translation/paraphrase of §2(4)). No word/page limit is published. GAUS requires a cover letter identifying research interests, up to three preferred investigators and projects; no length limit stated. [s2] [s7]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Programme summary says better than2.7; binding rules allow2.7/equivalent or relevant subject-grade assessment. Old admission descriptions mention postal letters while central heiCO is digital-only. Scholarship page uses MEZ in August, whereas FAQ uses CEST/UTC+2. Do not use English-only requirements from other Heidelberg programmes. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s8] [s9] [s17]",
