    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] MSc October 2027: 6 January, 10 March, or 28 April 2027, each 23:59 UK; corresponding decisions by 3 March, 5 May, 1 July. Applications open 30 September 2026; later availability not guaranteed. PhD: applications accepted year-round, funding decisions mainly December-April; departmental recommendation October-March, not a fixed final deadline. [s1] [s3]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] President’s explicit 2027-28: full tuition, £27,036 maintenance per year, £2,000/year consumables for first three years. Roth/EPSRC promise stipend and tuition but annual mathematics-specific 2027 amount not published in pages checked. MSc is not automatically funded; no guaranteed annual MSc support established. [s2] [s4]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: minimum UK 2:1 in mathematics/applied mathematics or overseas equivalent; UChicago mathematics bachelor’s may qualify subject to grade equivalence. Ordinary PhD normally requires a first/upper-second bachelor plus relevant master, or integrated master; exceptional research/accomplishments may justify an exception. Do not treat bachelor-only direct PhD eligibility as automatic. The separate LSGNT route explicitly welcomes outstanding four-year US bachelor students. International applicants considered; F-1 is not UK immigration permission. [s1] [s3] [s14]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] PhD: identify stream and contact a relevant supervisor with research fit and funding situation; proposed supervisor agreement is compulsory for President’s competition, strongly encouraged for ordinary admission. Prepare My Imperial account, documents, two academic referees. MSc: choose course/stream; seek fee waiver before submitting if needed. [s1] [s4] [s10]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc/PhD Standard level. If testing required: IELTS Academic 6.5 overall and 6.0 each; TOEFL before 21 January 2026 92 overall/20 each, new scale from that date 4.5 overall/4.5 each; within two years of start. Other accepted tests on linked English page. Doctoral academic communication requirement remains after entry. [s1] [s3] [s8] [Standing rule] Completed qualification equivalent to UK degree obtained in the USA exempts proof of English for this non-Business programme. UChicago bachelor’s therefore meets the published country criterion once completed; anticipated-degree handling/needed final evidence must be confirmed in offer. No nationality requirement in this exemption. [s7] [Standing rule] President’s all nationalities. Full departmental Roth awards open Home/Overseas. Administrative Roth tied to supervisors may cover only Home tuition or require joint funding - verify full overseas fee gap. EPSRC overseas awards limited (department reports normally one outstanding overseas candidate yearly) with department paying overseas fee difference for selected awards. [s2] [s4]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] 2027-28: MSc £90 per application, including permitted second choice; PhD and combined 1+3 CDT applications free. [s9]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] MSc departmental FAQ explicitly says GRE/GMAT not required. Ordinary PhD checklist does not request GRE; a categorical not-considered rule or permission to upload optional scores was not established. [s1] [s11]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] MSc GRE not required; no specific mathematics subject GRE requirement listed for ordinary PhD. Do not infer that unsolicited scores will be evaluated. [s1] [s11]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PhD: two academic referees with professional email addresses. MSc: two; at least one academic, second academic or relevant professional. For a current mathematics undergraduate, two academic faculty are the straightforward fit. [s1] [s5]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required personal statement serves SOP. General guidance typically one A4 page (guidance, not verified hard portal limit). Faithful paraphrase: motivations for Imperial and other information strengthening application. President’s overrides with prescribed two-page structure. [s1] [s12]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Departmental MSc FAQ says applications until places fill/no formal closing, while explicit 2027 prospectus gives staged closing dates: follow current prospectus. Broad automatic-scholarship language does not remove President’s selection/proposal/supervisor requirements. Old scheme deadlines and fellowship labels in research pages are not current admission guarantees. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s11]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm bachelor-only ordinary PhD exceptional eligibility or choose LSGNT/MSc; exact institutional grade equivalence; ordinary funding stipend and overseas fee coverage; President’s reference/nomination timing; MSc CV/transcript formatting; final qualification, offer acceptance and deposit dates. Faculty openings not verified. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4]",
