    "overview": "[Standing rule] A mathematics bachelor’s or master’s qualifies for application; a completed UChicago mathematics BA can support direct PhD entry, subject to preparation, selection and degree completion. Applications are to the unified programme; research fit with available groups is essential. The diploma does not name a subject specialization. [a] [b]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Study current groups and programme rotations; choose relevant research areas and potential groups, obtain three referees’ consent, prepare CV/SoP/transcripts and three short answers, then create/activate the application account. Use a desktop browser and regularly monitored email. Only groups appearing in the live portal are recruiting this cycle. [a] [c]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Formal English test proof is not required. Written/spoken English competence is essential and assessed during interviews. German is not required. [b] [Standing rule] No degree-specific waiver is necessary: ISTA does not require TOEFL/IELTS/CPE from applicants generally. UChicago study supports English preparation, but does not remove the interview’s language assessment. [b] [Standing rule] The programme recruits internationally and funds all admitted PhD students as employees. No nationality restriction on ordinary salary is stated; Austrian visa/residence paperwork follows an offer. US F-1 status provides no Austrian status. [a] [b] [d]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] No application fee and no tuition fee. [d]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] GRE is not required; the FAQ does not distinguish General from Mathematics Subject GRE in this statement. Valid existing results may be listed in additional information. No recommended-score threshold is published. [b]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] GRE is not required; the FAQ does not distinguish General from Mathematics Subject GRE in this statement. Valid existing results may be listed in additional information. No recommended-score threshold is published. [b]",
    "letters": "[Conflict] Enter exactly three referees; at least two should be academic/research, at most one from a nonacademic work environment. The FAQ requires three submitted letters and will not allow more than three referees. A manual completeness paragraph inconsistently says two; follow the repeated three-letter requirement and resolve with admissions if one letter risks missing. [a] [b] [c]",
    "writing": "[2027 confirmed] Required English PDF, preferably no more than two pages. Faithful paraphrase: explain preparation for graduate research, past projects, motivation for ISTA, technical skills, relevant background, chosen groups and research/career goals. This is explicitly not a research proposal. No font/margin rule published. ISTA expects the applicant’s own voice and discourages generic AI-generated statements. [a] [c]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current2027manual says three referee contacts but one completeness paragraph says two received; FAQ repeatedly requires three. Admissions page short-answer length5-8lines versus manual2-3short paragraphs. Older indexed page’s third question asks about an outside institution; current opened2027page asks about personal research experience. Follow current opened prompt/live portal. Group-selection counts differ by field. [a] [b] [c]",
