    "deadlineDetails": "[Unresolved] The official programme directs applicants to a dynamic selector by academic year, nationality and programme; the specific Mathematics 2027 result was not retrievable from public text. Do not substitute the March/June dates of other faculties. The general absolute registration backstop is 22 September 2027, not a safe international application target. For scholarship applications use the earlier dates below. PhD has no universal deadline; vacancy/supervisor controls. [s2] [s5] [s6] [s16]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Science@Leuven 2027: €12,000/year, plus non-EEA partial tuition reduction; residual 2027 tuition undecided (2026-27 was €3,252.72). Inspiring 2027: ONE award, €13,200/year and full tuition waiver except about€140 annual administration. Master Mind 2027 is PROVISIONAL: KU Leuven says€10,750 covering programme length, tuition around€1,200/year; annual interpretation is not confirmed. Prior government 2026 terms were€10,225/year with near-full waiver and explicitly under2027review. No universal MSc stipend. PhD scholarship net amount is individually calculated and equals an assistant’s net pay; salaried researchers use scale43. No mathematically specific 2027 annual offer verified. [s7] [s11] [s12] [s15] [s20] [s21]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A UChicago mathematics bachelor can apply to the MSc through individual foreign-degree assessment; it is not direct Flemish-degree admission. Programme describes at least 90 ECTS of broad mathematics as ideal preparation. PhD ordinarily requires a relevant Flemish master or equivalent foreign qualification with distinction (or distinguished research achievements), or a distinguished predoctoral exam. A BA alone is not established as equivalent; MSc-first is the ordinary route. F-1 status does not determine Belgian visa/fee/nationality rules. [s1] [s2] [s16]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc: check the year-specific requirements, application-window and tuition selectors; create the university application, upload core and programme documents and pay €120. Science@Leuven: first submit the degree application, then upload its confirmation email in the separate scholarship registration; do not wait for academic acceptance. Joint KU Leuven/Master Mind: add the candidacy annexe AND complete scholarship registration. PhD: first secure a supervisor or funded vacancy; only that supervisor can initiate the degree application and send its unique link. [s5] [s7] [s11] [s16]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc Mathematics: TOEFL old scale 94, reading19/listening18/speaking19/writing21; new scale4.5, reading4/listening4/speaking3.5/writing4.5. IELTS Academic7.0, reading6.5 and other sections6.0. Cambridge C1/C2 185, reading176 and other sections169. General accepted formats include TOEFL Home/Paper and IELTS Online; not TOEFL MyBest, IELTS One Skill Retake or Duolingo. PhD uses separate B2 thresholds: IELTS6.5/no section below6; old TOEFL79 with reading18/writing23; since July 2026 new TOEFL4 with listening/reading/speaking4, writing4.5. [s1] [s17] [s19] [Standing rule] Completed wholly English-taught US university degrees qualify for MSc exemption; UChicago BA meets the stated location/language route once awarded. Science scholarship accepts degree/transcripts confirming the whole course was in English; joint scholarships also explicitly exempt completed English US programmes. Confirm provisional handling before graduation. Arenberg PhD also lists the US-degree exemption and can assess other evidence through its doctoral committee. [s1] [s9] [s11] [s17] [Standing rule] Science: all nationalities except Belgian; non-Belgian bachelor, no previous KU Leuven study/work, no prior MSc/PhD, ambassador commitment. Joint Master Mind/Inspiring: all nationalities, prior degree outside Flanders; existing Flemish enrolment usually disqualifies except specified preparatory study/exchange exceptions. Nationality-specific ASEAN/Africa/Central-SouthAmerica awards share the joint application; eligibility cannot be determined from F-1 alone. [s7] [s11] [s12]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] €120 nonrefundable PER degree application; pay card through portal or bank transfer plus detailed proof. (Pre)doctoral applications are exempt. This is separate from tuition and from the approximately€140 administration charge associated with Inspiring scholarship. [s4]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] No GRE requirement appears in the specific Mathematics admission rules. The university generic checklist mentions GRE only if a programme requires it. Optional consideration/prohibition is not explicitly stated; doctoral vacancy conditions may differ. [s1] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No GRE requirement appears in the specific Mathematics admission rules. The university generic checklist mentions GRE only if a programme requires it. Optional consideration/prohibition is not explicitly stated; doctoral vacancy conditions may differ. [s1] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Ordinary Mathematics MSc page does not specify a letter count. Science@Leuven requires TWO references from internationally recognised professors. Generic recommendation templates are not evidence that all MSc applicants need letters. PhD letters depend on vacancy/funding. [s1] [s3] [s7]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Motivation letter required; recommended length ONE A4 page, not an explicit maximum. Public generic prompt is simply motivation for the programme. Science scholarship evaluates knowledge of the MSc and reasons for choosing it. No fixed font/margins stated. [s3] [s7]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Master Mind 2027 university amount/tuition differs sharply from old 2026 governmental annual grant/waiver and is provisional: no annual guarantee inferred. Ordinary top200 course-description exemption does not erase the Science scholarship’s explicit course-description request. Programme English thresholds exceed generic university minimums. The main Master Mind deadline says23:59CET but one instruction has malformed “23.CET”; companion Inspiring page confirms23:59. [s1] [s7] [s11] [s12] [s15] [s19]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Resolve Mathematics 2027 deadline/tuition in the official selectors using actual citizenship; confirm pending-UChicago BA exemption handling, Science course-description page scope, confidential-letter receipt/update/reuse, and whether joint nomination requests extra references. Recheck Master Mind terms inJanuary 2027. For doctorate obtain master-equivalence assessment, supervisor and concrete funding offer. [s1] [s6] [s7] [s11] [s16]",
