    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] September 2027: April 1, 2027 if a visa/residence permit is needed; May 15, 2027 otherwise (2027-28 brochure plus standing programme rules). Complete uSis, not merely Studielink. The departmental page labels the cutoff 23:59 CET; this label does not resolve April daylight-saving ambiguity. February entry standing dates: October 15 with immigration processing, November 15 otherwise. PhD deadlines are individual vacancy deadlines; employment can start throughout the year. [dates] [brochure] [phd]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] MSc has no automatic stipend. LExS offers tuition contributions at five levels: €10,000, €15,000, €17,500, €18,500 or €19,000. It is not full-cost support; substantial funds for living costs/remaining tuition are required. The public award page does not unambiguously state whether each figure is an annual or whole-programme amount: verify the offer. Illustrative 2026 Leiden PhD job scale: €3,204-€4,051 gross/month for 38 hours, plus 8% holiday and 8.3% year-end payments; this is not a guaranteed 2027 AG vacancy salary. [lexs] [salary]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: a UChicago mathematics BA is eligible for individual comparison with a Dutch research-university mathematics bachelor; completion before enrolment and adequate mathematical preparation required. Current final-year students can apply conditionally. F-1 status is not a Dutch immigration or scholarship category. A subsequent Leiden PhD normally requires a master’s degree and a supervisor/job or separately arranged funded route; this is not an ordinary US-style BA-to-PhD cohort. [admit] [docs] [phd] [phdapply]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose MSc Mathematics and specialisation, register through Studielink, then complete the separate uSis application. Studielink opens October 1 in the preceding year; ULCN credentials may take two days. Prepare the placement letter and records. Pay the application fee before processing. Scholarship applicants must complete academic submission/payment first, allow up to three working days, then return to the scholarship section. PhD: approach the institute or apply to an advertised vacancy before Graduate School registration. [process] [lexs] [phdapply]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] IELTS Academic 6.5 overall, each component at least 6.0; approved TOEFL/Cambridge and other tests are detailed in the July 2026 university table. Test validity normally two years; approved in-person format rules apply. The relevant exception here is a completed degree in the USA. [admit] [eng] [Standing rule] Yes under the published exemption for education completed in the United States; citizenship and F-1 status do not negate a US completed-degree exemption. If still completing UChicago at application, supply the expected-graduation record and obtain the final admission condition in writing; no invented early automatic portal waiver. [admit] [docs] [Standing rule] LExS generally requires a non-EEA/non-EFTA passport and ineligibility for Dutch student finance; mathematics is eligible. UChicago/F-1 alone does not prove citizenship eligibility. Strong prior performance, roughly top 10%, is an indicator rather than a required official ranking certificate. PhD jobs accept international applicants subject to immigration and vacancy requirements. [lexs] [phdapply]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] Application fee €100, nonrefundable, for a foreign qualification; it covers up to three programmes/specialisations in the same academic year. 2027-28 Mathematics tuition: non-EU/EEA institutional rate €23,300/year; statutory eligible Dutch/EU/EEA/Swiss/Surinamese rate €2,771. Citizenship/residence exceptions must be checked individually. The page lists €17,900 for a second Dutch master’s; cooperation-agreement fees can differ (ALGANT). [process] [tuition]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] Not listed among the Mathematics MSc admission criteria or required documents. No explicit public required/recommended/considered/prohibited GRE policy was found; do not infer that a score upload is permitted. PhD vacancies may specify their own evidence. [admit] [docs] [phd]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] Not listed among the Mathematics MSc admission criteria or required documents. No explicit public required/recommended/considered/prohibited GRE policy was found; do not infer that a score upload is permitted. PhD vacancies may specify their own evidence. [admit] [docs] [phd]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Ordinary MSc checklist: no letters listed. LExS: no extra referee listed. PhD: follow the specific vacancy; no universal number established. This does not apply to the separate ALGANT route. [docs] [lexs] [phd]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required placement letter rather than a US-style SOP: faithful paraphrase - explain how your knowledge, understanding and skills meet the standard of a Dutch research-university mathematics bachelor. Upload through the programme application section. No public word/page limit or layout rule located. [docs]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] LExS current page is for September and says December 1, 2026, whereas linked October 2022 terms contain older February-intake language. Use the current scholarship page for intake/deadline and obtain the actual award conditions. Routine deadline page calls its cutoff CET even for April/May; confirm the portal clock. Staff publication databases can be stale; recent personal/institutional lists are used below. [lexs] [lexsterms] [dates]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Confirm passport-based immigration route and LExS eligibility; seek an explicit plan for June UChicago graduation under the July 6/August 1 late-document rules. Verify LExS amount periodicity and individual acceptance deadline. No public GRE consideration policy, referee-update mechanics or unlisted optional-paper upload permission established. PhD requires a later master’s-level route and a live vacancy/supervisor; availability of each listed adviser is unknown. [late] [lexs] [admit] [phd]",
