    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[Prior cycle] Autumn 2027 dates not found. PRIOR PhD mathematics: 19 February 2026, 23:59 CET; six mathematics places. Qualification shortlist by 11 March; oral tests from 17 March; results by 2 April; course starts 1 November 2026. The displayed June second session concerned other science courses, not an established second mathematics round. PRIOR ordinary II level: 30 July 2026, 14:00 Italian time; analysis written 26 August, 08:30; geometry/algebra 27 August, 08:30 (each six hours); oral examinations from 7 September, 09:00, individual calendar published; final rankings not before 16 September. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s6]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] PRIOR 2026-27 PhD: €18,848 gross annually, including lodging allowance, in 12 deferred monthly instalments; free board except academic vacations. Residence access uses the lodging allowance, so it is not an additional unconditional free-housing award. Ordinary II level: free SNS residence/meals, subject to housing availability and academic vacations; if no SNS room, alternative accommodation or €460/month housing contribution for 2026-27. Additional annual all-inclusive teaching contribution depends on ISEE: ≤€40,000: €5,000; €40,001-45,000: €4,500; 45,001-50,000: €4,000; 50,001-55,000: €3,500; 55,001-60,000: €3,000; 60,001-65,000: €2,000; 65,001-70,000: €1,000; above €70,000 or no ISEE: €500. This includes full/partial reimbursement of Pisa university charges; it is not necessarily cash entirely available after tuition. 2027-28 values unpublished. [s2] [s6]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Two distinct routes. PhD: any citizenship; the qualifying degree must permit doctoral entry in its home system, normally a master's or equivalent degree of at least four years, subject to the committee's equivalence assessment. Thus a four-year UChicago BA is potentially admissible, not automatically approved: obtain a written eligibility ruling. Prior call required the qualifying degree within the preceding five years or by 31 October 2026, and barred holders of an Italian PhD or previous Italian doctoral scholarships. Ordinary II level: bachelor's/equivalent for concurrent Pisa MSc; prior call required first qualifying degree on/after 1 November 2024 or by 31 December 2026, and restrictions on previous master's enrollment in the relevant Italian classes or foreign equivalent. An undergraduate taking graduate classes is not necessarily a prior master's enrollee; clarify if applicable. Adequate Italian is required for ordinary admission. F-1 status is not Italian study authorization. [s2] [s3] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] PhD: resolve BA equivalence with phd@sns.it; prepare Europass CV, complete transcript, thesis/abstract, project, publications, passport, and 1-2 referees; register in SNS's online platform and complete every section. Ordinary II level: check degree-date/prior-enrollment conditions and Italian proficiency; independently arrange University of Pisa MSc admission and non-EU Universitaly/visa steps; prepare for on-site analysis and geometry/algebra written and oral examinations. The TOLC requirement for ordinary first-level undergraduate entry is not the second-level graduate route. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] PhD application asks for self-assessment of Italian/English using CEFR; mathematics admission tests may be in Italian or English. No mandatory TOEFL/IELTS certificate or numerical minimum identified in the legal call; Italian courses are offered to admitted non-Italian doctoral students. Ordinary II-level admission requires sufficient Italian to participate; examinations can use Italian/English and Italian competence can be assessed orally. Do not treat an English-speaking PhD route as evidence that the concurrent ordinary/MSc route is English-only. [s2] [s4] [s6] [Standing rule] No UChicago-specific waiver application established, because the inspected PhD call does not require a standardized English score. UChicago study does not remove ordinary-route Italian requirements or University of Pisa's separate language requirements. [s2] [s6] [Standing rule] Both competitions admit all citizenships and standard awards are available to international winners. Prior PhD calls reserve a place per course for qualifying foreign-university graduates under call conditions. Non-EU winners can request documented arrival-travel reimbursement up to €1,000; PhD graduates can request return-home reimbursement up to €1,000 within a year of defence, with additional conditions for early departure. Ordinary ISEE-sensitive funding requires economic evidence; an international student should not assume the maximum €5,000. [s2] [s6]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] SNS study/enrollment is free for successful students. PhD regional DSU tax may be payable initially and reimbursed through the specified process. A separate competition application fee was not established in the inspected sources; do not label it €0 solely from free attendance. University of Pisa MSc fees and recognition costs are separate for ordinary II-level entrants. [s2] [s6]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Neither GRE General nor GRE Mathematics is listed as required in the inspected SNS PhD or ordinary competition documents. This is absence from a complete requirements list, not an explicit statement that unsolicited scores are accepted or considered. Prioritize SNS's own examinations and required dossier. [s2] [s6]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Neither GRE General nor GRE Mathematics is listed as required in the inspected SNS PhD or ordinary competition documents. This is absence from a complete requirements list, not an explicit statement that unsolicited scores are accepted or considered. Prioritize SNS's own examinations and required dossier. [s2] [s6]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PhD: at least one and at most two scholarly recommendation letters, confidentially submitted through the online procedure. Ordinary II-level competition: none specified; selection uses examinations. [s2]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No standalone PhD statement-of-purpose prompt identified. Motivation, preparation and plans belong in the required research project/CV and oral assessment. Ordinary: no separate SOP listed. [s2] [s6]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] PhD FAQ allows home-system doctoral-entry degrees normally including an equivalent four-year degree, while application terminology often says master's: UChicago BA suitability needs committee confirmation. FAQ thesis-abstract advice is less differentiated than legal-call complete/unfinished-thesis limits. English/Italian project-limit wording differs in strictness. Old algebraic-geometry group pages contain obsolete personnel and mixed search results: current board/person pages govern appointments. Current second PhD session lists other disciplines, so its June deadline is not a math deadline. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s10]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Ask phd@sns.it whether the specific four-year UChicago BA and thesis satisfy equivalence and proposal/abstract requirements; obtain 2027 call, dates and budget. Confirm letter dispatch trigger, receipt display and replacement/reuse, portal file-size limits, individual offer-response deadline and any application fee. For ordinary II level, confirm Italian readiness, prior-enrollment eligibility, 2027 ISEE process for foreign finances, and Pisa MSc/visa timing. Confirm Vistoli/Zannier supervision availability and any completed new geometry/number-theory appointment. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s6] [s10] [s15]",
