    "deadlineDetails": "[Prior cycle] 2027-28 deadline not published. Prior GMP cycle: 19 January 2026, 13:00 Italian time, for 1 October 2026 entry; oral examination 23-27 February 2026 remotely. The call website’s general 'open until December' display is not the GMP application deadline. [s1] [s2] [s3]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] Prior 2026-27 call: €16,242.96 annually before INPS deductions, for the course duration. Additional benefits: relocation €1,000 if domiciled outside Europe or €500 in EU; eligible registered Trieste rental €150 gross/month; laptop reimbursement up to €400; eligible health insurance reimbursement up to €700/year; later-year career-development up to €1,000 and qualifying non-EU home-travel up to €500. These are conditional benefits, not guaranteed net salary. [s2]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Conflict] Conditional direct-bachelor possibility: the legal call requires a master’s or suitable foreign equivalent; FAQ says a degree allowing PhD entry in its home system, often a four-year BSc/Hons, may qualify, subject to institutional assessment. UChicago’s four-year mathematics BA therefore merits a specific equivalence inquiry; it is not automatically approved. No age/citizenship restriction in the 2026 call; qualifying degree due by enrolment. [s2] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Request foreign-degree eligibility clarification; select GMP’s actual call in PICA, prepare signed application and uploads, arrange professors’ institutional email addresses, and check the specific selection sheet. Faculty contact is encouraged for research fit but no pre-application supervisor commitment is listed. The old FAQ’s separate non-EU preselection should not be assumed for 2027. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Scientific/teaching activities are in English and Italian is not required according to the FAQ. TOEFL/IELTS or other certificates are described as non-mandatory but welcome; current 2026 legal call lists no compulsory English test or minimum score. Confirm the 2027 call rather than relying on the obsolete parts of the FAQ. [s2] [s4] [Standing rule] No UChicago-specific waiver is needed under the published non-mandatory-test approach, but no separate automatic US-degree exemption policy is stated. The English UChicago record can support language preparation; interview/committee assessment remains relevant. [s2] [s4] [Standing rule] The call expressly welcomes all citizenships; ordinary SISSA awards are not restricted to EU applicants. Non-EU status may qualify for specified insurance/travel support, subject to the exact rules. Visa/Italian residence steps are separate from US F-1 status. [s1] [s2]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] No application fee amount is stated in the checked call/PICA instructions; do not label it free from silence. Regional enrolment tax is separate: prior €120-€160/year. No 2027 tuition/tax schedule confirmed. [s2] [s5]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Not required in the legal checklist. The old FAQ jointly mentions GRE with English certificates as non-mandatory/welcome, without a clear General-vs-Subject distinction. Do not read this as a current explicit GRE recommendation. [s2] [s4]",
