    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] US Études en France HDAP for fall 2027: opened 1 October 2026; initial application due 15 January 2027, 6 pm EST. University responses by 30 April 2027. For an applicant routed to MonMaster/eCandidat instead, exact 2027 dates were not established. Prior 2026: M1 17 February-16 March; M2 26 March-11 June, some extensions to 26 June. [s4] [s11]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] PGSM published rate €1,150/month: M1 first year €13,800 over 12 months; M2 €12,650 over 11 months, or €13,800 if the specified 12th-month condition applies (annual totals calculated). Registration and student social coverage are included in published rules; international awardees receive a CROUS reservation and annual economy home-country round trip. PhD public-contract minimum in 2026 is €2,300 gross/month (€27,600 gross/year calculated); this is a statutory baseline, not a guaranteed 2027 offer. [s8] [s9] [s18]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] M1 is the usual bachelor’s-to-master’s route: a mathematics degree and adequate preparation are assessed. A four-year UChicago BA does not automatically count as French M1; direct M2 requires individual M1 equivalence. ED 386 normally requires a research master’s/equivalent, an HDR-qualified supervisor, an agreed project and institutional funding; personal self-funding is excluded. F-1 status establishes US residence/status, not French admission or nationality eligibility. [s1] [s2] [s14]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] For non-EU citizenship while resident in the US, the mathematics page directs applicants through Campus France/Études en France. EU/EEA citizenship changes the route to MonMaster. Check the exact programme’s portal listing and any additional institutional procedure. PGSM is an independent scholarship application; choose one to three eligible master’s routes and also apply for admission. A Campus France review and interview follow initial submission. [s1] [s4] [s5] [s9]",
    "international": "[Unresolved] No TOEFL/IELTS requirement was established for the general French-taught M1/M2 route. French is the relevant language: Science faculty recommends B2; the exact mandatory certificate/threshold for the selected track must be checked in Études en France. Individual M2 courses may be English, but that does not prove the whole degree is English-taught. [s13] [s20] [Unresolved] A UChicago English-medium degree does not establish a French-language exemption. Campus France exempts applicants applying only to entirely English-taught programmes from French-test submission; confirm that the chosen programme qualifies before relying on this. No specific UChicago English-test waiver was published. [s5] [Standing rule] PGSM’s international call is intended for students studying outside France; UChicago study fits that location condition. Nationality and any additional eligibility conditions still require the actual call review. French doctoral employment is a separate competitive route; foreign doctoral scholarships are explicitly allowed by ED 386. [s8] [s14]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] Campus France USA full DAP/HDAP admissions processing: US$460; this is not the lower US$270 regular pre-consular fee for already-admitted HDAP allégé applicants. No separate Sorbonne academic application fee established. Prior 2026-27 national tuition: master’s €255/year, doctorate €398/year, plus CVEC where applicable; 2027-28 amounts not established. [s6] [s16]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
