    "greMath": "[Unresolved] Neither GRE is listed among the checked admission, PGSM or doctoral-contract documents. This is not an explicit prohibition on submitting a score; no formal GRE policy located. [s3] [s8] [s15]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PGSM: one to three academic recommendations. Campus France generally suggests one or two, rather than universally requiring them. The Sorbonne M2 public checklist does not specify a required count. ED 386 prior contract call allows one or more optional support letters. [s4] [s8] [s15]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Études en France motivation statement: at most 2,500 characters, in French for French-taught programmes or English for English-taught programmes. Sorbonne M2 separately asks for a cover letter specifying proposed courses; no length/format published. [s4] [s3]",
