    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc is English taught. Accepted alternatives include an English-medium prior degree, a graded thesis written in English, or at least10 ECTS of English-taught modules, with documentary evidence. Doctoral admission itself has no formal language-test minimum, although fluent research English is expected. [s1] [s12] [Standing rule] UChicago English instruction should satisfy the published degree/module route if documented. Because a final degree may still be pending, use official English-course evidence rather than assuming a future diploma already proves the requirement. This is an application of the published rule, not an individual waiver decision. [s1] [Standing rule] Non-EU fee-paying international MSc applicants are the target of the tuition-waiver schemes. A UChicago degree does not itself confer EU fee status. Doctorates are exempt from the international tuition charge, but bachelor-only admission is unavailable. [s8] [s10] [s12]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] uni-assist: EUR75 for the first application/VPD request and EUR30 for each additional programme in the same semester. A separate TUMonline application charge was not established. Mathematics currently lists EUR6000 tuition/semester; TUM explicitly raises the EUR6000 master tier to EUR6800 from winter 2027-28. Thus EUR6800/semester (EUR13600/year) is the inferred mathematics 2027 rate pending programme-specific confirmation, plus the semester contribution (currently EUR97 at Garching;2027 unverified). [s2] [s7] [s8] [s9]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
