    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] BIGS current call: 6 December 2026 at 23:59:59 as displayed on MathJobs; timezone is not printed in the retrieved advertisement. Start should be no later than October 2027. Standing second round closes April 15, but no separate dated April-2027 call verified. MSc standing page permits international applications annually January 15 and May 15; however a calendar entry for 15 January 2027 says domestic applicants only. This conflict requires confirmation from apply@math.uni-bonn.de. Do not rely on the August domestic-only round. [a] [c] [d] [e]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] MSc: no tuition, but semester contribution and living costs; no admission-linked scholarship. Hausdorff doctoral positions:75%TV-L E13 employment. Standing BIGS page estimates €2,000-€2,300 net/month depending on circumstances (annual arithmetic €24,000-€27,600 net across12months), with healthcare/social-security benefits. This estimate is not an individualized or indexed 2027 salary promise. The current call confirms pay scale, not exact euros. [a] [d] [e] [g] [h]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: mathematics/related bachelor’s with at least 120 ECTS-equivalent mathematics and B2 English; university catalogue adds German-equivalent minimum grade 2.5. US-credit equivalence must be assessed, not assumed. Non-EU-degree preparation is assessed in analysis, linear algebra, numerical mathematics, probability/discrete mathematics and an advanced area; an aptitude assessment may be requested. BIGS normally requires a mathematics master’s/equivalent; exceptional bachelor admission is possible, and IMPRS describes qualifying-year entry. Ask BIGS whether the specific UChicago preparation qualifies before treating this as a direct-PhD route. [a] [b] [d] [f]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose MSc versus exceptional bachelor-to-BIGS route. MSc: assemble PDFs and one referee, English-medium evidence and optional thesis/papers; assess GRE Mathematics timing. BIGS: discuss exceptional bachelor eligibility with early-careers@hcm.uni-bonn.de, prepare two referees and a substantial mathematical work sample, identify interests/advisers and funding preference, then apply to the current MathJobs call. [a] [d] [e]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc requires CEFR B2; current opened page accepts an appropriate TOEFL/IELTS score, B2 coursework evidence, or English-medium bachelor’s proof. Its indexed earlier extract gives TOEFL79/IELTS6, but the opened current text no longer states those numbers, so rely on B2 and confirm exact tests if needed. BIGS requires English proficiency, no German; current call requires evidence. IMPRS accepts TOEFL or equivalent qualification, without a public numeric cutoff. [a] [d] [e] [f] [Standing rule] MSc explicitly accepts proof that the bachelor’s teaching language was English, so obtain UChicago registrar/degree evidence if the transcript does not establish it. Non-native nationality does not defeat this route. For BIGS/IMPRS, an English-medium UChicago degree may be equivalent evidence but an automatic US-degree waiver is not explicitly documented; confirm acceptable proof. [a] [e] [f] [Standing rule] IMPRS explicitly accepts all countries; BIGS recruits internationally, and the current employment call welcomes applicants regardless of origin. MSc international students also pay no tuition, but must finance living costs and semester contributions. [a] [e] [f] [h]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] Bonn’s university costs page states applying for admission is free. No programme-specific additional fee appears in the MSc or current BIGS call. Semester contribution is separate from application fee and tuition. [a] [e] [g]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No GRE General requirement appears in the MSc or BIGS current requirements. Optional General-score acceptance is not stated. [a] [d] [e]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] MSc recommends the Mathematics GRE for applicants whose bachelor’s was outside the EU, including UChicago; recommended is not required. ETS institution code6301. BIGS current call does not list a Mathematics GRE requirement. [a] [e]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] MSc international applicant: one referee. BIGS standing instructions say at least two; the current HCM-PHD27 call requires two. [a] [d] [e]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] MSc required motivation letter in English/German: faithful paraphrase - why Bonn, main mathematical interest and experience in it; no public length limit. BIGS required motivation/cover letter maximum 2pages: faithful paraphrase - why a mathematics PhD and Bonn, intended area and background, and any known/contacted suitable Bonn faculty. Upload PDF. [a] [d] [e]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] MSc detailed page: internationalJanuary15/May 15; dated15January2027calendar: domesticonly - confirm before relying. MSc catalogue lists winterentry while detailed page permits winter/summer. Current opened English rule givesB2, indexed text gives oldspecificTOEFL79/IELTS6. BIGS generic text says emailed letters but currentMathJobs call requires onlineletters. Currentcall allows possiblefourthyear while standingpage saysthreeyears. [a] [b] [c] [d] [e]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Ask MSc office to resolveJanuary2027internationaldeadline and assess UChicago credits against120ECTS. AskBIGS about bachelor exception, qualifying-year funding, equivalentEnglishproof and replacement ofmaster-specific fields. VerifyMathJobs timezone, MSclettertrigger/receipt/reuse, and offeracceptance dates. Faculty below are a selected core fit list; 2027capacity isnotguaranteed. [a] [b] [c] [d] [e] [f]",
