    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] MASt: 2 February 2027, 23:59 UK time. DPMMS PhD: 13 May 2027, 23:59 UK time, but contact phd-admissions@maths.cam.ac.uk before submitting after 6 January. Late availability is not assured. [a] [b]",
    "funding": "[Unresolved] No universal guaranteed annual mathematics stipend is published in the funding pages checked. Department funding is competitive, can include research-council awards, and must not be treated as automatic. Obtain exact maintenance amount, international fee coverage, and award period from each award. [k]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] Conditionally eligible for MASt with a first-class-equivalent mathematics degree; US equivalence is normally GPA 3.7/4.0. DPMMS PhD permits a comparable four-year mathematics degree, or three-year degree plus one postgraduate year; a separate master's is not categorically mandatory. Advanced preparation and supervisor fit remain competitive judgments. F-1 is not UK immigration permission. [c] [d] [m]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose the MASt pathway matching your background, or identify 2-3 suitable DPMMS supervisors and up to two research areas. PhD informal contact with CV is encouraged but not mandatory. Secure referee consent; upload documents and pay applicable fee before submitting. [j] [f] [h]",
    "international": "[2027 confirmed] If testing is required: IELTS Academic total 7.0, listening/writing/speaking 7.0, reading 6.5; published TOEFL scale total 100 with 25 each. Cambridge also lists C1/C2 alternatives. Verify accepted test format when booking. [c] [d] [Standing rule] Inference from published exemption: a completed US bachelor's of at least three years, completed within two years of Cambridge entry, normally removes the test requirement. UChicago should qualify on degree location/duration; the portal and offer determine any condition. Nationality alone is not the basis. [e] [Standing rule] Funding consideration is available irrespective of fee status, but each award has separate eligibility. Department explicitly expects applicants to seek other eligible awards. US residence on F-1 does not make one eligible for US-citizen-only awards. [k] [j]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] PhD: GBP 20 per applicant per entry year, covering up to seven doctoral applications. MASt: GBP 85 per application. Pay online before submission; Visa/Mastercard accepted, not AmEx. [h]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] MASt explicitly does not require GRE. PhD does not list GRE; general Cambridge guidance says only send it when the course requests it. No evidence that an unsolicited score helps. [l] [g] [a]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No mathematics GRE is requested on either current course checklist. MASt explicitly states no GRE requirement. Do not confuse non-required with a verified promise to consider optional scores. [l] [a]",
    "letters": "[2027 confirmed] Two references for each course application; academic referees are appropriate for a current undergraduate. [a] [b] [f]",
    "writing": "[2027 confirmed] Both require a portal response explaining reasons for applying, maximum 1,500 characters (prompt paraphrase). No separate long SOP listed. [a] [b]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] MASt page has generic Gates material although institutional fellowship guidance excludes MASt; verify directly before relying on Gates. Squarepoint text still says 6 January 2026, alongside the 2027 main deadline. Gates prompt wording in Cambridge help may be stale. These are unresolved rather than silently corrected. [b] [l] [q] [r]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Check current Gates eligibility/prompt directly; ask about 2027 stipend and full overseas-fee coverage; verify any course-list upload and already-submitted letter replacement. Confirm supervisor availability before outreach. Grojnowski's official list has no recent paper, so recent activity cannot be assessed from that list alone. [o] [k]",
