    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] MSc non-EU September entry: January 15,23:59CET, portal opens November 15 (standing rule, hence January 15, 2027 planning date). The explicitly advertised September 1, 2027 PhD call closed November 1, 2026,23:59GMT+1. Department also announces a recurring April 1 PhD call, usually posted in February; a specific April 2027 vacancy and its terms are not yet verified. February MSc intake is for legal-right applicants and is not the ordinary route from UChicago. [s1] [s4] [s8] [s9] [s10]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] MSc: no universal stipend. SCIENCE government scholarship covers full tuition and22 months of living costs; monthly cash amount is not published. Government study portal lists mathematics tuition EUR8700/semester, EUR17400/year, without a 2027-specific guarantee. Integrated PhD before master: up to48 grant portions at DKK7426 each (2026 rate), plus salary for 150 work hours/year; portions are not a stated48-month payment schedule. Later salaried phase and regular PhD follow collective agreement; math call does not quote annual salary. A separate UCPH 2026 PhD ad quotes DKK31800/month plus18.07% employer pension, indicative only, not a math 2027 guarantee. [s6] [s7] [s8] [s44]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: a completed or in-progress UChicago mathematics bachelor can be assessed as an international degree. Required background: at least30 ECTS analysis,22.5 ECTS linear algebra/algebra and15 ECTS geometry/topology. Supplementation after the bachelor is completed cannot cure missing prerequisites. Integrated PhD accepts bachelor-level entrants who qualify for the relevant MSc; regular three-year PhD normally requires the equivalent of a Danish180-ECTS bachelor plus120-ECTS master. F-1 status confers no Danish fee or immigration exemption. [s1] [s8] [s12] [s17]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] For MSc, prepare KU GPA calculator, programme self-assessment and course-description template, English evidence, verified records and passport; pay the non-EU fee before submission and upload receipt. For integrated PhD, identify appropriate research supervisors and enter their names; secure admission to the associated MSc as required by the offer. Do not complete later formal PhD enrollment forms before receiving a stipend offer. [s2] [s5] [s11] [s12]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc English B: legacy TOEFL iBT83 overall with20 each, new-scale TOEFL4.5 overall and4.5 each; IELTS Academic6.5 overall with6 each; Cambridge CAE/CPE180. Accepted versions include TOEFL Home Edition and IELTS Online; no TOEFL MyBest or IELTS One Skill Retake. TOEFL/IELTS expire after two years measured at study start; Cambridge does not expire. Upload report or official appointment/TRF identifier for verification. [s3] [Standing rule] NO for MSc: KU explicitly rejects an English-taught bachelor/master, university medium-of-instruction letter and native-speaker status as substitutes. It offers no language waiver. Unless you independently hold one of its listed school-level qualifications, plan a qualifying test. PhD appointment language assessment is separate; do not assume this removes integrated-MSc requirements. [s3] [s11] [Standing rule] MSc government scholarship is for non-EU/EEA candidates required to pay tuition and eligible for a Danish study permit, excluding those entitled to Danish SU. International applicants can compete for PhD employment/integrated stipends; citizenship is not an advertised exclusion. US F-1 does not replace Danish permission. [s6] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] MSc non-EU application fee DKK1120 (approximately EUR150), once per round for up to three programmes; pay in DKK before submission and upload receipt for each. Submitted applications are generally not refundable. Tuition is separate: first two semesters due April 15; third August 15 and fourth January 15 under the standing schedule. No application charge was found for the employment-based PhD call. [s5] [s8]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No GRE General requirement or recommendation appears in the MSc checklist or examined 2027 mathematics PhD call; no assurance was found that an unsolicited score would be considered. [s2] [s8]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No GRE Mathematics requirement or recommendation appears in the MSc checklist or examined 2027 mathematics PhD call. [s2] [s8]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] MSc: none in the ordinary checklist. Examined PhD call: references if available, no numerical minimum established. Do not borrow a two/three-letter rule from another Danish university. [s2] [s8]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No ordinary MSc motivation/SOP item listed. PhD: motivated letter, maximum one page. Mini-guide content: preparation and grades, research interests and reasons for Copenhagen; explain unfamiliar grading scales if helpful. Exact font, margins and spacing are not prescribed in the checked call. [s8] [s11]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Department old taxameter text says DKK80000/year, but central 2027 schedule says DKK85000/year (DKK255000 over three years; modules55000+30000, possible module exception). Use central 2027 rules. Legacy Rordam PDF demands a standard cover template; current 2027 call instead states motivated letter max one page, so do not import the old template uncritically. Staff roster marks Schlichtkrull emeritus although research-area prose lists him among permanent faculty. [s10] [s14] [s18] [s19] [s46]",
