    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] AGQ page explicitly gives 18 December 2026 for both forms/full consideration, with later rolling consideration only if possible; clock/timezone not stated. Edinburgh’s 2027 AGQ catalogue says 19 December 2026, while general Mathematics says 18 January 2027. Use 18 December as the prudent target and obtain written clarification rather than assuming January applies to AGQ/AGT. [s1] [s4] [s5]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] AGQ covers full tuition and tax-free annual UKRI-linked stipend; page still quotes £20,780 for 2025/26, not 2027. Edinburgh School/EPSRC page quotes £21,805 for 2026/27, also not 2027. Neither establishes exact 2027/28 stipend. EDCS covers fees plus stipend; Mathematics cash amount not yet specified. AGQ MSc pre-year likewise covers fees and stipend; amount unverified. Visa/IHS, payment schedule and additional travel allowance not established. [s1] [s4]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] AGQ accepts applicants with or expecting at least UK 2:1-equivalent bachelor’s; an MSc is not universally required. Applicants may request the fully funded MSc pre-year pathway. Edinburgh’s general direct PhD rule is first-class bachelor’s, or 2:1 plus master’s; do not conflate this with the AGQ threshold. UChicago international graduates may apply subject to equivalence, preparation and funding selection; US F-1 creates no UK status entitlement. [s1] [s3]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] AGQ requires BOTH its pre-application form and the Glasgow application portal, including for Edinburgh-aligned degrees. Choose admissions panel and three topic keywords; supervisor preferences optional. Ask two academics to send letters through AGQ’s separate reference link. Follow the programme-specific Glasgow placeholder instructions in portal_public_instructions. [s1]",
    "international": "[Conflict] AGQ lists IELTS 6.5 overall/6.0 each, TOEFL iBT 92/20 each, PTE 68/63 each, Cambridge 176/169 each; tests within two years at application. Edinburgh’s older general mathematics page instead has PTE 61/56 and measures test age at programme start. The degree route below is preferable if applicable; confirm current scale rules for newly reformatted TOEFL tests rather than extrapolating old totals. [s1] [s3] [Standing rule] AGQ accepts undergraduate/master’s degrees taught and assessed in English in a UKVI majority-English-speaking country, which includes a completed UChicago degree by inference. Edinburgh general page limits degree age to 3.5 years at programme start; Glasgow FAQ adds final two years in the country within six years. Confirm receiving university’s documentation and timing rather than requesting an unconditional blanket waiver. [s1] [s3] [s11] [2027 confirmed] Edinburgh School/EPSRC states awards open to all applicants with full fees and stipend; EDCS explicitly open to UK and overseas candidates. AGQ catalogue says eligibility is assessed under funder rules; precise 2027 international allocation/cap and MSc pre-year international availability need confirmation, not assumed from US residence. [s4] [s5]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] Edinburgh 2027 AGQ catalogue says no application fee; Glasgow FAQ likewise says postgraduate applications are free. [s5] [s11]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] No GRE requirement or recommendation found in AGQ or Edinburgh mathematics lists. Public sources do not explicitly say scores are ignored or prohibited; optional-upload policy remains unverified. [s1] [s3]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No GRE requirement or recommendation found in AGQ or Edinburgh mathematics lists. Public sources do not explicitly say scores are ignored or prohibited; optional-upload policy remains unverified. [s1] [s3]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Two academic letters for AGQ and Edinburgh mathematics. This is stricter than generic Glasgow wording permitting one professional letter; use two academic writers under programme-specific instructions. [s1] [s3] [s12]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] AGQ pre-form requires a motivation response, maximum 1,000 characters and described as half a page; faithful paraphrase: why pursue mathematics graduate study. Enter form text. If a separate Edinburgh EUCLID application is requested, its general personal statement limit is 3,500 characters (about 500 words): preparation, relevant experience, programme/Edinburgh motivation and career aims. These are distinct routes, not automatically cumulative essays. [s1] [s8]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Three different deadline pages (18 December, 19 December, 18 January) and two portals exist: route-specific AGQ instructions control planning pending clarification. AGQ allows applicant-uploaded reference PDFs while Edinburgh mathematics refuses applicant-uploaded references; use confidential direct AGQ writer upload. English PTE levels/test-age endpoints differ. AGQ supervisor list still labels Dervan Glasgow while current Warwick official pages list him there; not included as an available AGQ adviser. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s9]",
