    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] MSc non-EU applicant: July 15 for winter and January 15 for summer, standing annual dates; no 2027 cutoff clock is published. Central winter window opens April 15, while the departmental banner says May 15. Doctoral faculty acceptance is individual, with no annual admissions deadline stated; project-job deadlines are separate. [s1] [s2] [s5]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No guaranteed annual MSc stipend; the university states it does not offer fully funded scholarships. Deutschlandstipendium is EUR300/month for 12 months, EUR3600 total by arithmetic, for eligible selected students. Doctoral salary/stipend amount depends on a separate employment or fellowship offer; no universal 2027 mathematics amount verified. [s10] [s11] [s12]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: recognized mathematics/equivalent bachelor of at least three years;103 ECTS of mathematics including16 each in analysis, linear algebra, advanced pure mathematics and advanced applied mathematics. Committee exceptions are possible. Pending degree accepted with thesis-status or expected-completion evidence. Doctorate normally requires an above-average master/equivalent, but §5(3) permits exceptional bachelor graduates in the top5% of their programme over the preceding six semesters, with faculty sponsorship, assigned master modules and an oral aptitude examination within about two semesters. UChicago credit, rank and degree equivalence require individual confirmation. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc: map UChicago courses to the four subject-credit requirements, obtain English-medium-degree evidence, register in HISinOne and submit uploaded records. Clarify whether APS wording for applicants from China/India/Vietnam applies to a US-earned degree. Doctorate: obtain an eligible supervisor’s agreement first, clarify the bachelor exception, sign the doctoral agreement, then submit faculty acceptance materials. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s6]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc is taught in English from winter 2026-27 and requires B2 English, with no German requirement. Accepted examples include an English-medium undergraduate degree in the United States, TOEFL iBT72 on the older scale or4 on the new scale, and IELTS5.5; test evidence normally must be within two years. Doctoral rules allow adequate German or English evidence as applicable. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s7] [Standing rule] A completed English-medium UChicago undergraduate degree fits the central US-degree evidence route. The exact substitute accepted while the degree is still pending is not explicit; obtain a university instruction-language/completion letter and confirm with admissions. This is an evidence route, not a citizenship exemption. [s4] [Standing rule] Deutschlandstipendium accepts all nationalities, but winter entrants cannot use the pre-entry summer-applicant route and doctoral students are excluded. Foreign students may search DAAD and other funders; eligibility is award-specific. US F-1 status does not itself establish German funding eligibility. [s10] [s11]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] No explicit mathematics application-fee amount was established. Current non-EU consecutive MSc tuition is EUR1500/semester plus EUR190 semester contribution; these are study/enrollment charges, not application fees, and 2027 changes remain possible. Doctoral tuition treatment must be checked separately from MSc charges. [s8] [s9]",
