    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] MSc winter entry: May-July 15, standing annual schedule; no exact 2027 clock/time zone published. Early round ends around late May/early June. Summer: November-January 15, with first round November 30; the central calendar explicitly includes January 15, 2027. Doctoral autumn 2026 call: November 1, 2026, now closed; start no later than autumn 2027. Spring 2027 call date is not yet established. [s1] [s5] [s6] [s24]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] MSc Full Grant: EUR992/month, equivalent to EUR11,904 over12 funded months (arithmetic), plus a one-time origin-dependent travel allowance and semester fee. Competitive, not automatic. Doctoral positions:75% TV-L E13 employment for three years; exact annual gross/net euro amount depends on pay scale/step and is not published in the call. MSc tuition is zero; winter 2026-27 semester fee EUR369.50, not a confirmed 2027-28 charge. [s4] [s6] [s7] [s8]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: a recognized mathematics/comparable bachelor’s of at least six semesters, including120 ECTS in mathematics; final German-equivalent grade3.0 or better (department says US GPA2.0 equivalent). Provisional transcripts may be submitted with3.3 or better, but final degree is required for enrollment. UChicago is a plausible degree route; credit equivalence is assessed, not automatic. Doctoral calls normally presuppose master’s-level qualification; direct UChicago bachelor eligibility is not established. [s1] [s5] [s6]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] For MSc, prepare CV, transcripts/syllabi, English evidence and the department questionnaire; complete online application, then follow its emailed upload checklist. Submit the separate full-grant request if seeking funding. If Chinese/Indian/Vietnamese academic history or nationality applies, clarify APS requirements for a US-earned degree. For a doctorate, identify at least two local investigators and wait for an open call; the November 2026 round has closed. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s9]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc English B2: TOEFL iBT>=72 on the old scale, IELTS>=6.0, or an English-language bachelor’s. No German requirement is listed for this English MSc. Doctoral call asks fluent English, no German; certificates or transcripts showing English instruction/coursework are accepted. [s1] [s5] [s6] [Standing rule] The MSc explicitly accepts an English-language bachelor’s, so a completed UChicago degree fits. Confirmation is still needed for the proof accepted while the degree is pending. Doctoral FAQ also accepts English-taught coursework recorded in the transcript; no separate test is automatically needed under that route. [s1] [s5] [Standing rule] Full Grant targets international master’s students; first degree must be completed before funding starts, and prior residence in Germany cannot exceed12 months during the preceding three years. US F-1 status alone does not violate that condition. Doctoral call welcomes applicants regardless of nationality. [s4] [s6]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] No application fee is stated in the mathematics MSc or doctoral instructions checked, but an explicit mathematics-wide zero-fee confirmation was not established. Tuition is zero; semester contribution EUR369.50 for winter 2026-27 is an enrollment charge, not an application fee. [s1] [s2] [s6] [s8]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No GRE requirement appears in the complete public MSc checklist or doctoral call. Optional score consideration is not expressly described; do not assume a score upload is requested. [s1] [s6]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No GRE requirement appears in the complete public MSc checklist or doctoral call. Optional score consideration is not expressly described; do not assume a score upload is requested. [s1] [s6]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Ordinary MSc: no letters on the published required checklist. Full Grant scholarship: two university-professor letters. Doctoral call: at least two recommendation letters. [s1] [s4] [s6]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Ordinary MSc checklist has no separate SOP. Doctoral application requires a cover letter, without a public word/page limit or detailed prompt; explain research fit and name at least two local investigators as required elsewhere in the form. [s1] [s6]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] MSc grade3.0 final versus3.3 provisional are distinct stages, not interchangeable thresholds. Central APS wording refers broadly to applicants from China/India/Vietnam and does not clarify this UChicago-degree scenario. Old faculty/group membership pages are checked against current institutional investigators and personal pages. [s1] [s2] [s9] [s10]",
