    "rank": null,
    "rankSource": null,
    "rankNote": "Relevant European programme; no numerical ranking asserted",
    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] DPhil: 6 January 2027 at 12:00 noon UK time is the funding deadline; expected final deadline 2 March 2027 at 12:00 noon UK time, subject to places. OMMS: final deadline 27 January 2027 at 12:00 noon UK time. These are midday, not midnight. [a] [b]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] No universally guaranteed mathematics funding amount was established. Clarendon covers course fees and a living grant: its applicant page still illustrates at least £20,780 for 2025-26. Oxford’s living-cost page gives £21,805 as the 2026-27 UKRI-linked graduate scholarship rate. Neither is a confirmed 2027-28 award amount; the offer is controlling. Do not confuse a scholarship rate with automatic funding on admission. [k] [l]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] Both programmes accept an appropriate first-class-equivalent bachelor’s; the normal minimum for a US degree is 3.7/4.0. A master’s is not categorically required for the DPhil. A UChicago mathematics bachelor’s can therefore meet the degree-route requirement, conditional on grades, preparation and completion before entry. F-1 status is not a nationality or funding entitlement. DPhil 3-4 years; OMMS nine months. Both begin 4 October 2027. [a] [b]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select DPhil versus OMMS and create the Oxford graduate application. DPhil: name at least one research group in the proposed-field section; up to three supervisors may be suggested, without prior approval. OMMS: choose a preferred subject grouping; Algebra, Geometry, Number Theory, Topology and Logic is the closest initial choice and does not bind later options. Register three referees; request English waiver in the form; prepare transcripts and the programme-specific statement. [a] [b] [c] [d]",
    "international": "[2027 confirmed] DPhil uses standard English: IELTS Academic 7.0 overall, at least 6.5 each component. OMMS uses higher English: IELTS 7.5 overall, at least 7.0 each. Published TOEFL thresholds are 100 and 110 respectively, each requiring listening 22, reading 24, speaking 25, writing 24, BUT both current course pages say TOEFL tests taken from 21 January 2026 are not accepted pending review of the revised test. Consult the current official table before booking. [a] [b] [Standing rule] A waiver can be requested for a completed or current full-time degree of at least nine months taught and assessed entirely in English, with no more than two academic years between completion and Oxford entry. UChicago falls within the US/majority-English-country route: additional medium-of-instruction evidence is not normally required. Select the waiver request in the Languages section; the department decides, so it is not an automatic exemption. Completion of the qualifying degree can be a condition. [c] [Standing rule] Clarendon is open to all nationalities and full-time/part-time eligible graduate subjects; overseas fees are covered for recipients. Other awards may restrict citizenship or residence. F-1 status alone does not establish eligibility for any nationality-restricted award. [k] [n]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] DPhil research application £20; OMMS taught application £75, payable in GBP by Visa or Mastercard at submission unless a waiver is granted. Fees are non-refundable. [i]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Neither course seeks GRE or GMAT scores. No separate Mathematics Subject Test requirement is listed; do not add unsolicited scores as a substitute for the stated materials. [a] [b]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] Neither course seeks GRE or GMAT scores. No separate Mathematics Subject Test requirement is listed; do not add unsolicited scores as a substitute for the stated materials. [a] [b]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] DPhil: three referees, preferably academic; up to one professional reference can be accepted. OMMS: three, at least two academic. In both cases Oxford may begin assessment with two received, while retaining the right to require the third. [a] [b] [d]",
    "writing": "[2027 confirmed] Required in English. DPhil maximum 800 words: faithful paraphrase of prompt - explain motivation, relevant education/experience, research aptitude and intended areas and/or a research-plan outline. OMMS maximum 600 words: faithful paraphrase - explain motivation for Oxford, relevant educational/other background and areas or specialization of interest. Display the word count if possible. Upload as a supporting document using the accepted file formats; no special font/margin rule was found. [a] [b] [g]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] The published TOEFL numerical thresholds coexist with a warning that tests from 21 January 2026 are not currently accepted while the new format is reviewed; the warning governs booking decisions. Clarendon’s 2025-26 maintenance example and the university’s 2026-27 rate refer to different years, not competing 2027 guarantees. [a] [b] [k] [l]",
    "checks": "[Standing rule] Confirm degree completion date/GPA, request rather than assume the English waiver, and verify any post-January-2026 TOEFL policy change before booking. Resolve the precise funded amount and acceptance deadline from the offer. Ask about submitted-letter replacement if needed. Select citizenship-eligible separate awards and inspect their exact forms; establish each potential adviser’s 2027 capacity. Faculty coverage emphasizes algebraic/arithmetic/complex geometry and representation theory; broader analytic-number-theory coverage is not exhaustive. [a] [b] [c] [f] [k] [n] [p] [q] [r]",
