    "deadlineDetails": "[Prior cycle] Autumn 2027 dates unpublished. PRIOR MSc non-EU Italian-taught open-admission window: 8 July-31 December 2026; visa applicants must start before arrival, and scholarships/language tests close earlier. PRIOR PhD: 8 June 2026, 13:00 Italian time. Interviews within 22 June-6 July 2026, with detailed calendar separately published; final rankings by 27 July. Prior PhD ordinary start 1 November 2026. The general site's August Bando B date is not established as a second mathematics competition. [s2] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s7]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] PRIOR 2026-27 PhD: €16,243 gross beneficiary amount per year, monthly payments; 11 funded math positions, four unrestricted and seven topic-specific. Research budget at least 10% of stipend, plus authorized overseas-research stipend increase of 50% up to 12 months (18 for qualifying joint/cotutelle routes). MSc no guaranteed stipend. DSU prior standard non-resident annual cash: €3,338 for ISEE ≤€13,500; €2,262 for €13,500.01-18,000; €1,060 for €18,000.01-27,000, plus two meals/day and accommodation subject to availability/conditions and tuition relief. Noncash service valuations (€1,760 meals + €3,150 housing) are not extra cash. INdAM amount not verified; do not assume a national figure. [s4] [s5] [s11] [s13] [s14]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: a UChicago mathematics BA is a plausible qualifying foreign bachelor's, subject to suitability and preparation assessment by the degree council. Mathematics curriculum/foreign equivalence is checked; alternative Italian routes require ≥30 ECTS in mathematics. The Italian-taught route requires non-EU visa applicants to demonstrate Italian B2. PhD: the legal call requires an Italian master's or a foreign degree assessed as equivalent to an Italian second-cycle degree, considering level, duration, content and home-country academic rights. A four-year US BA is not automatically eligible; unlike SNS/SISSA's explicit four-year language, Pisa's call requires second-cycle equivalence, so plan the MSc route unless Pisa confirms otherwise. F-1 does not provide Italian residency authorization. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc non-EU visa route: initiate Universitaly pre-enrollment; register in Alice with passport/photo, then use AmmissioneLM (do not choose the MSc inside Alice), matching the exact program on Universitaly. Obtain degree, all-course transcript and university-certified syllabi with the required Italian translations. Resolve Italian B2 certificate/test before visa validation. After council review (approximately 2-3 weeks), upload the admission decision to Universitaly; arrange visa and residence permit. PhD: check foreign second-cycle equivalence, select each competition separately, prepare signed CV and academic file, two mathematician referees, any remote-interview form, and PagoPA payment. Contact project supervisors for restricted positions. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s7]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc mathematics requires English B2 by graduation if not already demonstrated on entry; acceptable evidence includes the Pisa CLI examination or recognized certificate. This does not replace Italian B2 for the Italian-taught non-EU visa route. Italian exemption requires approved CLIQ B2 certification or ministerial exemption; otherwise ITA L2 ≥55/72 plus successful CLI oral interview. PhD inspected call does not mandate TOEFL/IELTS or publish a numerical English threshold; confirm interview language with coordinator. [s1] [s3] [s4] [s5] [Unresolved] No explicit UChicago/US-degree English exemption for the MSc B2 graduation obligation was found: ask whether English-medium BA evidence is accepted. UChicago study does not waive Italian B2. PhD no standardized English certificate requirement identified, so no verified UChicago-specific waiver application. [s1] [s3] [s4] [Standing rule] PhD funded competitions accept suitable foreign degrees and international candidates. DSU explicitly open to all nationalities, for the first qualification at the relevant level; prior master's holders ineligible for master's-level DSU. Non-EU family income/assets require originals, Italian translations and prescribed legalization. UChicago attendance does not determine citizenship, country-of-origin fee category or financial independence. INdAM citizenship/foreign-degree eligibility remains unverified. [s4] [s11] [s13] [s14]",
    "costs": "[Prior cycle] PRIOR PhD application fee €30 per doctoral course via PagoPA, one payment covers multiple math selections, due closing date 23:59; generally nonrefundable. MSc separate application fee not established. Prior tuition maximum €2,900/year, plus regional tax €140 and initial stamp €16; country-of-origin flat rates €290/€580/€1,160/€2,900 for low/lower-middle/upper-middle/high-income categories. First-year non-EU visa tuition schedule: regional/stamp by 31 December 2026, then 30% by 1 February 2027, 25% by 1 March, 25% by 15 April, 20% by 31 May. Italian tests cost €35 written + €35 oral, if needed. CIMEA/translation/visa costs separate; 2027-28 amounts unknown. [s3] [s4] [s7] [s9] [s10]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Neither GRE General nor GRE Mathematics appears in the inspected MSc requirements or PhD mathematics selection checklist. This establishes no listed requirement; consideration or prohibition of unsolicited scores is not stated. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Neither GRE General nor GRE Mathematics appears in the inspected MSc requirements or PhD mathematics selection checklist. This establishes no listed requirement; consideration or prohibition of unsolicited scores is not stated. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PhD: at least two names and email/telephone contacts of mathematics academics/scholars willing to provide confidential references; they upload letters under emailed instructions. MSc ordinary admission: none listed. INdAM scholarship reference count unverified. [s2] [s5] [s14]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] PhD MATE01_A asks for a brief motivation paragraph inside the CV, maximum one page, explaining why applying to the mathematics PhD at Pisa (English rendering of Italian prompt; see selection-sheet page 3 for original wording). Restricted selections ask why applying for that specific topic under its named supervisor. This is not an additional unrestricted multi-page SOP. MSc no standalone SOP prompt found. [s2] [s5]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] International fee pages show 18 December 2027 for an installment among 2026-27 payments; the reduction table instead has 18 December 2026. Its low-income row says €80 where listed total €290 and 30% would imply €87; late-reduction row even says 31 November. These are source defects, not reliable deadlines; use individual Alice assessment and written clarification. Pardini roster says affiliate while personal CV says full professor present. General PhD guide mentions optional proposals, but mathematics sheet does not require one. INdAM source inaccessible, so eligibility/amount not inferred. [s5] [s7] [s9] [s10] [s14] [s16]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Obtain 2027 calls, Italian test calendar, scholarship dates and amounts. Ask mathematics office whether UChicago BA satisfies PhD second-cycle equivalence; otherwise use MSc. Confirm UChicago English evidence acceptance, Italian exemptions, required certified translations, referee trigger/receipt/reuse, application fee waiver, and interview language. Retrieve INdAM full legal conditions and award amount. Verify Pardini supervision status and Sala sabbatical availability. Resolve tuition-page date/arithmetic typos using formal fee assessment. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s8] [s10] [s14] [s16]",
