    "deadlineDetails": "[Unresolved] Winter 2027-28 MSc dates are not yet published. For orientation only, non-EU winter 2026 applications ran June 22-August 3, 2026. Explicit summer 2027 window: November 16, 2026-January 7, 2027; this is unsuitable if your bachelor will only finish later in 2027. No cutoff clock was established. Doctoral academic applications are accepted year-round; job deadlines are separate. [s3] [s9] [s30]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No guaranteed MSc annual stipend found. Current Mellit job quotes EUR3776.10/month gross at full time, paid14 times/year; the advertised appointment is30 hours/week. If prorated to75% of a40-hour week, arithmetic is EUR2832.075/month and EUR39649.05/year gross, subject to payroll rounding/contract confirmation. This is the 2026 advertisement, not a guaranteed Fall 2027 rate or offer. [s11] [s12] [s15]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] MSc: UChicago mathematics bachelor is assessed individually, with no advance equivalence ruling. Subject gaps may require up to30 ECTS of supplementary exams within two semesters; larger gaps preclude admission. Crucially, the degree must already be fully completed when applying to this programme without selection procedure: future-completion letters and provisional transcripts are not accepted. Doctorate normally requires a relevant master or qualification at the same level, plus a supervisor; no assured direct route from the UChicago bachelor was established. [s1] [s4] [s7] [s9]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Wait until the bachelor is completed, obtain final records or an official completion confirmation, prepare English evidence, create a u:account and apply through u:space. US-issued educational documents need no diplomatic legalisation; English records need no translation. Later doctorate: obtain supervision confirmation and project agreement in principle before academic application; apply separately to funded jobs. [s2] [s4] [s6] [s9] [s10]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc requires B2 English, not German. Accepted degree evidence: completed full-time programme of at least two years, entirely English-taught, at an institution in the US or another listed country. Tests valid no more than three years: published TOEFL iBT94 or IELTS Academic6.5; the page still uses the legacy TOEFL scale. Doctoral guidance generally expects C1 English/German depending on the project. [s1] [s5] [s9] [s30] [Standing rule] A completed English-taught UChicago bachelor satisfies the published educational-evidence route, with diploma/completion evidence and transcript. It also meets the same degree-based C1 evidence rule where applicable. F-1 status alone is irrelevant to the exemption. [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] VSM advertises international recruitment; no citizenship exclusion appears in the examined post. Master equivalence and employment/residence permissions still matter. Austrian statutory student aid/merit schemes have citizenship or equal-status rules; US F-1 status does not establish eligibility. [s11] [s12] [s16]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] No mathematics application charge was established in the public checklist; do not infer one from tuition. Current ordinary non-EU tuition is EUR726.72 plus EUR26.20 student-union contribution per semester, totalEUR752.92;2027 changes remain possible. These are enrollment/study charges, not application fees. [s2] [s14]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] No GRE General requirement or recommendation is listed in the MSc curriculum/application checklist or general doctoral academic procedure. Individual funded-job conditions remain separate. [s2] [s7] [s9]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] No GRE Mathematics requirement or recommendation is listed in the MSc curriculum/application checklist or the examined Mellit position. [s2] [s7] [s13]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Ordinary MSc: none listed. Ordinary doctoral academic admission requires the supervisor-confirmation form rather than a standard three-letter packet. Mellit funded job5204 requires two recommendation letters. [s2] [s7] [s9] [s13]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No ordinary MSc motivation essay listed. Later doctoral academic admission: maximum 1 page explaining research interests, motivation for the project and why Vienna. Mellit job separately asks for a motivation letter without a published length limit. These are paraphrases; full instructions are linked. [s2] [s7] [s9] [s13]",
    "warnings": "[Unresolved] General doctoral guidance gives C1 language expectations; mathematics emphasizes an English research environment. A new programme-specific test-certificate decision remains necessary. Some older Vienna webpages redirect to a maintenance notice; current central pages and institutional research records were used instead. Historical VSM entrants with a bachelor listed do not establish a general bachelor-to-PhD admission entitlement. [s5] [s9] [s10] [s30]",
