    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[Conflict] Doctoral department admits on a rolling basis, but university-scholarship applicants must submit course application by 7 December 2026, 16:59 GMT. Central 2027 deadline for applicants needing a visa is 2 August 2027; department FAQ advises unfunded visa applicants by end of June. Treat June as the safer planning target and ask about the discrepancy. MSc central on-time deadline is 2 August 2027; late consideration is discretionary, not guaranteed. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s10]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] Department: full tuition plus published annual stipend £21,805 for 2027/28, laptop, £2,000 travel and £2,000 third-year study-visit support. Figure is quoted exactly from the opened department page, not silently replaced by a different indexed figure or an assumed UKRI rate; payment frequency and health/visa cover not stated. Central Chancellor’s streams: UKRI-rate stipend (2027 cash amount not independently fixed here), full fees, £5,000 research/training support; possible international immigration-cost assistance. MSc has no general stipend guarantee established. [s4] [s5]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] MSc: first-class-equivalent mathematics or mathematically intensive science bachelor’s. PhD: first-class integrated four-year master’s or first-class bachelor’s plus distinction-level MSc, or overseas equivalent. A US four-year bachelor’s is not explicitly guaranteed to meet the integrated-master’s requirement; ask for individual equivalence before relying on direct entry. MSc is the clearly documented bachelor’s-entry route. F-1 status does not determine UK admission or Home fee status. Programme begins 4 October 2027; PhD initially registers as MPhil with first-year upgrade. [s1] [s9]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Review preparation against Warwick fourth-year mathematics; choose one-year MSc or diploma plus MSc if further preparation needed. PhD: identify interests and possible supervisors; prior supervisor agreement is not required. Apply to Mathematics Institute, postgraduate research, code P-G1P4. For university funding submit course application first, wait for seven-digit ID (up to 48 hours), register ITS, then submit separate scholarship form. [s1] [s2] [s6] [s14]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Band A for both routes: IELTS 6.5 overall, minimum 6.0 each component, or accepted equivalent. Tests must be within two years and one month of course start; use most recent result. [s1] [s8] [s9] [Standing rule] Potential degree-based satisfaction: entire degree taught in English in a UKVI-recognised majority-English-speaking country and completed within two years four months before course start. A recent UChicago degree fits the published country/medium pattern, but the department retains discretion and may impose an English condition. Confirm exact graduation timing and provide transcript/degree evidence. [s8] [2027 confirmed] Department studentships explicitly open to overseas students and cover full overseas fees, but international places are limited by cost. Chancellor’s competitions welcome all nationalities. CSC requires its nationality/status eligibility; US Fulbright citizenship is not conferred by US study/F-1. Sanctuary relates to UK protection/asylum status, not ordinary F-1 status. [s4] [s5]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] PhD research application: no assessment fee. Taught master’s: £75, non-refundable, payable before submission unless waiver approved. [s3] [s10] [s11]",
    "size": "The PhD course page describes more than 100 postgraduate students and almost 100 mathematics academics. University enrollment category not verified.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] Not listed in Mathematics PhD/MSc entry or application requirements; no official instruction found saying scores are considered, forbidden, or beneficial. Do not treat absence as a recommendation to submit. [s1] [s2] [s9]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] Not listed in Mathematics PhD/MSc entry or application requirements; no official instruction found saying scores are considered, forbidden, or beneficial. Do not treat absence as a recommendation to submit. [s1] [s2] [s9]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] PhD: two academic references. MSc: normally one academic reference. As a recent full-time undergraduate, use academics who directly taught or supervised your academic work; friends, peers, relatives and school teachers are not accepted. [s1] [s7] [s9]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] A personal/academic statement is required. Faithful paraphrase: explain preparation, interests and motivation for this course. Central taught-course advice suggests approximately one to two pages, English and own words; this is not established as a hard PhD limit. Upload; exact file format/size unverified. [s2] [s10] [s12]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Programme checklist says research proposal while mathematics FAQ says no detailed proposal needed and permits personal-statement reuse; follow the specific mathematical clarification. Central August visa deadline differs from department June advice. Scholarship deferred-letter email exception differs from generic no-email policy. Department stipend direct page states £21,805; do not substitute conflicting search-index snippets. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6] [s7]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Ask postgradmaths@warwick.ac.uk whether a UChicago BA with advanced courses qualifies directly for the integrated-master’s-equivalent PhD threshold; otherwise plan MSc. Confirm 2027 supervisor capacity, English degree waiver, ordinary reference receipt/update mechanics, any offer acceptance dates, and actual award letter stipend/visa coverage. Obtain the live portal writing/upload limits before drafting final files. [s1] [s4] [s8] [s13]",
