    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] US EEF HDAP fall 2027: 15 January 2027, 6 pm EST. Strasbourg’s 30 April 2027 EEF date is the university review deadline, not the student submission deadline. Other 2027 master calendars are pending; faculty says eCandidat dates will appear in February 2027. DU MARI: 30 April 2027, time/timezone unpublished. PhD 2027 competition dates are unpublished; prior 2026 applications closed 19 May. [s2] [s5] [s8] [s12]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] Mobil’ITI: €7,000 net over 10 months (€700/month). Eligible incoming students may receive €500 installation plus travel reimbursement up to €2,000 when travel exceeds 4,000 km, or €1,000 below that distance; maximum €9,500. Existing Strasbourg higher-education students do not receive travel/installation benefits. ED269 requires funding at least €1,300 net/month for the full PhD: an eligibility floor, NOT a scholarship offer. [s6] [s7] [s8]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] UChicago mathematics BA can be assessed for M1 equivalence; M2 normally requires M1 or equivalent advanced preparation, not an automatic four-year-BA entitlement. Master’s teaching is French. Doctorate normally requires a research master’s, French grade at least 12/20 or approved exception; foreign-degree equivalence needs ED approval. Direct BA-to-PhD eligibility is not established. International status is permitted; F-1 confers no French immigration or EU fee status. [s1] [s2] [s8]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Identify citizenship/residence route: US-resident non-EU candidates normally use Études en France (EEF), whereas eligible EU applicants use MonMaster. Submit the exact mathematics master application before the separate DU/Mobil’ITI form; that form requires its application number. For PhD, obtain an HDR supervisor’s agreement, laboratory approval, research plan and funding before Amethis enrolment. [s2] [s6] [s8] [s12]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Master: French B2, not an English-medium programme. ED269 doctorate: French OR English B2. No IELTS/TOEFL minimum or specific English test mandate was found in the checked mathematics/ED pages. [s1] [s2] [s8] [Unresolved] An English-medium UChicago degree does not establish French B2 or a master French-test exemption. For PhD, whether the degree itself documents English B2 needs ED confirmation; no automatic UChicago-specific waiver is published. [s2] [s8] [Standing rule] Mobil’ITI is open to eligible international applicants selected for an associated master and DU; geography affects relocation benefits, not automatic entitlement. Doctoral foreign degrees need equivalence and a funded supervisor/project. Citizenship-specific external scholarship eligibility must be checked separately. [s5] [s7] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] Campus France USA full admissions processing US$460; already-admitted pre-consular processing US$270 is a different route. No separate mathematics application fee established. Current form gives PRIOR 2026-27 master registration €255 for listed exempt/national-fee groups versus €3,950 for other international students, plus DU €167; 2027-28 rates/CVEC not established. These are tuition/registration, not application fees. [s6] [s13]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not listed in the checked master, DU or doctoral requirements; no published requirement or invitation to upload GRE scores was found. Treat as not requested on those checklists, not a verified prohibition. [s1] [s6] [s8]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Not listed in the checked master, DU or doctoral requirements; no published requirement or invitation to upload GRE scores was found. Treat as not requested on those checklists, not a verified prohibition. [s1] [s6] [s8]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] DU/Mobil’ITI: at least TWO professor contact details; this is not a requirement to upload two letters initially. EEF broadly recommends one or two references, but the mathematics master’s mandatory count is not publicly established. Doctoral-contract dossier asks recommendations without a fixed published count. [s6] [s8] [s12]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Master motivation advice (paraphrase): explain course/institution changes and concrete reasons for this programme and its courses. EEF motivation text maximum 2,500 characters, in French for French-taught programmes. DU motivation letter required; one upload, 10 MB maximum, no published word/page/font limit. [s3] [s6] [s12]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] New DU form renewal 6-10 months conflicts with older scholarship page maximum 6 months. Legacy IRMA eCandidat link does not supersede the faculty’s EEF route rule. IRMA AGA roster still lists Christine Noot-Huyghe, while current official journal/publisher sources place Christine Huyghe at Besançon; she is excluded as an ordinary Strasbourg adviser pending clarification. [s2] [s4] [s6] [s7] [s10] [s15]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm citizenship/residence routing, 2027 M2 theme, French proof, master references and course-description needs; inspect scholarship DOCX; obtain 2027 fees and written award renewal terms. For doctorate, confirm master equivalence, HDR supervisor, current funding offer and full 2027 competition calendar. Several long-standing members have no recent paper metadata on checked official pages and are explicitly flagged below. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s6] [s8]",
