    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing September-entry calendar: opens October 1; scholarship applicants February 1, non-EU passport holders April 1, EU passport holders June 1, all 23:59 CET/CEST. The routine programme table does not explicitly label the year; for September 2027 these are the standing calendar dates, not an independently dated 2027 call. February-entry calendar: opens July 1; non-EU September 1, EU October 15. The live PhD closes November 15, 2026 (hour unstated). [admit] [phd]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] No automatic MSc stipend. NL Scholarship offers €5,000/€10,000/€15,000 only in the first year, including for two-year programmes; remaining costs must be funded. Current mathematics PhD example pays €3,204 gross/month in year 1 up to €4,051 in year 4 at 38 hours, plus 8% holiday and 8.3% year-end bonus, pension benefits and research travel support; not a guaranteed 2027 offer. [nl] [phd]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Selective MSc: mathematics bachelor, or related degree with substantial mathematics, individually compared with Utrecht preparation. UChicago BA potentially qualifies. Requires real analysis, linear algebra and probability, plus advanced work in at least three listed areas (including complex/functional analysis, geometry/topology, algebra/number theory, logic and others). Motivation and academic performance matter. Direct BA-to-PhD is not established: the live mathematics PhD explicitly requires completed/nearly completed MSc. [admit] [phd]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Register in Studielink, then complete OSIRIS documents, referee invitations and fee. Credentials may take up to two working days. Obtain UChicago’s signed/stamped anticipated-degree statement if still studying. Apply separately for NL Scholarship after academic application. No MSc supervisor agreement prerequisite listed. [admit] [anticipated] [nl]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] EMI-experienced: IELTS Academic 6.5 overall/6.0 each; pre-January 21, 2026 TOEFL iBT 93/20 each; later TOEFL scale overall 4.5, speaking 4/listening 4.5/reading 4.5/writing 4. Cambridge C1 176/169 each or C2 180/169 each. IELTS/TOEFL maximum two years old. TOEFL Home accepted; IELTS Online, One Skill Retake and TOEFL MyBest rejected. [eng] [Standing rule] Yes for a fully English-taught bachelor or master obtained in the United States. After conditional admission, provide certified degree/transcript establishing the exemption. Admissions gives the binding decision during formal assessment, not by a pre-application email. [eng] [faq] [2027 confirmed] NL Scholarship: non-EU/EEA passport, ineligible for Dutch study finance/statutory tuition, no earlier Dutch institutional enrolment except exchange, eligible September 2027 programme. Mathematics expressly lists it. F-1 status alone does not establish these conditions. [nl] [tuition]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] €100 nonrefundable application fee, paid in OSIRIS after uploads by Visa/Mastercard/Amex; valid for three years and covers multiple programme applications. 2027-28 tuition €26,100/year non-EU/EEA; €2,771 statutory-eligible full-time students. Individual nationality/residence exceptions apply. [fee] [tuition]",
