    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] SI: 16 October 2026, 14:00 to 15 December 2026, 14:00 Paris time. Signed calendar controls the website typo. Shortlist from 27 January 2027; test invitations 28 January-2 March; interviews 3-19 March; results from 26 March. CNE 2027 not published: previous cycle 9 March-24 April 2026, 14:00 (page does not separately specify timezone). The separate EEF January deadline is not an ENS SI deadline; ENS uses its own competition, followed by pre-consular formalities if needed. [s1] [s3] [s6] [s26]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] SI €1,000/month for 36 months (€12,000 per full 12-month year, arithmetic). Room access is not free housing; rent TBD and August closure. PSL master 2026 grant €1,200/month for ten months (€12,000 total), conditional second-year renewal. PSL doctorate 2026 indicative gross €2,300/month (€27,600/12 months, arithmetic), registration fees still payable. No 2027 PhD salary confirmed. Separate PGSM published rate is €1,150/month: M1 first year €13,800/12 months; M2 €12,650/11 months, or €13,800 with the specified twelfth-month condition (totals calculated). Published rules include registration/social coverage, CROUS housing reservation and annual economy home-country return travel for international recipients; a reservation is not free rent. Do not assume combination with ENS SI is allowed. [s2] [s4] [s8] [s9] [s21] [s22]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] SI Sciences: potentially eligible with UChicago study, subject to age under 26 on opening day; at least one foreign university year completed when applying and two at enrolment; no previous SI attempt; French secondary/higher-education registration no more than six months total during the competition academic year and preceding year. Exceptional cases require director approval. Master/DENS entry, not a bachelor-to-PhD offer. Later doctorate needs M2/equivalent and an HDR supervisor. Age and prior France study remain unverified. [s1] [s9]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose Mathematics in SI and request referees through OnePSL30. CNE is a separate alternative; exceptional M1-level entry requires checking department placement. SI selection includes remote scientific and motivation interviews; use the FAQ and prior jury reports to prepare. Campus France does not transmit SI applications; visa processing follows admission. For ordinary ENS/PSL master admission, PSL also directs applicants to the academic portal first, then EEF pre-consular processing after acceptance. Dauphine-hosted programmes are the stated exception requiring both portals. Do not import the January EEF full-admissions deadline into ENS International Selection. [s1] [s2] [s6] [s26]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] SI Sciences has no officially prescribed language level. Interviews may be in French or English. French lessons are available; pure-math M1 teaching is French in the PSL grant notice. [s2] [s8] [Standing rule] No UChicago-specific waiver needed under the SI rule above; this does not establish an English-taught curriculum or waive any separate master requirement. [s2] [Standing rule] SI is expressly an international selection. PSL master and doctoral calls admit international candidates. F-1 status itself is not French residence permission; citizenship and visa requirements need individual checking. PGSM international call is for students studying outside France; UChicago meets that location condition, subject to other call rules. [s4] [s8] [s9] [s21]",
    "costs": "[Unresolved] SI application fee not established publicly. Registration fees are required but FAQ amount is awaiting update. Do not label application free from silence. For an accepted US-resident applicant who needs Campus France pre-consular processing, the regular charge is US$270; US$460 is the different full-admissions route and must not be added automatically to ENS SI. Waiver/visa costs remain situation-dependent. [s2] [s19] [s20] [s24] [s26]",
