    "deadlineDetails": "[Standing rule] Standing MSc windows: mid-November-15 December and 16 December-31 March, autumn start only; exact year/clock/timezone not shown in application page. For 2027 entry, Excellence explicitly requires the first window (December 15, i.e. December 2026 by cycle inference). EDMA standing cutoffs: 1 December, 15 April, 15 September; no cycle-specific clock/timezone published. Complete letters by chosen EDMA cutoff. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s7]",
    "funding": "[Prior cycle] MSc Excellence CHF 10,000 per semester (arithmetic CHF 20,000 for two semesters), paid each semester; student pays tuition, rent and insurance from it. Mathematics is 90 ECTS, normally max three funded semesters. Room reservation is offered, not free housing. Doctoral assistant 2026 gross salary CHF 55,225 year 1, 56,225 year 2, 57,225 year 3, 58,225 years 4-6, including thirteenth salary month; 2027 rate not yet established. [s1] [s5] [s6] [s10] [s11]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Conflict] MSc: UChicago mathematics bachelor’s can be considered with excellent records; prerequisites may be added. EDMA normally requires master’s/equivalent. Central FAQ permits four/five-year bachelor’s applicants who explain preparation; EDMA’s exception mentions excellent four-year bachelor’s from other mathematically intensive domains. Whether a UChicago math BA qualifies directly is not unambiguously established - seek EDMA equivalence advice; MSc is the straightforward route. Same/similar-field master’s holders cannot apply for another MSc; Excellence excludes existing master’s holders. [s1] [s2] [s7] [s9]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] MSc: choose one programme per academic year, scan documents, arrange three professors, select Excellence checkbox, pay and validate online. Visa-needing applicants should use December window. EDMA: study groups/openings, choose relevant prospective advisers and obtain three writers; final enrolment needs a supervisor, topic and secured funding. No account or application was created for this research. [s2] [s3] [s7] [s8]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] MSc mathematics is taught in English with some optional French; EPFL recommends C1 in teaching language, but language test certificates are optional. EDMA encourages TOEFL if native language neither English nor French; no mandatory minimum score found. French is not necessary to begin PhD. [s1] [s3] [s7] [s9] [s12] [Standing rule] MSc has no mandatory language-test certificate to waive. EDMA recommendation is based on native language, not solely English-medium degree; no explicit UChicago/US-degree waiver of that recommendation found. Explain English-medium undergraduate study and confirm whether EDMA wants a test; do not call it required. [s3] [s7] [s9] [Standing rule] MSc Excellence explicitly open internationally and external graduates may receive room reservation. Doctoral assistant employment/funding is available to foreign applicants subject to admission/work permission; external home-country scholarships must be supplemented to institutional income-equivalent level under policy. US F-1 does not establish Swiss permit or fee status. [s5] [s6] [s8] [s10]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] MSc application CHF 150 for foreign bachelor’s, non-refundable; card/PayPal/Twint, paid before validation. Doctoral application free; foreign-degree doctoral registration CHF 150 and completion tax CHF 1,500 are separate. Current MSc semester invoice normally CHF 2,240 for foreign students relocating for study (CHF 2,190 tuition + CHF 50 charges), with nationality/residence exceptions; confirm individual classification. [s3] [s9] [s15] [s18]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] MSc GRE optional, welcomed, and explicitly has no influence on Excellence scholarship evaluation. EDMA checklist highly recommends GRE and central FAQ identifies General GRE as recommended, not required. Code 3253, no department code; notify programme if sending official results. [s3] [s6] [s7] [s9]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No distinct Mathematics Subject GRE requirement established. EDMA says GRE without specifying subject; central FAQ clarifies General GRE. Ask EDMA whether a Math Subject result is useful before interpreting generic recommendation as a subject-test requirement. MSc optional GRE upload is allowed but subject-specific preference unverified. [s3] [s7] [s9]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] MSc: enter three academic professor referees familiar with work; at least two received letters needed for processing, but three requested. Swiss-degree exemptions do not cover UChicago. EDMA: three confidential recommendations, each questionnaire plus letter, all required for complete file. [s3] [s8]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] MSc required SOP ≤1,000 words; faithful paraphrase: academic background, career strategy and precise objectives for EPFL study. Upload within application; font/spacing/page limit unverified. EDMA required objectives statement, unprotected PDF ≤2 MB; exact word/page limit not published on EDMA page (do not import EDIC computer-science two-page rule). [s3] [s7]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Excellence main page expressly removes second-window eligibility for 2027, while FAQ still mentions June second-round notification; follow December-only current rule. General doctoral four-year BA eligibility is broader than EDMA exception language. MSc final-record September 30 outer limit does not override requirement to have records before matriculation. Fellowship stacking wording differs: no substantial combined award versus individual review. [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s7] [s9] [s13]",
