    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] 2027/28 main round: 1 December 2026. Clearing round: 31 March 2027, subject to places remaining. The mathematics listing does not specify a clock time for ordinary main/clearing applications; CUHK’s HKPFS full application explicitly closes 1 December 2026 at 23:59 Hong Kong time. Application opens 1 September 2026. [s1] [s4] [s9]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] Regular PGS: published 2026/27 annual amount HK$229,200; no 2027/28 regular rate is confirmed. It is financial assistance, not a quoted net-after-tuition salary. 2027/28 tuition is HK$49,500 annually unless separately waived. HKPFS 2027/28: HK$344,400 annual stipend plus HK$14,400 annual research-travel allowance; CUHK additionally lists tuition waiver, lodging award HK$40,000 first year/HK$20,000 subsequent years, and first-year hostel-fee waiver. Published maximum package exceeds HK$1.81m over four years, not per year. Health/other fee coverage is not fully specified. [s6] [s7] [s9] [s13]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] A UChicago mathematics bachelor’s can support application to either stream of this articulated MPhil-PhD, subject to CUHK equivalence and academic review. The bachelor’s route normally requires honours at least Second Class, or an honours programme averaging at least B; do not apply the separate standalone-PhD master’s requirement to Mathematics. Final-year students can apply before graduating. Mathematics or a related major is expected and an interview may be required. Nonlocal applicants follow the same academic process; U.S. F-1 status does not substitute for Hong Kong student immigration permission. GPA and completion date remain unverified. [s1] [s2] [s5] [s15]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Select MPhil versus PhD stream and intended mathematical area; verify degree equivalence, prepare official transcript scans and grading legend, obtain a UChicago Registrar English-medium letter, and ask academic referees in advance. Public rules do not establish a mandatory prior supervisor agreement. For HKPFS first obtain the RGC reference number, then submit CUHK’s separate full application and any HKPFS supplement. RGC permits two ranked programme choices; priority changes stop at its initial deadline. Submit early enough to activate referees after submission. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s9] [s10] [s13] [s17]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] A degree taught in English satisfies the general English requirement. Otherwise current listed alternatives include TOEFL iBT 79/120 or 4.5/6, IELTS Academic 6.5, or specified GMAT verbal scores. TOEFL Home Edition and IELTS Online are listed as accepted; scores are normally valid two years (GMAT five). The FAQ rejects TOEFL MyBest and IELTS One Skill Retake. Programme-specific additional requirements take precedence. [s2] [s5] [Standing rule] Likely satisfied through UChicago’s English-medium bachelor’s, conditional on the degree and documentation: central instructions require a Registry certifying letter confirming English as the programme’s medium. Obtain that letter rather than relying only on U.S. location or F-1 status. The older Mathematics page uses a narrower native-English-country formulation; current Graduate School documentation is clearer and should control, subject to confirmation in the application. [s2] [s3] [s15] [Standing rule] Nonlocal applicants can receive PGS, Vice-Chancellor and HKPFS awards. HKPFS is open regardless of nationality; F-1 is not a nationality. The government local-student research tuition-waiver scheme is not automatically available to an international applicant. Belt and Road awards depend on qualifying citizenship/region, which is unknown here. [s7] [s9] [s10] [s14]",
    "costs": "[Conflict] HK$500 per programme application under current Graduate School instructions, paid online by credit card, non-refundable/non-transferable. The departmental page’s HK$300 is older and conflicts; budget the current HK$500. Multiple programme applications require separate fees. RGC’s initial HKPFS application itself has no application fee. [s5] [s6] [s10] [s15]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] No General GRE requirement is listed in the current Mathematics programme or general graduate requirements. Public evidence does not establish whether an unsolicited General GRE is ignored, accepted, or considered; do not label it prohibited. [s1] [s2] [s15]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] The current Mathematics programme explicitly says the GRE Subject Test in Mathematics may be required in some cases. It gives neither a universal requirement nor an exemption for UChicago graduates, and no score minimum. Ask rpg.math@cuhk.edu.hk whether your application will require it before relying on an untested application. [s1]",
    "letters": "[Conflict] Current Graduate School checklist: three referees for research doctoral applications, two for other applications (therefore three for Mathematics PhD and two for MPhil). The older Mathematics page still says two, creating a conflict; prepare three for the doctoral stream and confirm the portal’s actual requirement. [s3] [s15]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] Statement of purpose: not separately listed in the public Mathematics programme/department admissions or central documents checklist. Requirement versus optionality, exact prompt, length, formatting, and upload-versus-link rules remain unverified in the current application. Public silence is not proof that the live application omits this item. For HKPFS, also inspect its distinct supplement before drafting. [s1] [s3] [s15] [s16] [s18]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current central fee HK$500 versus departmental HK$300; central three doctoral references versus departmental two; current HKPFS 2026 deadline versus stale FAQ 2025 date and older department funding. Departmental native-English-country wording differs from the central English-medium-degree route. Michael McBreen’s research-profile heading says Associate Professor while biographical/department text still says Assistant Professor. Old pages list Jiu-Kang Yu (now HIMIS), Xuhua He (now HKU), and Luen-Fai Tam (former faculty through 2024); they are not treated as ordinary current CUHK advisers. Shing-Tung Yau’s visiting role and Tom Wan’s emeritus role need separate supervision verification. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s6] [s9] [s15] [s16] [s23] [s31] [s32] [s33] [s34] [s35]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Before drafting/submitting: obtain current Mathematics portal prompts and any HKPFS supplement; confirm three PhD reports, invitation timing, actual letter cut-off, receipt indicators and update/reuse rules; ask whether Math GRE is required in your case; confirm fee-waiver possibilities, degree/English-medium documentation and qualification-verification procedure; obtain a written 2027 funding offer with tuition, summer, housing and other-fee details; check adviser availability. Current public sources do not resolve these points, and no invented portal wording or 2027 regular stipend is supplied. [s1] [s3] [s5] [s7] [s9] [s15] [s18]",
