    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Fall September 2027: 1 June 2027 for nonlocal full-time Mathematics MPhil/PhD; ordinary deadline clock time is not stated in the catalogue. Rolling review means earlier is preferable. Applications opened 1 September 2026. HKPFS full application: 1 December 2026, 23:59 HKT/GMT+8. Spring February 2027 nonlocal deadline was 1 November 2026 and is already past as of this report. [s1] [s10] [s36]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] 2027/28 admissions flyer quotes regular PGS HK$229,620/year (HK$19,135/month by division by 12); tuition HK$49,500/year is normally paid from it unless separately waived. HKPFS: HK$344,400/year stipend plus HK$14,400/year travel, four-year tuition waiver, RedBird HK$40,000 recruitment award first year and HK$20,000/year subsequent excellence awards subject to renewal. Approximate HK$1.7m is a four-year package, not annual cash. No universal health/other-fee waiver was established; housing is guaranteed first year, not advertised as free. [s8] [s10] [s12] [s14]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] Both MPhil and direct PhD are open to a recognized bachelor’s graduate. PhD entry additionally requires outstanding undergraduate performance or satisfactory postgraduate work (at least one year full-time/two part-time). Final-year applicants may receive conditional offers. UChicago’s degree therefore provides an eligible route, conditional on academic assessment and completion; no published numerical Mathematics GPA threshold was found. A nonlocal student requiring a Hong Kong student visa cannot take part-time research study. U.S. F-1 status does not authorize Hong Kong residence. [s1] [s10] [s11]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Identify research fit, choose MPhil or PhD, prepare full tertiary records/grade legend and an official English-medium degree letter, secure academic referee consent, and draft the mandatory research fields. There is no published Mathematics requirement for a supervisor’s prior agreement. For HKPFS obtain an RGC reference first, then tick the HKPFS option and enter the matching number in HKUST’s application. Separate programmes require separate applications, fees, uploads and invitations; no automatic PhD-to-MPhil fallback is promised. [s4] [s5] [s6] [s8] [s11] [s12]",
    "international": "[2027 confirmed] 2027/28 minimums: TOEFL iBT 80 for tests before 21 January 2026 or 4.5 for tests from that date; IELTS Academic 6.5 overall with each component at least 5.5. Scores must come from one sitting; home-test options are not accepted. The English first-language or English-medium bachelor’s exception is explicit. Admission waiver does not remove all post-enrolment language obligations: full-time research students take a speaking assessment and may need LANG 5000. [s1] [s10] [s14] [Standing rule] UChicago’s English-medium bachelor’s should qualify under the explicit degree exception, subject to completion and official evidence. Upload an official institutional letter confirming English as the bachelor’s medium of instruction; U.S. location/F-1 alone is not the specified proof. The central FAQ also recognizes an English-medium master’s, but that is unnecessary for the assumed UChicago route. [s1] [s4] [s8] [Standing rule] PGS and HKPFS are available to nonlocal/international applicants. RedBird’s advertised international award depends on the University’s classification; citizenship is not established by F-1. AFLSP is for nonlocal students from Asia entering a full-time master’s; a UChicago degree alone does not establish Asian eligibility. Local-government tuition waiver requires qualifying Hong Kong local status. [s10] [s12] [s14] [s15]",
    "costs": "[2027 confirmed] HK$180 per MPhil/PhD application. Current instructions allow Visa/Mastercard, Alipay or WeChat Pay; a consenting third party’s card may be used. Each programme requires its own fee. Wait for payment acknowledgement before closing the session. [s1] [s6] [s8]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[2027 confirmed] Not required by the current Mathematics programme: the general checklist requires GRE only when specified by a programme, and Mathematics lists no GRE condition. Whether voluntarily submitted General GRE scores influence review is not stated. [s1] [s4] [s8]",
    "greMath": "[2027 confirmed] No Mathematics Subject GRE is required in the current programme catalogue or department application checklist. Neither a recommendation nor a prohibition on voluntary submission was found. This differs from CUHK’s case-by-case Math GRE rule. [s1] [s2] [s4]",
    "letters": "[2027 confirmed] At least two academic referees; the system allows two to five. Use institutional email addresses and obtain consent. The current guide permits additional recommendation-letter files in additional documents, but the FAQ says reports/letters are considered through the online system only; this does not authorize paper mailing. [s4] [s6] [s8]",
    "writing": "[Conflict] The Mathematics department explicitly lists a statement of purpose among application materials, whereas the central FAQ calls a personal statement optional. Treat the department’s SOP as requested and ask whether the mandatory research/vision text satisfies it or a separate upload is wanted. No Mathematics SOP prompt, word/page limit or formatting rule is public; do not import undergraduate 500-word advice. [s2] [s4] [s8]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Central FAQ says personal statement optional while Mathematics lists an SOP; clarify whether separate upload is expected. FAQ has two contradictory HKPFS tuition answers: the dedicated HKPFS section says four-year waiver, an older funding answer says pay; current 2027 flyer and main scholarship page confirm waiver. Detailed HKPFS tips say reports on/before 8Dec 2026 23:59HKT while FAQ says best before. Department catalogue calls Tianling Jin Associate Professor, current roster Professor. Fong’s institutional paper title has “Symmetric”; publisher gives “Symmetry”. Historical Chang and emeritus pages are not reliable current adviser rosters. [s1] [s2] [s8] [s12] [s13] [s14] [s20] [s28] [s29] [s32] [s33]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm the separate Mathematics SOP delivery/limit; current full research-plan and four vision-question text/limits (only experience/topic/additional limits are exposed in current guide); referee report update/reuse policy; programme-specific final score/document cut-offs; RedBird citizenship classification and exact award; written funding with fees/health/summer obligations; 2027 adviser capacity. AFLSP eligibility depends on citizenship and extra-reference count is not fixed publicly. [s2] [s6] [s8] [s12] [s15] [s16]",
