    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] Current 2027 booklet: postal receipt 22-26 June 2026, closing 26 June 17:00 (Japan local time inferred), now closed. It covers April 2027 and exceptional October 2026, not October 2027. Overseas couriers must arrive by deadline; a narrowly defined early-postmark exception applies to domestic registered express mail. [s1] [s2]",
    "funding": "[2027 confirmed] No guaranteed master’s/doctoral department annual stipend established. AFLSP April 2027: approximately JPY 150,000-220,000/month plus reimbursement of JPY 535,800 annual tuition and JPY 282,000 admission. Twelve-month arithmetic: JPY 1.8-2.64 million living stipend, exchange-rate dependent. MEXT 2027 master’s/PhD: JPY 144,000/145,000 monthly, plus Kyoto City’s published JPY 3,000 regional supplement; tuition/exam/admission waiver and conditional travel. [s10] [s14] [s17]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[2027 confirmed] UChicago bachelor’s normally qualifies for a master’s if complete before matriculation; a master’s or equivalent normally precedes the three-year PhD. April 2027 requires degree by 31 March 2027, so June 2027 graduation misses it. October 2027 remains a possible future route requiring next-year instructions, not the closed booklet’s October 2026 option. [s5] [s2]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Complete AAO before the school’s application period; start 2-3 months before the deadline. AAO requires an account, academic documents and SOP/research plan; it is separate from admission and funding. Identify a supervisor, await AAO permission where applicable, then contact them. Regular entrance exams require travel to Kyoto and a suitable visa; US F-1 is insufficient for Japan. [s6] [s7] [s5]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Math/RIMS regular admission includes its own English examination. Science master’s is not an English-taught program; Math says sufficient Japanese for courses/life is needed although exam questions have English versions. Forms may be completed in English. AFLSP separately expects TOEFL iBT 90/4.5 or IELTS 6.5-level English, with alternative evidence permitted. [s4] [s5] [s10] [Standing rule] No UChicago-degree waiver of Math’s English entrance exam verified. AFLSP accepts proof of an English-taught bachelor’s; the English Evaluation Form explicitly permits completed or expected English-medium degrees and requires an evaluator’s ratings/signature even for native speakers. UChicago evidence must be supplied; F-1 is not proof. [s2] [s10] [s13] [2027 confirmed] AFLSP requires one of its listed Asian citizenships, under 35, Japanese Student status; Japanese dual nationals excluded. F-1 reveals none of this. UChicago is not a designated pre-admission institution: applicant must already have passed the relevant Kyoto entrance examination for the ordinary AFLSP eligibility route. MEXT has separate nationality/birth-date rules. [s10] [s14]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] Screening fee JPY 30,000; payment via Kyoto system (credit cards usable from overseas; domestic alternatives available). Admission JPY 282,000 and tuition JPY 535,800/year, subject to change; admission due at registration, tuition normally May/November. [s2] [s18]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Unresolved] No GRE listed for Math/RIMS in the ordinary application/exam instructions. They conduct their own written/oral selection. Whether unsolicited GRE scores would be accepted or ignored is not established; no requirement should be inferred. [s2] [s4]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No GRE listed for Math/RIMS in the ordinary application/exam instructions. They conduct their own written/oral selection. Whether unsolicited GRE scores would be accepted or ignored is not established; no requirement should be inferred. [s2] [s4]",
    "letters": "[2027 confirmed] Ordinary Math/RIMS master’s checklist: no academic recommendation letter specified. Exceptional early-entry eligibility category 9: one sealed faculty letter. AAO’s published general document list also contains no academic recommendation. Scholarships have separate requirements below. [s2] [s7]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] AAO requires SOP including research plan. Optional template paraphrase: personal context, motivation for supervisor/Kyoto graduate study, previous study/research, proposed research, career plans; Japanese/English, upload. Template contains provided space but no numerical word/page limit. School admission separately requires the Math or RIMS report; AAO does not replace it. [s6] [s7] [s8] [s3]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Current AFLSP April 2027 page links a 2026-cohort application DOCX; confirm correct form/video title before submission. Its broad PDF-only instruction conflicts with its explicit JPEG-photo requirement; follow the specific exception after confirmation. AAO is mandatory for Science overseas-degree applicants despite softer central/landing wording. General university-recommended MEXT is explicitly unavailable for 2027. [s9] [s10] [s12] [s5] [s17]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm October 2027 route and next booklet, AAO timing, Japanese proficiency and adviser acceptance. Obtain corrected AFLSP form and referee questions; determine citizenship eligibility, scholarship commitment date and 2027 tuition-exemption dates. Obtain any TA/RA rate/package in writing; no funding guarantee inferred. [s1] [s5] [s9] [s19] [s20]",
