    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] August 2027: 31 January 2027, with applications opening 1 October 2026. Basis: the current guide explicitly identifies August 2027 and gives the August 1 October-31 January calendar; no separate Mathematical Sciences exception is listed. Exact closing hour/time zone is not stated. January intake uses 1 June-31 July; the corresponding 2027-intake window has passed. [s3]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] NTU Research Scholarship international PhD: S$3,000/month from January 2026, plus up to S$500/month after qualifying examination, with annual tuition covered: S$36,000 or up to S$42,000 annually (12-month arithmetic). NPGS international rate S$4,300/month = S$51,600/year plus tuition; benefits include conference funding up to S$5,000 per financial year, S$500 annual books, S$1,500 one-time IT and S$600 thesis allowance. PGA international rate also S$4,300/month plus tuition and up to S$3,000 annual conference funding, but its page is for AY 2026-27. Yunqi lists S$3,000/S$3,500 before/after QE plus tuition. These are award-specific rates, not guaranteed offers or additive stipends. [s5] [s6] [s7] [s8]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Direct PhD admission accepts a mathematics bachelor's degree at Honours (Distinction) equivalent; a master's is optional. UChicago mathematics is the appropriate subject, but NTU must assess grade equivalence. International applicants are eligible. Research MSc intake is small and ad hoc; ask the intended supervisor before treating it as a fallback. F-1 status does not confer Singapore residence or establish nationality. [s1] [s2] [s26]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] SPMS advises contacting a prospective supervisor before applying, including discussion of funding. Establish degree equivalence and seek English-test waiver confirmation; prepare academic records, references, written materials and the required science video. Select the scholarship route early: NPGS closes before ordinary admission. Use the current portal. Medical examination and insurance belong to enrolment, not the initial application. [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Departmental wording requires TOEFL/IELTS from international nonnative speakers; SPMS FAQ accepts TOEFL iBT, with scores within two years, or IELTS. No current mathematics numerical minimum found. Central admission instead conditions testing on the bachelor's medium of instruction. Seek a written School ruling on that discrepancy. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [Conflict] An English-taught UChicago bachelor's fits the central medium-of-instruction exception (inference), but the department's broader nonnative-speaker wording and central case-by-case waiver FAQ prevent promising automatic exemption. Ask spms-grad@ntu.edu.sg whether the transcript suffices or a Registrar medium-of-instruction letter is required. [s1] [s3] [s4] [Conflict] Research Scholarship, NPGS, PGA and Yunqi admit international applicants. NPGS/PGA require highest-distinction-equivalent bachelor's performance; ordinary admission/Research Scholarship uses distinction equivalence. Citizenship-specific external awards cannot be assessed from F-1 status. SPMS warns MSc research support is generally unavailable, conflicting with central scholarship-level master's eligibility. [s2] [s5] [s6] [s7] [s8]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] S$50 nett per research application, nonrefundable and nontransferable; pay by Visa/Mastercard before submission. Unpaid applications are not processed. [s3]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Current Mathematics page: GRE/GATE optional; strong scores can help. SPMS FAQ strongly encourages GRE and gives 319 combined verbal/quantitative plus 3.5 analytical writing as its benchmark. A mirrored older PhD page says international applicants must submit GRE/GATE. Prefer the current divisional page but flag the contradiction to SPMS. GRE validity five years. [s1] [s2] [s10]",
    "greMath": "[Conflict] An older official PhD mirror welcomes, but does not require, the Mathematics Subject Test. Current divisional PhD page does not restate a subject-test policy; submission value/handling for 2027 is unverified. It is not established as required, forbidden, or disregarded. [s1] [s10]",
    "letters": "[Conflict] Two academic references. Central guide requires institutional email addresses, while FAQ describes them as strongly encouraged and allows academic or employer alternatives. For this applicant, two UChicago academic referees with university email addresses avoid that inconsistency. [s3] [s4]",
    "writing": "[Unresolved] No separately named mathematics statement of purpose beyond the central personal statement was identified. Use the personal-statement field for academic development, research interests and goals; whether the live portal adds a distinct SOP is unverified. [s1] [s3]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] GRE: current division optional versus older mirror required. English: central English-medium exception versus department nonnative-speaker rule. References: details-submission versus post-application invitation; current 14 working days versus obsolete 7 days. General all-documents deadline versus late-reference contact option. Institutional email mandatory versus FAQ encouraged. SPMS older stipend rates are below January 2026 central rates. MSc scholarship availability differs between SPMS and central award eligibility. GATE validity differs within the guide (three versus five years); not material unless using GATE. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s6] [s9] [s10] [s11]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Obtain SPMS confirmation of UChicago grade equivalence, English waiver evidence and Mathematics GRE submission value. Confirm current reference trigger, deadline relative to NPGS closing, scholarship report reuse and replacement rules. Inspect the portal's exact personal-statement/proposal/video prompts and limits before drafting; clarify ordinary-math proposal applicability. Confirm 2027 award values, duties, tuition/mandatory-fee coverage and any fifth-year support in the offer. Establish citizenship before fee-waiver or nationality-restricted scholarship assessment. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6]",
