    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] August 2027 PhD: application window 16 May-15 November 2026, explicitly printed in the Math poster. Exact closing hour/timezone is not published there; confirm the GradApp listing and submit early in Singapore time. January 2027: 1 January-15 May 2026, already closed. Research MSc follows the same Science standing 15 November/15 May schedule; no separately explicit 2027 MSc notice located. [s2] [s3]",
    "funding": "[Standing rule] NUS Research Scholarship international PhD rate effective1Jan 2026: SGD3000/month, plus SGD500/month after QE, with full tuition waiver (12-month arithmetic SGD36000/42000 before/after QE). Math 2027 poster additionally promises SGD500/month departmental allowance to recipients of scholarships other than PGF: if applied to RS, arithmetic becomes SGD42000/48000 per12months; have the offer confirm stacking and duration. Science Dean’s Fellowship: SGD3600/month (43200/year arithmetic) plus full tuition waiver. PGF: SGD3900/month (46800/year arithmetic), full tuition waiver, international settlingSGD1000 and one-way airfare up toSGD750; additional NUSGS monthly/research incentive amounts are not published. These alternatives are not additive scholarships. Miscellaneous student/health fees and insurance costs are not explicitly covered by the quoted tuition waiver. [s2] [s9] [s10] [s11]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Direct PhD entry is possible with a four-year mathematics honours bachelor’s or equivalent; a master’s is not mandatory. Science describes a relevant four-year degree averaging B as an example of equivalence, while its preferred honours standard is Distinction or better. UChicago mathematics education is a plausible qualifying background, subject to transcript/equivalence and competitive evaluation. MSc by Research is another route, but the department gives preference to applicants intending a PhD. F-1 is not Singapore student status; admission does not itself provide a Singapore Student’s Pass. Citizenship and final degree date still need to be supplied. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s7] [s14] [s38]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Choose PhD or research MSc; review current faculty and indicate research areas. A specific thesis topic and prior agreement from a supervisor are not mandatory under central FAQ. Gather transcript, current-student/degree evidence, passport, English-medium proof, CV, statement, and two academic referees. Select scholarship interest inside GradApp, check mandatory fields, send reference requests and pay the fee before closing. Shortlisted scholarship applicants may be interviewed. No evidence of a mandatory pre-application faculty interview. [s1] [s3] [s6] [s7]",
    "international": "[Conflict] Updated Math FAQ: TOEFL5.0 on the new scale or95 on the old iBT scale, with old-scale writing minimum 22; IELTS7.0. No corresponding new writing subsection threshold supplied. Science states two-year validity. However the explicit 2027 Math poster still prints TOEFL85/IELTS6.0, and general NUS admissions calls English tests optional whereas Math/Science FAQ requires proof if undergraduate teaching was not entirely English. Use the English-medium exemption when documented; otherwise obtain written reconciliation before selecting a test. Home editions, IELTS One Skill Retake, score combining and official-receipt grace are not established in the Math sources. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5] [Standing rule] Math and Science expressly allow documentary proof that the first degree’s instruction was100% English instead of a test. A completed UChicago degree should meet that instructional-language condition (inference), but supply official institutional evidence; USF-1 status alone is irrelevant. Exact acceptable document issuer/template and treatment of an unfinished degree are not specified; obtain a UChicago registrar English-medium letter and confirm with Math. Dean’s Fellowship likewise exempts English-taught undergraduates. [s1] [s4] [s11] [Standing rule] RS, PGF and Science Dean’s Fellowship explicitly accept all international nationalities. Citizenship-specific Commonwealth funding requires citizenship of a qualifying Commonwealth country and excludes Singapore citizens/PR; UChicago/F-1 does not determine that eligibility. Scholarships are competitive, not an automatic funding guarantee for every admitted student. [s9] [s10] [s11] [s12] [s38]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] SGD50 per application including GST, nonrefundable; must be paid by programme closing. December 2025 guide supports Visa, Mastercard, American Express or PayNow. Older guide additionally listed Alipay; use current payment screen rather than assume it remains available. [s1] [s3] [s7] [s8]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Conflict] Strongly encouraged by the current Math page and 2027 poster; central research-admissions list calls it optional and application-strengthening. Science FAQ contradicts itself: admission-requirements paragraph says compulsory, later GRE question says strongly encouraged. Treat the department’s published position as the best programme-specific evidence, but obtain written clarification if submitting without GRE. No Math-specific minimum found; do not import Statistics’320/3.5 thresholds. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5]",
    "greMath": "[Unresolved] No separate Mathematics Subject GRE requirement or recommendation established in the PhD/research-MSc pages. Their generic GRE language does not establish whether Subject scores substitute for General scores or receive consideration. Coursework-MSc rules for nonmathematics applicants are a different programme; ask Math before ordering a Subject report. [s1] [s4] [s14]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] At least two academic referees under the Math supporting-document checklist; Science specifically requires receipt of two reports. General admissions also mentions professional referees, but academic mathematics references are the programme-specific choice. Maximum accepted number and any mandated referee relationship are not publicly confirmed. [s1] [s3] [s5]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] Required statement of purpose. Prompt (faithful paraphrase): explain research interests, career aims and reasons for choosing the programme. Exact portal wording, word/page/character limit and font specifications are not public. Supporting files are PDFs; verify whether the current programme requests an upload or text box before drafting to a length. [s1] [s3] [s5]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Key official discrepancies: Science GRE compulsory paragraph versus its own encouraged FAQ and Math/central optional language; poster TOEFL85/IELTS6 versus updated Math95/7; general28-day reference invitation versus all Science documents due at programme closing; early Send to Recommender versus later after-submission invitation wording; old referee replacement instructions omitted in new guide; annual versus semester scholarship renewal;31May versus earlyJune decisions; central oversized-document mailing suggestion versus Math PDF/no-hardcopy instruction. Preserve these and verify adverse ambiguities before submission. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s7] [s8] [s9]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Urgent: complete August 2027 application by 15November 2026, confirming exact portal closing time and whether both letters must be in by then. Obtain English-medium evidence and written GRE clarification if omitting it. Inspect exact SOP/CV fields, limits, extra scholarship questions and reference receipt/update controls. Confirm stipend departmental500 stacking, fees/insurance, fifth-year support, and adviser capacity in any offer. No need to send unsolicited full papers unless the relevant supporting field permits them. [s1] [s2] [s3] [s7] [s9] [s10] [s11]",
