    "rankNote": "Canadian/Asian selection; not a US News graduate rank.",
    "deadline": null,
    "deadlineDetails": "[2027 confirmed] For 2027-28 entry: main round 1 September-1 December 2026, closing 23:59 Hong Kong Time (UTC+8). First clearing round 2 December 2026-30 April 2027, 23:59 HKT; second 1 May-31 August 2027, 23:59 HKT. Clearing applications depend on vacancies. Review can start before a round closes; use the main round. Mathematics’ own page still displays 2023-24 dates and is not the controlling 2027 calendar. [s4] [s1]",
    "funding": "[Conflict] Standard PGS, effective 1 September 2026: HKD19,135/month before PhD probation confirmation; HKD19,655/month afterward, from the following month. Twelve-month arithmetic equivalents: HKD229,620 and 235,860 gross; these are current rates, not a guaranteed 2027 rate. Tuition is separate: full-time 2027-28 HKD49,500/year. HKPFS/HKU-PS 2027-28 stipend: HKD28,700/month = HKD344,400/year, plus HKD14,400/year travel, tuition waiver, HKD40,000 cash in year1 and HKD20,000 in later normative years. Housing place is guaranteed in year1 but is not stated to be free. Medical insurance/other-fee coverage is not established. The Presidential page’s HKD445,800 year1 aggregate conflicts with its listed components, which total HKD448,300; use components pending clarification. [s10] [s12] [s13] [s16] [s18]",
    "fundingType": "Unknown",
    "overview": "[Standing rule] Eligible to seek the MPhil with a recognized honours bachelor’s or equivalent. Direct 4-year PhD requires a first-class honours bachelor’s equivalent; HKU evaluates the UChicago degree/GPA, so eligibility for that route is conditional, not automatic. A bachelor’s plus a master’s is another PhD route. The 3-year PhD normally requires a research master’s. Interviews or qualifying assessment may occur. International applicants are admitted; US F-1 status supplies no Hong Kong study permission. Complete the bachelor’s before enrollment and obtain the required Hong Kong student visa. [s2] [s3] [s16]",
    "admissions": "[Standing rule] Discuss a feasible project with a potential supervisor before applying: Science calls this necessary, and its proposal guidance says an application without a named supportive supervisor is unlikely to succeed. Obtain consent from two academic referees. Prepare PDF credentials and a Science research proposal; select the PGS funding option. For HKPFS, first obtain the RGC reference number, then quote it in the HKU application and select fellowship consideration. Review current portal questions and disclose AI assistance, including information retrieval, to the extent required by HKU/RGC. [s2] [s5] [s7] [s13] [s14]",
    "international": "[Standing rule] Testing applies to applicants from institutions outside Hong Kong whose instruction and examination are not entirely in English. Science follows the general threshold: TOEFL iBT 85 for tests before 21 January 2026, or 4.5 for tests on/after that date; IELTS Academic 6.5 overall with no component below 6.0. Single sitting, within two years. TOEFL Home Edition and IELTS One Skill Retake are not accepted. Other listed alternatives include specified GCE/IGCSE or Cambridge proficiency credentials. Official TOEFL delivery: institution 9671, department 99. [s3] [s6] [Standing rule] A completed UChicago degree taught and examined entirely in English appears to satisfy the English-medium exception, independent of citizenship (inference from the published rule). Confirm the evidence HKU wants if the degree is unfinished at application or if any study was elsewhere; a US F-1 visa itself is irrelevant. No UChicago-specific waiver form or automatic portal outcome is publicly established. [s3] [s6] [Standing rule] PGS and HKPFS/HKU-PS support nonlocal students; HKPFS expressly allows applicants from any country/ethnic background who seek a new full-time PhD. Standard PGS eligibility includes at least upper-second-class bachelor’s equivalent and full-time enrollment. Local-student tuition waivers and listed local hardship bursaries do not automatically extend to an international applicant. Citizenship affects Belt and Road scholarship eligibility; US F-1 status establishes none of these categories. [s10] [s13] [s17]",
    "costs": "[Standing rule] HKD780 per university application, nonrefundable and nontransferable; pay online with Visa or Mastercard. RGC’s initial HKPFS application is free, but it does not replace the university fee. Only one application per department is permitted regardless of degree/mode; separate departments require separate application/document sets and fees. [s8] [s9] [s14]",
    "size": "University enrollment and mathematics cohort size are not verified in this dossier.",
    "greGeneral": "[Standing rule] Not required for Science according to its FAQ. The central GRE/GMAT requirement applies to specified Business/Economics or Psychology applicants, not Mathematics. Whether optional math GRE results are accepted or given weight is not publicly specified; do not interpret “not required” as “not considered.” [s2] [s6]",
    "greMath": "[Standing rule] Not required under Science’s GRE policy. No separate requirement, recommendation, ban, or optional-score weighting for the Mathematics Subject Test was found in the mathematics/Science instructions. [s1] [s2] [s6]",
    "letters": "[Standing rule] Two academic referees who know the applicant’s achievements and research potential. Obtain consent before nomination. Professional/nonacademic referees are not considered appropriate. [s6]",
    "writing": "[Standing rule] No separate conventional statement of purpose is specified for Mathematics. Science requires a research proposal; do not replace it with a generic SOP. General guidance for a research-interest statement includes reasons for graduate work at HKU, but Science’s faculty-specific proposal rule governs. Separate SOP prompt, limit and upload field remain unverified. [s6] [s7]",
    "warnings": "[Conflict] Four operational discrepancies: (1) old department 2023-24 dates versus current central 2027-28 calendar; use s4. (2) Science FAQ describes uploading after payment, while the current operational guide allows preparation/upload before submission and additions afterward; follow s9. (3) central supervisor contact is presented as optional, while Science requires prior discussion and its proposal guidance expects a supportive named supervisor; follow the faculty-specific expectation. (4) general supporting-document deadline versus the explicit 14-day referee window needs HKPFS clarification. The Presidential year1 aggregate is also arithmetically inconsistent with listed benefits. [s1] [s2] [s4] [s5] [s6] [s7] [s9] [s12]",
    "checks": "[Unresolved] Confirm direct-PhD first-class equivalence for the actual UChicago record; proposed supervisor’s 2027 capacity; English-medium evidence while degree is pending; HKPFS exact essay prompts/limits, referee questions and internal letter cutoff; letter revision/reuse; any dedicated CV/course-list or optional-paper fields; 2027 PGS rate and net budget after fees/housing; Presidential aggregate correction; offer-specific acceptance/deposit deadlines. Public admission, Science FAQ, proposal document, portal guide, funding regulations and current faculty/paper sources were checked; these remaining points were not silently inferred. [s2] [s3] [s6] [s7] [s9] [s10] [s12] [s16]",
